{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'git show cb32394'","aggregated_output":"commit cb32394c6d27959254363c1440867230228a8e2e\nAuthor: Stuart Bowness <1020179+stuartbowness@users.noreply.github.com>\nDate:   Sun May 3 17:06:16 2026 -0700\n\n    [task-8] Smoke test — all structural checks pass\n\ndiff --git a/UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md b/UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md\nindex 8f60c2a..92ddbe5 100644\n--- a/UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md\n+++ b/UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md\n@@ -99,6 +99,30 @@\n | **Design Template** | A reference document defining mandatory design.md sections and scoring rubrics, used by the orchestrator alongside openspec config rules | Design spec, design schema |\n | **Spec Reference** | A capability/scenario identifier (e.g., add-todo/1) used to trace contract checks back to formal spec requirements | REQ-ID, requirement ID, spec ID |\n \n+## Frontend architecture\n+\n+| Term | Definition | Aliases to avoid |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| **Deep component** | A React component with a small prop interface that hides significant state, effects, and rendering logic, owning one user-facing workflow end-to-end | Smart component, container component, feature component |\n+| **Allowed-shallow exception** | A component that is intentionally thin and exempt from depth rules: design system leaves, route/layout glue, adapter components, or headless behavior primitives | Dumb component, presentational component, wrapper |\n+| **Component contract** | A lightweight per-component declaration written before implementation, specifying name, deep/shallow classification, prop interface, and key render states | Component spec, component design, component plan |\n+| **Design-implement-test** | The `/frontend` skill's implementation workflow: design component interfaces, build with visual verification, then write behavioral tests. Replaces red-green-refactor for React components. | Frontend TDD, component TDD |\n+| **Visual verification** | Using chrome-devtools-mcp during the Build phase to confirm a component renders correctly before writing tests | Visual testing, screenshot testing, visual QA |\n+| **Frontend depth gate** | A self-skipping scrutiny validator gate (gate 7) that evaluates React component structure against the four deep-component rules when `.tsx`/`.jsx` files are in the diff | Component review, React lint, frontend lint |\n+| **Methodology** | The implementation workflow skill assigned to a task -- either `/tdd` (red-green-refactor) or `/frontend` (design-implement-test). Mutually exclusive per task. | Implementation skill, build skill, workflow |\n+| **Constraint** | An additive design-guidance skill layered on top of a methodology -- `/ui-system`, `/react-perf`, or future `/backend-ts`. Zero or more per task. | Supplementary skill, pattern skill |\n+| **Task layer** | A specific vocabulary value in task topology metadata that determines which methodology applies. `frontend/component`, `frontend/page`, `frontend/layout` map to `/frontend`; `frontend/hooks`, `backend`, `shared/*` map to `/tdd`. | Task type, task category |\n+| **Browser tools** | A mission config flag (`browser_tools: true/false`) indicating whether chrome-devtools-mcp is required. Auto-set by the orchestrator when any task has `Skill: /frontend`. | Browser testing, visual tools |\n+\n+## Frontend: deep component rules\n+\n+| Term | Definition | Aliases to avoid |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| **Small semantic interface** | A component prop interface where each prop represents a domain concept, not an implementation knob. Count concepts, not props. Audit hidden inputs (context, URL, cache). | Narrow props, minimal API |\n+| **Derive don't sync** | Computing values during render (useMemo, inline computation) instead of syncing state with useEffect. Effects that transform data without I/O are a depth violation. | Computed state, reactive state |\n+| **Composition over configuration** | Using compound component slots and children instead of config objects with many options. Callers compose behavior without understanding internals. | Compound components, slots pattern |\n+| **Collapse coordination** | A deep component owns one workflow end-to-end, exposing semantic events (onSubmit) not coordination knobs (onValidate, onStep1Complete). Parents choose what happens, not how. | Single responsibility, workflow ownership |\n+\n ## Relationships\n \n - A **Mission** belongs to exactly one **Change**\n@@ -123,6 +147,14 @@\n - **Spec References** in the **Contract** trace **Checks** back to specific **Spec** capability/scenario pairs (e.g., add-todo/1), replacing arbitrary row numbers\n - **Task Topology** metadata is written per task in tasks.md and reviewed during Phase 4.4 -- tasks touching more than 2 architectural layers are flagged for human review\n - The **Design Template** is a reference document in `templates/` -- the actual design.md generation is driven by openspec config rules that require the same sections\n+- A **Task** has exactly one **Methodology** (`/tdd` or `/frontend`) and zero or more **Constraints** (`/ui-system`, `/react-perf`)\n+- The **Task layer** determines the **Methodology**: `frontend/component`, `frontend/page`, `frontend/layout` map to `/frontend`; all other layers map to `/tdd`\n+- `frontend/hooks` maps to `/tdd` despite being frontend code -- hooks have testable interfaces suited to red-green-refactor\n+- The **Frontend depth gate** (gate 7) is a **Self-skipping gate** that only fires when `.tsx`/`.jsx` files are in the diff\n+- **Visual verification** requires **Browser tools** (`browser_tools: true` in **Mission config**), checked at mission-init and at dispatch time\n+- A **Deep component** satisfies all four rules: **Small semantic interface**, **Derive don't sync**, **Composition over configuration**, **Collapse coordination**\n+- An **Allowed-shallow exception** is exempt from depth rules but must be classified: design system leaf, route/layout glue, adapter, or headless behavior primitive\n+- The **Component contract** is written per component during the `/frontend` workflow's Contract phase, before the Build phase begins\n \n ## Example dialogue\n \n@@ -170,6 +202,24 @@\n >\n > **Orchestrator:** \"The **Test quality review** catches that. It's an LLM subagent that reads the test diff alongside the production diff and flags **Tautological assertions** -- tests that pass regardless of correctness. A P0 finding like `assert!(true)` is a hard FAIL.\"\n \n+## Example dialogue (frontend architecture)\n+\n+> **Dev:** \"I need to build a payment form. Should that be one task or two?\"\n+>\n+> **Orchestrator:** \"Two. The validation logic (card format, expiry, required fields) is a hook with a testable interface -- that's a `/tdd` task with **Task layer** `frontend/hooks`. The form component itself is visual and owns the submission workflow -- that's a `/frontend` task with **Task layer** `frontend/component`.\"\n+>\n+> **Dev:** \"How does the `/frontend` worker know what to build?\"\n+>\n+> **Orchestrator:** \"The workflow starts with a Scan (read existing components), then a **Component contract** -- name the component, declare it **Deep** or **Allowed-shallow**, define the prop interface, list render states. Then Build with **Visual verification** via chrome-devtools-mcp, then behavioral tests.\"\n+>\n+> **Dev:** \"What if the worker builds a component with 15 props?\"\n+>\n+> **Orchestrator:** \"The deep-component audit checklist catches it before commit -- **Small semantic interface** says count concepts, not props. If the worker misses it, the **Frontend depth gate** (gate 7) flags it during scrutiny validation.\"\n+>\n+> **Dev:** \"And if the project is Rust, none of this applies?\"\n+>\n+> **Orchestrator:** \"Correct. Every task gets `/tdd`, no **Constraints**, no **Browser tools**. The **Frontend depth gate** self-skips because there are no `.tsx` files in the diff.\"\n+\n ## Flagged ambiguities\n \n - **\"template\"** is used for two different things in the mission skill: the **Design Template** (a reference document defining mandatory design.md sections and scoring rubrics) and the **CLAUDE.md template** (a fill-in-the-blanks document for the closing task). Both live in `templates/` but serve different purposes. **Resolved:** use the full name (\"design template\" or \"CLAUDE.md template\") when context is ambiguous. The file names distinguish them: `design-template.md` vs `claude-md.md`.\n@@ -181,3 +231,5 @@\n - **\"validation\"** was used for both the contract checks and the act of running validators. **Resolved:** the **Contract** contains **Checks**. **Validation** is the act of a **Validator** verifying those checks against the code. Be consistent: don't use \"validation\" to refer to the contract itself.\n - **\"coverage\"** could mean line coverage (percentage of lines executed during tests) or spec coverage (percentage of PRD requirements mapped to tasks). **Resolved:** **Diff coverage** means line coverage on added lines in a git diff. **Coverage audit** means the spec-to-task mapping in Phase 4a. Don't use \"coverage\" without the qualifier.\n - **\"check\" / \"assertion\" / \"gate\"** had overlapping usage across contract items, validator steps, and code test assertions. **Resolved** with a three-way split: a **Gate** is a numbered step in the scrutiny validator's sequence (e.g., gate 3: tests, gate 10: contract checks). A **Check** is a single verifiable statement in a contract. An **Assertion** is reserved for code test assertions only (e.g., **Tautological assertion**, `assert_eq!`, `expect().toBe()`). Don't use \"assertion\" for contract items or \"check\" for validator steps.\n+- **\"skill\"** could mean both a methodology (implementation workflow) and a constraint (design guidance). **Resolved** with a two-axis model: a **Methodology** is the implementation workflow (`/tdd` or `/frontend`, mutually exclusive per task). A **Constraint** is additive design guidance (`/ui-system`, `/react-perf`, zero or more per task). Both are skills, but the axes are orthogonal. Don't say \"skill\" when you mean methodology or constraint specifically.\n+- **\"frontend\"** as a task layer could mean component work (visual, needs `/frontend`) or hook work (logic, needs `/tdd`). **Resolved** with specific layer vocabulary: `frontend/component`, `frontend/page`, `frontend/layout` map to `/frontend`; `frontend/hooks` maps to `/tdd`. Don't use bare \"frontend\" as a task layer.\ndiff --git a/openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/.openspec.yaml b/openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/.openspec.yaml\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..e5764a1\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/.openspec.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,2 @@\n+schema: spec-driven\n+created: 2026-05-03\ndiff --git a/openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/contract.md b/openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/contract.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..4fa8fa2\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/contract.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,143 @@\n+# Contract\n+\n+## Task 1: Foundation vocabulary files (DEEP-COMPONENTS.md, STACK.md)\n+<!-- Specs: frontend/1, frontend/8, frontend/9, frontend/10, frontend/11, frontend/12, frontend/13 -->\n+- [ ] [output] `skills/frontend/DEEP-COMPONENTS.md` exists and contains the heading or phrase \"Small semantic interface\" (rule 1)\n+- [ ] [output] `skills/frontend/DEEP-COMPONENTS.md` contains the heading or phrase \"Derive don't sync\" (rule 2)\n+- [ ] [output] `skills/frontend/DEEP-COMPONENTS.md` contains the heading or phrase \"Composition over configuration\" (rule 3)\n+- [ ] [output] `skills/frontend/DEEP-COMPONENTS.md` contains the heading or phrase \"Collapse coordination\" (rule 4)\n+- [ ] [output] `skills/frontend/DEEP-COMPONENTS.md` contains \"design system\" in the allowed-shallow exceptions section\n+- [ ] [output] `skills/frontend/DEEP-COMPONENTS.md` contains \"route\" or \"layout\" in the allowed-shallow exceptions section\n+- [ ] [output] `skills/frontend/DEEP-COMPONENTS.md` contains \"adapter\" in the allowed-shallow exceptions section\n+- [ ] [output] `skills/frontend/DEEP-COMPONENTS.md` contains \"headless\" in the allowed-shallow exceptions section\n+- [ ] [output] `skills/frontend/DEEP-COMPONENTS.md` contains \"deletion test\"\n+- [ ] [output] `skills/frontend/STACK.md` exists and contains \"React 19\"\n+- [ ] [output] `skills/frontend/STACK.md` contains \"Vite\"\n+- [ ] [output] `skills/frontend/STACK.md` contains \"TailwindCSS\" or \"Tailwind\"\n+- [ ] [output] `skills/frontend/STACK.md` contains \"Radix\" or \"ShadCN\"\n+- [ ] [output] `skills/frontend/STACK.md` contains \"Vitest\"\n+- [ ] [output] `skills/frontend/STACK.md` contains \"barrel\" (in context of prohibiting barrel file imports)\n+- [ ] [output] `skills/frontend/STACK.md` contains \"cn()\" (utility reference)\n+- [ ] [output] `skills/frontend/STACK.md` contains \"components/ui/\" (file organization)\n+- [ ] [output] `skills/frontend/STACK.md` contains \"React Router\"\n+- [ ] [output] `skills/frontend/STACK.md` contains \"semantic\" in context of color tokens\n+- [ ] [output] `skills/frontend/STACK.md` contains \"data-slot\"\n+\n+## Task 2: Scrutiny validator gate 7 + gate renumbering + gate 1 update\n+<!-- Specs: frontend-validation/1, frontend-validation/2, frontend-validation/3, frontend-validation/4, frontend-validation/5, frontend-validation/6, frontend-validation/7, frontend-validation/8 -->\n+- [ ] [output] `skills/mission/prompts/scrutiny-validator.md` contains a gate named \"Frontend depth review\" or \"frontend depth\"\n+- [ ] [execution] The scrutiny-validator.md contains exactly 15 gate headings in its gate sequence, numbered sequentially from 1 to 15\n+- [ ] [output] The gate sequence in scrutiny-validator.md has \"Frontend depth\" after \"Module depth\" and before \"Code standards\"\n+- [ ] [output] scrutiny-validator.md contains \"no React component files in diff\" (self-skip text)\n+- [ ] [output] scrutiny-validator.md gate 7 section contains \".tsx\" or \".jsx\" (file extension trigger)\n+- [ ] [output] scrutiny-validator.md gate 7 section references \"semantic concepts\" or \"prop\" (rule 1 check)\n+- [ ] [output] scrutiny-validator.md gate 7 section references \"useEffect\" and \"setState\" (rule 2 check)\n+- [ ] [output] scrutiny-validator.md gate 7 section references \"config\" or \"configuration\" (rule 3 check)\n+- [ ] [output] scrutiny-validator.md gate 7 section references \"coordination\" or \"semantic events\" (rule 4 check)\n+- [ ] [output] scrutiny-validator.md gate 7 section references \"*/ui/*\" or \"ui/\" (allowed-shallow directory pattern)\n+- [ ] [output] scrutiny-validator.md gate 7 section references \"@radix-ui\" (Radix wrapper exception)\n+- [ ] [output] scrutiny-validator.md gate 1 section contains \"/frontend Test phase not followed\" (updated rationale)\n+- [ ] [output] scrutiny-validator.md gate 1 section contains \"Skill:\" or \"/frontend\" (methodology-aware test presence)\n+\n+## Task 3: Core /frontend SKILL.md\n+<!-- Specs: frontend/2, frontend/3, frontend/4, frontend/5, frontend/6, frontend/7 -->\n+- [ ] [output] `skills/frontend/SKILL.md` exists and starts with YAML frontmatter containing `name: frontend`\n+- [ ] [output] SKILL.md frontmatter contains `user-invokable: true`\n+- [ ] [output] SKILL.md frontmatter description contains \"frontend\" or \"React\" or \"component\"\n+- [ ] [output] SKILL.md contains \"Scan\" as a workflow phase heading or label\n+- [ ] [output] SKILL.md contains \"Contract\" as a workflow phase heading or label\n+- [ ] [output] SKILL.md contains \"Build\" as a workflow phase heading or label\n+- [ ] [output] SKILL.md contains \"Test\" as a workflow phase heading or label\n+- [ ] [output] SKILL.md contains \"scan note\" (Scan phase output)\n+- [ ] [output] SKILL.md contains \"deep\" and \"shallow\" in the Contract phase section (classification)\n+- [ ] [output] SKILL.md contains \"chrome-devtools\" or \"visual\" in the Build phase section\n+- [ ] [output] SKILL.md contains \"browser_tools\" (conditional visual verification)\n+- [ ] [output] SKILL.md contains \"per-component\" or \"one component at a time\" (forcing function)\n+- [ ] [output] SKILL.md contains a checklist section with \"audit\" or \"before commit\"\n+- [ ] [output] SKILL.md contains markdown links to `DEEP-COMPONENTS.md`, `STACK.md`, `PATTERNS.md`, `TESTING.md`\n+- [ ] [execution] Run `test -f skills/frontend/DEEP-COMPONENTS.md && test -f skills/frontend/STACK.md` — both files exist (SKILL.md link targets)\n+\n+## Task 4: PATTERNS.md and TESTING.md\n+<!-- Specs: frontend/14, frontend/15, frontend/16, frontend/17, frontend/18, frontend/19, frontend/20 -->\n+- [ ] [output] `skills/frontend/PATTERNS.md` exists and contains at least 2 code blocks showing deep component examples\n+- [ ] [output] PATTERNS.md contains at least 2 code blocks showing allowed-shallow examples (design system leaves or compound components)\n+- [ ] [output] PATTERNS.md contains at least 1 code block showing a hook with derive-don't-sync pattern\n+- [ ] [output] PATTERNS.md contains at least 1 anti-pattern with a before/after or \"don't do this\"/\"do this\" structure\n+- [ ] [output] `skills/frontend/TESTING.md` exists and contains \"role\" or \"label\" (query-by-role testing)\n+- [ ] [output] TESTING.md contains \"userEvent\" or \"user event\" or \"fire events\" (user interaction testing)\n+- [ ] [output] TESTING.md contains \"prop plumbing\" or \"internal state\" or \"implementation\" (what not to test)\n+- [ ] [output] TESTING.md contains \"snapshot\" (prohibiting snapshot tests for layout)\n+- [ ] [output] TESTING.md contains \"/tdd\" (hook logic boundary — tested in separate /tdd tasks)\n+\n+## Task 5: /ui-system skill\n+<!-- Specs: ui-system/1, ui-system/2, ui-system/3, ui-system/4, ui-system/5 -->\n+- [ ] [output] `skills/ui-system/SKILL.md` exists and starts with YAML frontmatter containing `name: ui-system`\n+- [ ] [output] SKILL.md frontmatter contains `user-invokable: true`\n+- [ ] [output] SKILL.md frontmatter description contains \"ShadCN\" or \"Radix\" or \"design system\"\n+- [ ] [output] SKILL.md contains \"search existing\" or \"existing components\" (component selection)\n+- [ ] [output] SKILL.md contains \"semantic\" and \"token\" (semantic token discipline)\n+- [ ] [output] SKILL.md contains \"raw\" or \"bg-blue\" (prohibiting raw color values)\n+- [ ] [output] SKILL.md contains \"cn()\" (conditional classes utility)\n+- [ ] [output] SKILL.md contains \"gap\" (gap-* over space-x/y-*)\n+- [ ] [output] SKILL.md contains \"Title\" and \"Dialog\" or \"Sheet\" or \"Drawer\" (accessibility defaults)\n+- [ ] [output] SKILL.md contains \"AvatarFallback\" or \"fallback\" (Avatar accessibility)\n+- [ ] [output] SKILL.md contains \"form\" or \"Form\" or \"FieldGroup\" (form patterns)\n+- [ ] [output] SKILL.md contains \"icon\" (icon handling guidance)\n+- [ ] [output] SKILL.md contains \"CLI\" or \"npx\" or \"shadcn\" (CLI usage guidance)\n+\n+## Task 6: /react-perf skill\n+<!-- Specs: react-perf/1, react-perf/2, react-perf/3, react-perf/4, react-perf/5 -->\n+- [ ] [output] `skills/react-perf/SKILL.md` exists and starts with YAML frontmatter containing `name: react-perf`\n+- [ ] [output] SKILL.md frontmatter contains `user-invokable: true`\n+- [ ] [output] SKILL.md frontmatter description contains \"performance\" or \"perf\"\n+- [ ] [output] SKILL.md contains \"Promise.all\" or \"waterfall\" (waterfall elimination)\n+- [ ] [output] SKILL.md contains \"barrel\" or \"dynamic import\" (bundle size)\n+- [ ] [output] SKILL.md contains \"startTransition\" or \"useTransition\" (re-render discipline)\n+- [ ] [output] SKILL.md contains \"Suspense\" (React 19 patterns)\n+- [ ] [output] SKILL.md contains \"derive\" or \"derived\" or \"render\" in context of state (derive during render)\n+- [ ] [output] SKILL.md contains \"server\" or \"Server\" (server-side patterns)\n+- [ ] [output] SKILL.md contains \"content-visibility\" or \"visibility\" (rendering patterns)\n+- [ ] [output] SKILL.md contains \"Map\" or \"Set\" or \"flatMap\" (JS performance patterns)\n+\n+## Task 7: Template modifications, config, and mission-init\n+<!-- Specs: skill-assignment/1, skill-assignment/2, skill-assignment/3, skill-assignment/4, skill-assignment/5, skill-assignment/6, skill-assignment/7, skill-assignment/8, skill-assignment/9, skill-assignment/10 -->\n+- [ ] [output] `skills/mission/templates/worker-brief.md` contains \"/frontend\" (conditional methodology reference)\n+- [ ] [output] worker-brief.md contains \"Skill:\" (reads task topology field)\n+- [ ] [output] worker-brief.md contains \"Constraints:\" or \"constraint\" (appends constraint references)\n+- [ ] [output] `skills/mission/templates/design-template.md` contains \"prop interface\" or \"semantic concepts\" (frontend module guidance)\n+- [ ] [output] design-template.md contains \"deep\" and \"shallow\" (component classification guidance)\n+- [ ] [output] `skills/mission/SKILL.md` contains \"browser_tools\" (config flag)\n+- [ ] [output] skills/mission/SKILL.md contains \"frontend/component\" (layer vocabulary)\n+- [ ] [output] skills/mission/SKILL.md contains \"frontend/hooks\" and \"/tdd\" in proximity (hooks → /tdd mapping)\n+- [ ] [output] skills/mission/SKILL.md contains \"/ui-system\" and \"/react-perf\" and \"Skill: /frontend\" in proximity (constraint validation)\n+- [ ] [output] skills/mission/SKILL.md contains \"chrome-devtools\" and \"dispatch\" or \"pre-flight\" (dispatch pre-flight check)\n+- [ ] [output] skills/mission/SKILL.md contains \"browser_tools: false\" and \"override\" or \"skip\" (human override handling)\n+- [ ] [output] `skills/mission-init/SKILL.md` contains \"chrome-devtools\" or \"browser_tools\" (init availability check)\n+- [ ] [output] skills/mission-init/SKILL.md contains \"install\" or \"missing\" (fail-fast with instructions)\n+\n+## Task 8: Smoke test\n+<!-- Specs: frontend/1, ui-system/1, react-perf/1, frontend-validation/2, skill-assignment/1 -->\n+- [ ] [execution] Run `./install.sh` — output contains \"frontend\" in the linked skills\n+- [ ] [execution] Run `./install.sh` — output contains \"ui-system\" in the linked skills\n+- [ ] [execution] Run `./install.sh` — output contains \"react-perf\" in the linked skills\n+- [ ] [execution] Run `ls -la ~/.claude/skills/frontend` — symlink exists and points to ~/.darkfactory/skills/frontend\n+- [ ] [execution] Run `ls -la ~/.claude/skills/ui-system` — symlink exists and points to ~/.darkfactory/skills/ui-system\n+- [ ] [execution] Run `ls -la ~/.claude/skills/react-perf` — symlink exists and points to ~/.darkfactory/skills/react-perf\n+- [ ] [execution] All markdown links in skills/frontend/*.md resolve to existing files\n+- [ ] [execution] Scrutiny validator gates are numbered 1-15 with no gaps or duplicates\n+- [ ] [execution] Run `grep -r \"/shadcn\" skills/ UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md README.md` — returns zero matches\n+- [ ] [execution] worker-brief.md does not contain hardcoded \"Use `/tdd` to implement this task\" as the only methodology option\n+- [ ] [execution] scrutiny-validator.md gate 1 contains \"/frontend Test phase not followed\"\n+- [ ] [execution] skills/mission/SKILL.md contains layer vocabulary mapping rules and constraint validation rules\n+\n+## Task 9: Cleanup + module shape re-check\n+<!-- Specs: (closing task — structural integrity) -->\n+- [ ] [execution] No unused or orphaned files in skills/frontend/, skills/ui-system/, skills/react-perf/\n+- [ ] [output] `mission/validations/module-shape-audit.md` exists with findings for each design.md module\n+\n+## Task 10: Documentation\n+<!-- Specs: frontend-validation/8 -->\n+- [ ] [output] README.md contains \"frontend\" skill with description\n+- [ ] [output] README.md contains \"ui-system\" skill with description\n+- [ ] [output] README.md contains \"react-perf\" skill with description\n+- [ ] [execution] UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md gate number references match the 1-15 sequence (no stale references to old numbering)\ndiff --git a/openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/coverage-audit.md b/openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/coverage-audit.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..261aa06\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/coverage-audit.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@\n+# Spec Coverage Audit\n+\n+## Coverage Table\n+| # | PRD Requirement (User Story) | Spec Requirement | Task(s) | Status |\n+|---|------------------------------|-----------------|---------|--------|\n+| 1 | US1: Assign /frontend or /tdd per task based on layer | skill-assignment: Layer vocabulary determines Skill assignment (7 scenarios) | Task 7 | COVERED |\n+| 2 | US2: Prescriptive workflow (Scan → Contract → Build → Test) | frontend: SKILL.md defines the design-implement-test workflow (7 scenarios) | Task 3 | COVERED |\n+| 3 | US3: Visual verify via chrome-devtools-mcp during Build | frontend: Build phase with visual verification; skill-assignment: browser_tools config flag | Tasks 3, 7 | COVERED |\n+| 4 | US4: Per-component contract template | frontend: Contract phase scenario | Task 3 | COVERED |\n+| 5 | US5: Deep-component audit checklist before commit | frontend: Deep-component audit before commit scenario | Task 3 | COVERED |\n+| 6 | US6: Self-skipping gate 7 (frontend depth) | frontend-validation: Gate 7 exists, self-skips, checks four rules, recognizes exceptions, produces verdict (13 scenarios) | Task 2 | COVERED |\n+| 7 | US7: /ui-system guidance on component selection and tokens | ui-system: skill exists, includes verbatim ShadCN content (4 scenarios); valid/invalid constraint pairing (2 scenarios) | Tasks 5, 7 | COVERED |\n+| 8 | US8: /react-perf guidance on waterfalls, bundle, re-renders | react-perf: skill exists, includes verbatim Vercel content (4 scenarios); valid/invalid constraint pairing (2 scenarios) | Tasks 6, 7 | COVERED |\n+| 9 | US9: browser_tools config flag auto-sets | skill-assignment: browser_tools config flag (5 scenarios) | Task 7 | COVERED |\n+| 10 | US10: Specific layer vocabulary for skill assignment | skill-assignment: Layer vocabulary determines Skill assignment (7 scenarios) | Task 7 | COVERED |\n+| 11 | US11: Task topology Skill: and Constraints: fields | skill-assignment: Task topology includes fields, exactly one Methodology, constraints validated (10 scenarios) | Task 7 | COVERED |\n+| 12 | US12: Developer can invoke /frontend directly | frontend: skill exists with user-invokable: true; ui-system: independent invocation; react-perf: independent invocation | Tasks 3, 5, 6 | COVERED |\n+| 13 | US13: Split complex frontend features (hook + component) | skill-assignment: Task decomposition splits complex features (2 scenarios) | Task 7 | COVERED |\n+| 14 | US14: Soft pre-flight check for chrome-devtools-mcp at dispatch | skill-assignment: Soft pre-flight at dispatch scenario | Task 7 | COVERED |\n+| 15 | US15: TESTING.md for behavioral component testing | frontend: TESTING.md defines frontend behavioral testing (3 scenarios) | Task 4 | COVERED |\n+| 16 | US16: Non-TypeScript missions unchanged | skill-assignment: Non-TypeScript projects scenario; frontend-validation: No React files self-skip | Tasks 2, 7 | COVERED |\n+| 17 | ID: Gate renumbering (7→8 through 14→15) | frontend-validation: Gate numbering sequence scenario | Task 2 | COVERED |\n+| 18 | ID: Gate 1 rationale update for /frontend tasks | frontend-validation: Gate 1 rationale updated (2 scenarios) | Task 2 | COVERED |\n+| 19 | ID: DEEP-COMPONENTS.md four rules + exceptions | frontend: DEEP-COMPONENTS.md defines four rules and exceptions (3 scenarios) | Task 1 | COVERED |\n+| 20 | ID: STACK.md technology reference | frontend: STACK.md defines technology reference (3 scenarios) | Task 1 | COVERED |\n+| 21 | ID: PATTERNS.md concrete code examples | frontend: PATTERNS.md provides concrete code examples (4 scenarios) | Task 4 | COVERED |\n+| 22 | ID: Worker brief template becomes conditional | skill-assignment: Worker brief references correct methodology (3 scenarios) | Task 7 | COVERED |\n+| 23 | ID: Design template frontend module guidance | skill-assignment: Design template includes frontend module guidance (1 scenario) | Task 7 | COVERED |\n+| 24 | ID: Supplementary skills verbatim upstream content | ui-system: verbatim ShadCN; react-perf: verbatim Vercel | Tasks 5, 6 | COVERED |\n+| 25 | ID: install.sh unchanged (auto-discovers all 3 skills) | frontend: Skill registration; ui-system: Skill registration; react-perf: Skill registration | Tasks 5, 6, 8 (smoke test) | COVERED |\n+| 26 | ID: UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md gate refs updated | frontend-validation: Gate references updated scenario | Task 10 | COVERED |\n+\n+## Gaps\n+(none)\n+\n+## Deviations Requiring Approval\n+(none)\ndiff --git a/openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/design.md b/openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/design.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..a555b4c\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/design.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,110 @@\n+## Context\n+\n+Darkfactory is a skill-based mission orchestration system. Skills are markdown directories (`skills/<name>/SKILL.md` plus optional reference files) discovered by `install.sh` and invoked via `/name` in Claude Code sessions. The scrutiny validator runs 14 sequential gates against worker output. Worker briefs are assembled from a template that currently hardcodes `/tdd` as the implementation methodology.\n+\n+This mission adds 3 new skills and modifies the validator, brief template, and design template to support frontend-specific workflows.\n+\n+## Goals / Non-Goals\n+\n+**Goals:**\n+- Add `/frontend`, `/ui-system`, `/react-perf` skills following existing skill conventions\n+- Extend the scrutiny validator with a self-skipping frontend gate\n+- Enable the orchestrator to assign different methodologies per task\n+- Support visual verification via chrome-devtools-mcp during frontend builds\n+- Zero impact on non-TypeScript missions\n+\n+**Non-Goals:**\n+- Visual design (aesthetic direction, layout design)\n+- Browser-based QA suites (belongs in testkitchen)\n+- Backend TypeScript patterns (deferred to #144)\n+- Framework-agnostic support (React only)\n+\n+## Architecture Decision\n+\n+This is an existing codebase mission. No architecture change — the new skills follow the established skill pattern (markdown directories, YAML frontmatter, bundled reference files, auto-discovery by install.sh). The validator modification follows the established gate pattern (sequential, self-skipping).\n+\n+The one architectural addition is the two-axis skill assignment model (`Skill:` + `Constraints:` in task topology), which extends the existing `Layers:` field rather than replacing it.\n+\n+**Current architecture:** Skills are flat directories in `skills/`. The validator is a single prompt file with numbered gates. The worker brief template has a hardcoded Procedures section. All three patterns are extended, not replaced.\n+\n+**How changes fit:**\n+- New skill directories are auto-discovered — no install.sh changes\n+- New gate is inserted by renumbering — the sequential gate pattern is preserved\n+- Brief template conditioning uses the existing topology metadata — new fields, same mechanism\n+- Config flag (`browser_tools`) follows the existing `engines:` pattern in config.yaml\n+\n+## Module Inventory\n+\n+| Module name | Interface width | What it hides | Why this boundary |\n+|---|---|---|---|\n+| `skills/frontend/` | Narrow: 1 entry point (SKILL.md), 4 reference files | Deep-component rules, workflow phases, stack conventions, code patterns, testing guidance. Workers see the workflow; the principles and examples are progressive disclosure. | The core skill is the single unit a worker interacts with. Reference files are internal to the skill — workers read them via SKILL.md links, not directly. |\n+| `skills/ui-system/` | Narrow: 1 entry point (SKILL.md) | Verbatim upstream ShadCN/Radix guidelines. Workers get component selection and token discipline without knowing the upstream source. | Standalone constraint skill. Independent of `/frontend` — callable on its own for design system questions. |\n+| `skills/react-perf/` | Narrow: 1 entry point (SKILL.md) | Verbatim upstream Vercel React best practices. Workers get performance patterns without knowing the upstream source. | Standalone constraint skill. Independent of `/frontend` — callable on its own for performance questions. |\n+| Gate 7 (frontend depth) | Narrow: 1 gate in the validator sequence | LLM evaluation of React component depth against four rules. The gate reads the diff, applies DEEP-COMPONENTS.md criteria, and produces PASS/FAIL/WARN. | Self-skipping gate follows the established pattern (like gate 9/security). Isolates frontend concerns from the language-agnostic module depth gate (gate 6). |\n+| Task topology extensions | Narrow: 2 new fields (`Skill:`, `Constraints:`) | Layer-to-methodology mapping rules, constraint validation logic. The orchestrator applies the mapping; workers see only the assembled brief. | Extends existing topology metadata. The mapping rules live in the orchestrator's task generation logic (Phase 4.3a/4.4), not in a separate module. |\n+| Worker brief conditioning | Narrow: 1 conditional section (Procedures) | Methodology selection logic. The template reads `Skill:` and `Constraints:` and assembles the right references. Workers see a brief with one methodology and zero or more constraints. | Extends the existing template. The conditional is a single if/else on the `Skill:` field. |\n+| `browser_tools` config | Narrow: 1 boolean flag | Chrome-devtools-mcp lifecycle (availability checks, dispatch pre-flight, human override). The orchestrator manages the flag; workers either have visual verification in their brief or don't. | Follows the existing `engines:` pattern in config.yaml. One flag, two check points (init, dispatch). |\n+\n+### Frontend module depth\n+\n+For React component modules in the Module Inventory, describe:\n+- **Prop interface:** how many semantic concepts the caller must understand\n+- **State/effects encapsulated:** what the component hides behind its interface\n+- **Classification:** deep component (owns a workflow) or allowed-shallow exception (design system leaf, route glue, adapter, headless primitive) with reason\n+\n+## Type Catalog\n+\n+This mission produces markdown skills, not code with domain types. No domain types are introduced. The terminology is captured in UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md (deep component, allowed-shallow exception, methodology, constraint, task layer, etc.) rather than in code types.\n+\n+| Type name | Purpose | Owning module |\n+|---|---|---|\n+| (none) | This mission produces markdown files, not code with typed interfaces | -- |\n+\n+## Error Strategy\n+\n+This mission modifies markdown files and prompt templates. There are no runtime error types to define.\n+\n+**Failure modes and handling:**\n+- **Missing chrome-devtools-mcp at mission-init:** Hard fail with clear error message. Human installs and re-runs.\n+- **chrome-devtools-mcp unavailable at dispatch:** Block dispatch, log to progress.md, surface to human with options (retry, skip visual verify, abort).\n+- **Invalid `Skill:` or `Constraints:` values in topology:** Caught during Phase 4.4 human review. The orchestrator validates combinations before dispatch.\n+- **Gate 7 false positive on allowed-shallow components:** The gate recognizes `*/ui/*` directories and Radix imports as exceptions. Persistent false positives are addressed by updating the gate's exception list.\n+- **Gate 7 false negatives:** Gate 7 is an LLM gate and may miss violations. Mitigation: the deep-component audit checklist in SKILL.md is the first line of defense; gate 7 is the backstop. Neither is perfect, but both catching the same violation is redundant by design.\n+- **Upstream content drift:** `/ui-system` and `/react-perf` include verbatim upstream content that may drift from the skills.sh sources over time. Mitigation: diff against upstream periodically. No automated sync — the content is vendored and owned by Layercode.\n+- **Mid-build chrome-devtools-mcp failure:** If the MCP server crashes after dispatch, the worker's MCP call fails and the worker must handle the error. This is outside the orchestrator's control — the worker reports it in the handoff, and the validator catches incomplete visual verification.\n+- **Hardcoded symlink count in tests:** The test strategy checks for 20 symlinks (17 + 3). This couples to the current skill count. Mitigation: check for the 3 new symlinks specifically rather than a total count.\n+\n+## Integration Points\n+\n+| Caller | Callee | Method/interface | Direction |\n+|---|---|---|---|\n+| Orchestrator (Phase 4.3a) | `config.yaml` | Sets `browser_tools: true/false` based on task skills | Internal |\n+| Orchestrator (Phase 4.4) | `tasks.md` | Writes `Skill:` and `Constraints:` fields per task | Internal |\n+| Orchestrator (Step 1: Brief) | `worker-brief.md` template | Reads `Skill:` and `Constraints:` fields, conditionally sets Procedures section and appends constraint references | Internal |\n+| Worker brief | `/frontend` SKILL.md | References skill in Procedures: \"Use `/frontend`\" | Outbound |\n+| Worker brief | `/ui-system` SKILL.md | References skill as constraint: \"Also follow `/ui-system`\" | Outbound |\n+| Worker brief | `/react-perf` SKILL.md | References skill as constraint: \"Also follow `/react-perf`\" | Outbound |\n+| `/frontend` SKILL.md | `DEEP-COMPONENTS.md` | Markdown link: `[DEEP-COMPONENTS.md](DEEP-COMPONENTS.md)` | Internal |\n+| `/frontend` SKILL.md | `STACK.md` | Markdown link: `[STACK.md](STACK.md)` | Internal |\n+| `/frontend` SKILL.md | `PATTERNS.md` | Markdown link: `[PATTERNS.md](PATTERNS.md)` | Internal |\n+| `/frontend` SKILL.md | `TESTING.md` | Markdown link: `[TESTING.md](TESTING.md)` | Internal |\n+| Scrutiny validator | Gate 1 (test presence) | Gate 1 reads task's `Skill:` field to select rationale text | Internal |\n+| Scrutiny validator | Gate 7 (frontend depth) | Sequential gate execution after gate 6 | Internal |\n+| Gate 7 | `DEEP-COMPONENTS.md` criteria | References four rules for evaluation | Outbound |\n+| `/mission-init` | chrome-devtools-mcp | Reads `browser_tools` from config.yaml; if `true`, checks MCP server is registered via tool listing. Fails fast with install instructions if missing. | Outbound |\n+| Orchestrator (Step 2: Dispatch) | chrome-devtools-mcp | Soft pre-flight check before `/frontend` task dispatch | Outbound |\n+| `/frontend` worker | chrome-devtools-mcp | Visual verification during Build phase | Outbound |\n+\n+## Test Strategy\n+\n+- **Test framework:** None. This mission produces markdown files, not code. Validation is structural.\n+- **Where tests live:** No test files. Verification is done via bash commands and manual inspection.\n+- **Structural validation:**\n+  - All new skill directories contain SKILL.md with valid YAML frontmatter (`name`, `user-invokable: true`, `description`)\n+  - `./install.sh` produces 20 symlinks (17 existing + 3 new)\n+  - `/mission-init` passes with all 12 required skills OK\n+  - All markdown links in new files resolve to existing files\n+  - Scrutiny validator gates are numbered 1-15 sequentially with no gaps or duplicates\n+  - UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md gate number references match the new sequence\n+- **Backward compatibility:** Run an existing non-TypeScript mission's scrutiny validator output through the new gate sequence. Gate 7 should SKIP. All other gates should produce identical results.\n+- **Coverage approach:** Every spec scenario maps to a structural check (file exists, content contains, link resolves, gate number matches). No line coverage — there's no executable code.\ndiff --git a/openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/mission/briefs/task-1.md b/openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/mission/briefs/task-1.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..7f35b28\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/mission/briefs/task-1.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,91 @@\n+# Worker Brief: Task 1 - Foundation vocabulary files (DEEP-COMPONENTS.md, STACK.md)\n+\n+## Your Task\n+\n+Create the `skills/frontend/` directory and write two foundation reference files that define the deep-component rules and technology stack conventions.\n+\n+**File 1: `skills/frontend/DEEP-COMPONENTS.md`**\n+\n+Write a reference document defining the \"deep components\" thesis for React frontend architecture. Include:\n+\n+### Four Rules (each with a diagnostic question)\n+\n+1. **Small semantic interfaces** — A component's prop interface should represent domain concepts, not implementation knobs. Count concepts (props + context providers + URL params + cache dependencies), not raw prop count. A component with 6 props describing one concept is fine; a component with 1 prop bag containing 4 unrelated concerns is shallow.\n+   - Diagnostic: \"How many independent domain concepts must a caller understand to use this component?\"\n+\n+2. **Derive don't sync** — Compute values during render (useMemo, inline computation) instead of syncing state with useEffect. Effects that transform data without I/O are a depth violation. Canonical source: React team's \"You Might Not Need an Effect.\"\n+   - Diagnostic: \"Can this value be computed from existing state/props during render instead of stored separately?\"\n+\n+3. **Composition over configuration** — Use compound component slots and children instead of config objects with many options. Callers compose behavior without understanding internals. A component accepting `items: [{label, icon, onClick, disabled, variant}]` is shallower than one accepting `<Menu><MenuItem>...</MenuItem></Menu>`.\n+   - Diagnostic: \"Would this be clearer as compound components with children/slots instead of a config prop?\"\n+\n+4. **Collapse coordination** — A deep component owns one user-facing workflow end-to-end. It exposes semantic events (onSubmit, onCancel) not coordination knobs (onValidate, onStep1Complete, onReset). Parents choose what happens, not how the child reaches every intermediate state.\n+   - Diagnostic: \"Does the parent coordinate state that belongs inside this component?\"\n+\n+### Allowed-Shallow Exceptions (each with rationale)\n+\n+- **Design system leaves** (Button, Badge, Card sub-components) — Thin by design. CVA wrappers with data-slot attributes. Their job is visual consistency and accessibility hooks, not workflow ownership.\n+- **Route/layout glue** (App.tsx, page wrappers) — Read route params, hand data to a feature component. Acceptable if they stay thin and don't become workflow owners.\n+- **Adapter components** (auth-callback-page, OAuth redirect handlers) — Boundary concerns that adapt external flows. Not behavior ownership.\n+- **Headless behavior primitives** (Radix Dialog, Combobox, Popover wrappers) — Infrastructure that provides behavior without business rules. Should not know domain logic.\n+\n+### Deletion Test\n+\n+Include this diagnostic: \"If you deleted this component, would complexity vanish (it was a pass-through) or reappear across every consumer (it was earning its keep)?\"\n+\n+**File 2: `skills/frontend/STACK.md`**\n+\n+Write a reference document declaring the technology stack and conventions:\n+\n+- **Stack:** React 19, Vite, TailwindCSS 4, Radix UI / ShadCN, Vitest, React Router\n+- **Import discipline:** Direct imports only — `import { Button } from '@/components/ui/button'`, NOT from barrel files like `'@/components/ui'`. Use `cn()` from `@/lib/utils` for conditional class composition.\n+- **File organization:** `components/ui/` for design system leaves, `components/<domain>/` for deep components (e.g., `components/chat/`, `components/toyo/`), `hooks/` for stateful logic extraction, `lib/` for pure utilities.\n+- **Semantic color tokens:** Use `bg-card`, `text-muted-foreground`, never raw Tailwind colors like `bg-blue-500`. No manual `dark:` overrides.\n+- **data-slot attributes:** Follow ShadCN convention — each component renders a `data-slot` attribute for styling hooks.\n+- **Testing:** Vitest + React Testing Library. Test components through rendered behavior, not implementation details.\n+- **React Router:** Use React Router for client-side routing.\n+\n+## Project Context\n+\n+Darkfactory is a mission orchestration system built as Claude Code skills. This mission adds frontend architecture guidance. These two files are the foundation that all other skill files reference.\n+\n+## Architecture\n+\n+These files live in `skills/frontend/` alongside SKILL.md (task 3), PATTERNS.md, and TESTING.md (task 4). SKILL.md will link to both files via markdown links. Gate 7 in the scrutiny validator (task 2) will reference DEEP-COMPONENTS.md criteria for its evaluation.\n+\n+## Key Terms (from UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md)\n+\n+- **Deep component**: A React component with a small prop interface that hides significant state, effects, and rendering logic, owning one user-facing workflow end-to-end.\n+- **Allowed-shallow exception**: A component that is intentionally thin and exempt from depth rules.\n+- **Small semantic interface**: A component prop interface where each prop represents a domain concept, not an implementation knob.\n+- **Derive don't sync**: Computing values during render instead of syncing state with useEffect.\n+- **Composition over configuration**: Using compound component slots and children instead of config objects.\n+- **Collapse coordination**: A deep component owns one workflow end-to-end, exposing semantic events not coordination knobs.\n+\n+## Domain Types\n+\n+None for this task.\n+\n+## What Previous Tasks Built\n+\n+This is the first task. No prior code has been committed for this mission.\n+\n+## Downstream Consumers\n+\n+- Task 2 (gate 7) references DEEP-COMPONENTS.md criteria for React component evaluation\n+- Task 3 (SKILL.md) links to both files via markdown\n+- Task 4 (PATTERNS.md) illustrates the rules defined in DEEP-COMPONENTS.md\n+\n+## Procedures\n+\n+- Use `/tdd` to implement this task\n+- Commit all changes (code + tests) in a single commit with message: \"[task-1] Add foundation vocabulary files (DEEP-COMPONENTS.md, STACK.md)\"\n+- Write your handoff report to openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/mission/handoffs/task-1.md\n+\n+## Handoff Report Format\n+\n+- Task: Task 1 - Foundation vocabulary files\n+- Commit SHA: <the full SHA>\n+- Approach: <brief explanation of what you did and why>\n+- Commands run: <any commands and their exit codes>\n+- Concerns: <anything you're uncertain about>\ndiff --git a/openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/mission/briefs/task-2.md b/openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/mission/briefs/task-2.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..0506bba\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/mission/briefs/task-2.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,117 @@\n+# Worker Brief: Task 2 - Scrutiny validator gate 7 + gate renumbering + gate 1 update\n+\n+## Your Task\n+\n+Modify `skills/mission/prompts/scrutiny-validator.md` to:\n+1. Insert a new gate 7 (Frontend depth review) after gate 6 (Module depth review)\n+2. Renumber existing gates 7-14 to 8-15\n+3. Update gate 1 (test presence) to be methodology-aware\n+\n+The file is 301 lines. The gate sequence starts at line 113 with `1. **Test presence gate:**`. The current gate numbering is 1-14.\n+\n+## Exact Changes\n+\n+### Change 1: Insert gate 7 after gate 6\n+\n+After the current gate 6 (Module depth review, which ends around line 159), insert the following new gate:\n+\n+```markdown\n+7. **Frontend depth review:** If the diff contains zero `.tsx` or `.jsx` files, report `frontend-depth | SKIP | no React component files in diff` and move to the next gate.\n+\n+   When `.tsx`/`.jsx` files are present, evaluate each against the four deep-component rules defined in `skills/frontend/DEEP-COMPONENTS.md`:\n+\n+   - **Small semantic interface:** Flag components where the caller must understand more than 7 independent semantic concepts (count props + context providers consumed + URL params read + cache keys depended on). Do not count raw prop count alone — a component with 6 props describing one domain concept is deep. Exempt components in `*/ui/*` directories, components with only `className` + `children` + `...rest` props (design system leaves), and components importing from `@radix-ui/*` that wrap a Radix primitive with styling (headless behavior primitives).\n+   - **Derive don't sync:** Flag `useEffect` paired with `setState` where the effect body is pure data transformation (no I/O, no subscriptions, no browser APIs). Suggest `useMemo` or inline computation as remediation. Do not flag effects that perform I/O, subscribe to external sources, or call imperative browser APIs.\n+   - **Composition over configuration:** Flag components accepting config-style props — arrays of item objects or option objects with more than 5 configuration entries — where compound components with children/slots would be clearer. Do not flag headless primitives or design system components that use config props by convention.\n+   - **Collapse coordination:** Flag components that expose coordination knobs such as `onStep1Complete`, `onValidate`, `onReset`, `onLoadingChange` rather than semantic events such as `onSubmit`, `onCancel`, `onSelect`, `onChange`. Coordination knobs indicate the parent is driving the child's internal workflow rather than the child owning it.\n+\n+   Allowed-shallow exceptions (do not flag these for depth violations):\n+   - Components in `*/ui/*` directories\n+   - Components with only `className` + `children` + `...rest` props\n+   - Components importing from `@radix-ui/*` that wrap a Radix primitive\n+   - Route/layout glue components (thin wrappers that read route params and pass data)\n+\n+   Verdict:\n+   - PASS: No violations found, or all flagged items are in allowed-shallow exception categories.\n+   - WARN: Isolated finding in a single component.\n+   - FAIL: Systematic violations found across multiple components in the diff.\n+\n+   Report: Write one bullet per finding instance; state which component, which rule, and what specifically violates it. If nothing flagged, write \"No frontend depth issues.\"\n+```\n+\n+### Change 2: Renumber gates 7-14 to 8-15\n+\n+After inserting the new gate 7, renumber the existing gates:\n+- Current gate 7 (Code standards) → gate 8\n+- Current gate 8 (Code simplify) → gate 9\n+- Current gate 9 (Security review) → gate 10\n+- Current gate 10 (Contract checks) → gate 11\n+- Current gate 11 (Behavioral conformance) → gate 12\n+- Current gate 12 (Silent skip detection) → gate 13\n+- Current gate 13 (Diff coverage) → gate 14\n+- Current gate 14 (Test quality review) → gate 15\n+\n+### Change 3: Update gate 1\n+\n+Current gate 1 text (line 113):\n+```\n+1. **Test presence gate:** ... Workers are required to use /tdd -- no new tests means TDD was not followed. ...\n+```\n+\n+Change to be methodology-aware:\n+```\n+1. **Test presence gate:** Run `git show <commit-sha> --stat` and check if any test files were added or modified. If the diff contains zero test files and zero new test assertions, this is an automatic FAIL. If the task has `Skill: /tdd`, the rationale is \"TDD not followed.\" If the task has `Skill: /frontend`, the rationale is \"/frontend Test phase not followed.\" Exception: closing tasks that produce no testable code (documentation, cleanup, module shape re-check) are exempt from this gate.\n+```\n+\n+### Change 4: Update Gate Results output format\n+\n+The output format table (around line 270) lists gate rows. Add a row for gate 7 and renumber:\n+```\n+| Gate 7: Frontend depth review | PASS/FAIL/WARN/SKIP | ... |\n+```\n+\n+## Project Context\n+\n+The scrutiny validator is the spine of Darkfactory's validation system. Every worker's commit passes through these gates. This change adds React-specific quality checks while preserving all existing functionality.\n+\n+## Architecture\n+\n+The gate sequence is a flat numbered list in a single markdown file. Gates are independent — each reads the diff and produces a verdict. The new gate follows the self-skipping pattern established by gate 9 (Security review): check a condition, skip if not applicable.\n+\n+## Key Terms\n+\n+- **Gate**: A numbered step in the scrutiny validator's sequence. Reports PASS, FAIL, WARN, SKIP, or N/A.\n+- **Self-skipping gate**: A gate that naturally skips itself when the diff contains no relevant files.\n+- **Deep component**: A React component with a small prop interface hiding significant behavior.\n+- **Allowed-shallow exception**: A component exempt from depth rules (design system leaf, route glue, adapter, headless primitive).\n+- **Methodology**: /tdd (red-green-refactor) or /frontend (design-implement-test), assigned per task.\n+\n+## Domain Types\n+\n+None for this task.\n+\n+## What Previous Tasks Built\n+\n+### Task 1: Foundation vocabulary files\n+- Created: skills/frontend/DEEP-COMPONENTS.md, skills/frontend/STACK.md\n+- DEEP-COMPONENTS.md defines: four deep-component rules (Small Semantic Interfaces, Derive Don't Sync, Composition Over Configuration, Collapse Coordination), allowed-shallow exceptions (design system leaves, route/layout glue, adapter components, headless behavior primitives), and the deletion test\n+- STACK.md defines: React 19 + Vite + TailwindCSS 4 + Radix/ShadCN + Vitest + React Router stack, import discipline, file organization, semantic tokens, data-slot conventions\n+\n+## Downstream Consumers\n+\n+- Gate 7 is consumed by every future mission that touches .tsx/.jsx files\n+- The gate renumbering affects any UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md references to gate numbers (updated in task 10)\n+\n+## Procedures\n+\n+- Use `/tdd` to implement this task\n+- Commit all changes in a single commit with message: \"[task-2] Add frontend depth gate 7 and renumber gates\"\n+- Write your handoff report to openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/mission/handoffs/task-2.md\n+\n+## Handoff Report Format\n+\n+- Task: Task 2 - Scrutiny validator gate 7 + renumbering + gate 1 update\n+- Commit SHA: <the full SHA>\n+- Approach: <brief explanation of what you did and why>\n+- Commands run: <any commands and their exit codes>\n+- Concerns: <anything you're uncertain about>\ndiff --git a/openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/mission/briefs/task-3.md b/openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/mission/briefs/task-3.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..23cb9b9\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/mission/briefs/task-3.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,130 @@\n+# Worker Brief: Task 3 - Core /frontend SKILL.md\n+\n+## Your Task\n+\n+Write the main `skills/frontend/SKILL.md` file — the core builder guide for React/TypeScript component development. This is a prescriptive, worker-facing skill that defines the design-implement-test workflow.\n+\n+The file MUST start with this YAML frontmatter:\n+\n+```yaml\n+---\n+name: frontend\n+user-invokable: true\n+description: Prescriptive builder guide for React/TypeScript component development. Use when building frontend UI components, pages, or layouts. Defines the design-implement-test workflow with visual verification. Not for hooks, utilities, or backend code — those use /tdd.\n+---\n+```\n+\n+## Workflow\n+\n+Define a workflow with these phases, executed as a per-component loop:\n+\n+### Phase 1: Scan\n+Instruct the worker to:\n+- Search existing components in the feature area (grep for domain nouns in component file names)\n+- Identify reusable ShadCN/Radix primitives already in use (`grep -r \"@/components/ui\"`)\n+- Check existing hooks to consume (not write — hook creation is a separate /tdd task)\n+- Open 3-5 nearby components and their test files to learn patterns\n+- Check for existing dev routes, stories, or fixtures for visual verification\n+- Write a **scan note** listing: similar components found, reusable primitives, existing hooks, test pattern, visual mount point, constraints\n+\n+### Phase 2: Contract (per component, lightweight)\n+Instruct the worker to declare before building each component:\n+- **Component name**\n+- **Deep or allowed-shallow** classification with reason (if shallow)\n+- **Prop interface** with types — list each prop and what domain concept it represents\n+- **Key render states** — only those that apply: default, loading, error, empty, disabled\n+\n+This is NOT a heavy artifact. Four items, written as a comment block or in the scan note.\n+\n+### Phase 3: Build (per component, with visual verification)\n+Instruct the worker to:\n+- Implement the component, composing from existing ShadCN/Radix primitives\n+- Apply the four deep-component rules from [DEEP-COMPONENTS.md](DEEP-COMPONENTS.md)\n+- Follow stack conventions from [STACK.md](STACK.md)\n+- If `browser_tools: true` in mission config: visually verify via chrome-devtools-mcp (navigate to the component, check layout, check render states)\n+- If `browser_tools: false` (human override): skip visual verification and proceed to Test\n+\n+### Phase 4: Test (per component)\n+Instruct the worker to:\n+- Write behavioral tests using Vitest + React Testing Library\n+- Follow testing guidance from [TESTING.md](TESTING.md)\n+- Test through rendered output: query by role, label, visible text; fire user events; assert visible outcomes\n+- Do NOT test implementation details (hook calls, internal state, prop plumbing, class names)\n+\n+### Per-Component Loop (forcing function)\n+State clearly: \"Complete Contract → Build → Test for each component before starting the next component. Do not build all components then test at the end.\"\n+\n+### Deep-Component Audit (before commit)\n+Include a checklist the worker runs after all components are built and tested:\n+\n+```\n+Before committing, review every .tsx file you created or modified:\n+[ ] Each prop represents a semantic domain concept, not an implementation knob\n+[ ] No useEffect syncing derived state (use useMemo or inline computation)\n+[ ] No config objects where compound components with slots would work\n+[ ] Parent doesn't coordinate state that belongs inside this component\n+[ ] Shallow components are classified as allowed-shallow with a reason\n+[ ] Behavioral tests cover key render states and user interactions\n+```\n+\n+## References\n+\n+Include these markdown links in the file:\n+- `[DEEP-COMPONENTS.md](DEEP-COMPONENTS.md)` — Four rules and allowed-shallow exceptions\n+- `[STACK.md](STACK.md)` — Technology stack and conventions\n+- `[PATTERNS.md](PATTERNS.md)` — Concrete code examples (created in task 4)\n+- `[TESTING.md](TESTING.md)` — Frontend behavioral testing guidance (created in task 4)\n+\n+## Project Context\n+\n+This skill is the frontend counterpart to `/tdd`. While `/tdd` uses red-green-refactor for code with testable interfaces, `/frontend` uses design-implement-test for React components where the output is visual and emergent.\n+\n+## Architecture\n+\n+The file goes in `skills/frontend/SKILL.md` alongside the foundation files created in task 1 (DEEP-COMPONENTS.md, STACK.md). It will be referenced by the worker brief template (task 7) when a task has `Skill: /frontend`.\n+\n+## Key Terms\n+\n+- **Methodology**: /tdd (red-green-refactor) or /frontend (design-implement-test). Mutually exclusive per task.\n+- **Design-implement-test**: The /frontend workflow. Design component interfaces, build with visual verification, then write behavioral tests.\n+- **Component contract**: Lightweight per-component declaration (name, deep/shallow, props, render states) written before building.\n+- **Visual verification**: Using chrome-devtools-mcp during Build to confirm correct rendering.\n+- **Deep component**: A React component with small prop interface hiding significant behavior, owning one workflow.\n+- **Allowed-shallow exception**: Intentionally thin component exempt from depth rules.\n+\n+## Domain Types\n+\n+None for this task.\n+\n+## What Previous Tasks Built\n+\n+### Task 1: Foundation vocabulary files\n+- Created: skills/frontend/DEEP-COMPONENTS.md, skills/frontend/STACK.md\n+- DEEP-COMPONENTS.md: four rules (Small Semantic Interfaces, Derive Don't Sync, Composition Over Configuration, Collapse Coordination), allowed-shallow exceptions (design system leaves, route/layout glue, adapters, headless primitives), deletion test\n+- STACK.md: React 19 + Vite + TailwindCSS 4 + Radix/ShadCN + Vitest + React Router, import discipline (no barrels, cn()), file organization, semantic tokens, data-slot\n+\n+### Task 2: Scrutiny validator gate 7\n+- Modified: skills/mission/prompts/scrutiny-validator.md\n+- Inserted gate 7 (Frontend depth review) — self-skipping, checks four rules\n+- Renumbered gates 7-14 to 8-15 (now 15 gates total)\n+- Gate 1 now methodology-aware (\"/frontend Test phase not followed\")\n+\n+## Downstream Consumers\n+\n+- Task 4 (PATTERNS.md, TESTING.md) illustrates the workflow and rules defined here\n+- Task 7 (template modifications) references this skill in worker brief Procedures\n+- Task 8 (smoke test) verifies frontmatter and links\n+\n+## Procedures\n+\n+- Use `/tdd` to implement this task\n+- Commit all changes in a single commit with message: \"[task-3] Add core /frontend SKILL.md\"\n+- Write your handoff report to openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/mission/handoffs/task-3.md\n+\n+## Handoff Report Format\n+\n+- Task: Task 3 - Core /frontend SKILL.md\n+- Commit SHA: <the full SHA>\n+- Approach: <brief explanation>\n+- Commands run: <any commands and their exit codes>\n+- Concerns: <anything uncertain>\ndiff --git a/openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/mission/briefs/task-4.md b/openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/mission/briefs/task-4.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..a514e23\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/mission/briefs/task-4.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,234 @@\n+# Worker Brief: Task 4 - PATTERNS.md and TESTING.md\n+\n+## Your Task\n+\n+Write two reference files in `skills/frontend/`:\n+1. `PATTERNS.md` — concrete code snippets illustrating the deep-component rules\n+2. `TESTING.md` — frontend behavioral testing guidance\n+\n+## PATTERNS.md\n+\n+Write PATTERNS.md with the following structure. Use the pre-extracted code snippets below. Each snippet is 5-10 lines. Label each with the rule it illustrates.\n+\n+### Deep Component Examples (at least 2)\n+\n+**Example 1: FilesDrawer — small prop interface owning a workflow**\n+Source: ~/Code/toyo (file management drawer)\n+Rule: Small Semantic Interfaces + Collapse Coordination\n+\n+```typescript\n+interface FilesDrawerProps {\n+  open: boolean\n+  onClose: () => void\n+  mode?: \"drawer\" | \"page\"\n+}\n+```\n+\n+Three props, two semantic events. The component owns file upload, delete, directory navigation, drag-drop, and folder creation internally. The parent only knows \"open/close\" and \"drawer or page mode.\"\n+\n+**Example 2: BrowserPane — derives state from props**\n+Source: ~/Code/toyo (browser preview pane)\n+Rule: Derive Don't Sync\n+\n+```typescript\n+const iframeUrl = useMemo(\n+  () => buildLiveViewUrl(browserSession.liveViewUrl, readOnlyMode),\n+  [browserSession.liveViewUrl, readOnlyMode],\n+)\n+```\n+\n+The iframe URL is derived during render via useMemo, not stored in state and synced with useEffect. The component has ~8 props but they describe one concept (browser session display).\n+\n+### Allowed-Shallow Examples (at least 2)\n+\n+**Example 1: Button — design system leaf**\n+Source: ~/Code/toyo (UI primitives)\n+Rule: Allowed-shallow exception — design system leaf\n+\n+```tsx\n+function Button({\n+  className,\n+  variant = \"default\",\n+  size = \"default\",\n+  asChild = false,\n+  ...props\n+}: ButtonProps) {\n+  const Comp = asChild ? Slot.Root : \"button\"\n+  return (\n+    <Comp\n+      data-slot=\"button\"\n+      className={cn(buttonVariants({ variant, size, className }))}\n+      {...props}\n+    />\n+  )\n+}\n+```\n+\n+Zero logic. CVA for variants, Slot for polymorphism, rest spread. This is intentionally shallow — its job is visual consistency, not workflow ownership.\n+\n+**Example 2: Card + CardHeader — compound component pattern**\n+Source: ~/Code/toyo (UI primitives)\n+Rule: Composition over Configuration (design system side)\n+\n+```tsx\n+function Card({ className, ...props }: React.ComponentProps<\"div\">) {\n+  return (\n+    <div\n+      data-slot=\"card\"\n+      className={cn(\"bg-card text-card-foreground flex flex-col gap-6 rounded-xl border py-6 shadow-sm\", className)}\n+      {...props}\n+    />\n+  )\n+}\n+\n+function CardHeader({ className, ...props }: React.ComponentProps<\"div\">) {\n+  return (\n+    <div\n+      data-slot=\"card-header\"\n+      className={cn(\"@container/card-header grid auto-rows-min ...\", className)}\n+      {...props}\n+    />\n+  )\n+}\n+```\n+\n+Each sub-component is a thin wrapper. Callers compose: `<Card><CardHeader>...</CardHeader><CardContent>...</CardContent></Card>`. No config objects.\n+\n+### Hook Pattern — Derive Don't Sync (at least 1)\n+\n+**Example: useChatScroll — pure function derives from DOM**\n+Source: ~/Code/toyo (chat scroll behavior)\n+Rule: Derive Don't Sync\n+\n+```typescript\n+export function isAtBottomPosition(\n+  element: Pick<HTMLDivElement, \"scrollHeight\" | \"scrollTop\" | \"clientHeight\">\n+): boolean {\n+  return element.scrollHeight - element.scrollTop - element.clientHeight < AT_BOTTOM_THRESHOLD\n+}\n+\n+// Inside useChatScroll:\n+function onScroll() {\n+  const el = scrollRef.current\n+  if (!el) return\n+  const atBottom = isAtBottomPosition(el)\n+  isBottomLockedRef.current = getNextBottomLockState({\n+    atBottom,\n+    nextScrollTop: el.scrollTop,\n+    previousScrollTop: previousScrollTopRef.current,\n+    wasLocked: isBottomLockedRef.current,\n+    isUserScrollUp: recentUserScrollIntentRef.current === \"up\",\n+  })\n+  setIsAtBottom(atBottom)\n+}\n+```\n+\n+Pure function computes `isAtBottom` from DOM measurements. Lock state lives in a ref (not useState). Display state (`isAtBottom`) is the only useState — it's the minimal state needed for rendering.\n+\n+### Anti-Pattern with Fix (at least 1)\n+\n+**Anti-pattern: useEffect syncing derived state**\n+\n+```typescript\n+// BAD: syncing a pure derivation via useEffect\n+const [isAtBottom, setIsAtBottom] = useState(false)\n+\n+useEffect(() => {\n+  setIsAtBottom(\n+    scrollRef.current.scrollHeight -\n+    scrollRef.current.scrollTop -\n+    scrollRef.current.clientHeight < 50\n+  )\n+}, [scrollRef.current?.scrollHeight])\n+```\n+\n+**Why it's wrong:** Derives state in an effect with incomplete dependency tracking. Creates stale closures, triggers unnecessary renders, and races with scroll events.\n+\n+**Fix:** Extract the pure function, call it in the scroll handler:\n+\n+```typescript\n+// GOOD: pure function called on demand\n+const atBottom = isAtBottomPosition(scrollRef.current)\n+setIsAtBottom(atBottom)\n+```\n+\n+## TESTING.md\n+\n+Write TESTING.md covering frontend behavioral testing. This is NOT a copy of /tdd's testing philosophy — it's React-specific.\n+\n+### Structure\n+\n+1. **Core principle:** Test what users see and do, not how the component works internally.\n+\n+2. **How to test components:**\n+   - Render the component with realistic props\n+   - Query by role, label, visible text (use `getByRole`, `getByLabelText`, `getByText`)\n+   - Fire user events with `userEvent` (click, type, tab — not `fireEvent`)\n+   - Assert visible outcomes (text appears, element disappears, callback fires)\n+\n+3. **What NOT to test:**\n+   - Prop plumbing (parent passes X, child receives X)\n+   - Hook calls (useEffect fired, useState set)\n+   - Internal state names or values\n+   - Class names or Tailwind utility classes\n+   - Snapshot tests for layout (use visual verification instead)\n+\n+4. **Hook logic boundary:**\n+   - Complex hook logic (validation, state machines, data transformation) is tested in separate `/tdd` tasks\n+   - Component tests should NOT re-test hook logic — test the component's visible behavior that results from the hook\n+\n+5. **Test survival rule:**\n+   - A good test survives refactoring that preserves behavior\n+   - If renaming internal state, extracting a sub-component, or switching from local state to a hook breaks the test, the test was coupled to implementation\n+\n+## Project Context\n+\n+These files complete the `/frontend` skill's reference library. SKILL.md (task 3) already links to both files.\n+\n+## Architecture\n+\n+Both files go in `skills/frontend/` alongside SKILL.md, DEEP-COMPONENTS.md, and STACK.md.\n+\n+## Key Terms\n+\n+- **Deep component**: Small prop interface, owns one workflow end-to-end\n+- **Allowed-shallow exception**: Intentionally thin (design system leaf, route glue, adapter, headless primitive)\n+- **Derive don't sync**: Compute during render, not in useEffect\n+- **Behavioral test**: Tests visible behavior through rendered output, not implementation details\n+\n+## Domain Types\n+\n+None for this task.\n+\n+## What Previous Tasks Built\n+\n+### Task 1: Foundation vocabulary files\n+- skills/frontend/DEEP-COMPONENTS.md: four rules, allowed-shallow exceptions, deletion test\n+- skills/frontend/STACK.md: React 19 + Vite + Tailwind 4 + ShadCN + Vitest stack\n+\n+### Task 2: Scrutiny validator gate 7\n+- Gate 7 (Frontend depth review) inserted, gates renumbered 1-15, gate 1 methodology-aware\n+\n+### Task 3: Core /frontend SKILL.md\n+- Workflow: Scan → Contract → Build (visual verify) → Test → Deep-component audit\n+- Per-component loop, checklist before commit\n+- Links to DEEP-COMPONENTS.md, STACK.md, PATTERNS.md, TESTING.md\n+\n+## Downstream Consumers\n+\n+- SKILL.md links to both files (links already exist, files need to be created)\n+- Workers following /frontend will reference PATTERNS.md for examples and TESTING.md for testing guidance\n+\n+## Procedures\n+\n+- Use `/tdd` to implement this task\n+- Commit all changes in a single commit with message: \"[task-4] Add PATTERNS.md and TESTING.md\"\n+- Write your handoff report to openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/mission/handoffs/task-4.md\n+\n+## Handoff Report Format\n+\n+- Task: Task 4 - PATTERNS.md and TESTING.md\n+- Commit SHA: <the full SHA>\n+- Approach: <brief explanation>\n+- Commands run: <any commands and their exit codes>\n+- Concerns: <anything uncertain>\ndiff --git a/openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/mission/briefs/task-7.md b/openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/mission/briefs/task-7.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..6188cb6\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/mission/briefs/task-7.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,211 @@\n+# Worker Brief: Task 7 - Template modifications, config, and mission-init\n+\n+## Your Task\n+\n+Modify 4 existing files to integrate the new `/frontend`, `/ui-system`, and `/react-perf` skills into the mission infrastructure.\n+\n+## Change 1: Worker Brief Template\n+\n+**File:** `skills/mission/templates/worker-brief.md`\n+**Line 53** currently reads:\n+```\n+- Use `/tdd` to implement this task\n+```\n+\n+Replace with conditional methodology + constraints:\n+```\n+- Use `<Skill from task topology>` to implement this task\n+  - If Skill: /frontend — \"Use `/frontend` to implement this task\"\n+  - If Skill: /tdd — \"Use `/tdd` to implement this task\"\n+- <For each Constraint in task topology, append:>\n+  - \"Also follow `/ui-system` for component selection and token discipline\"\n+  - \"Also follow `/react-perf` for performance optimization patterns\"\n+```\n+\n+The orchestrator reads the task's `Skill:` and `Constraints:` fields from topology metadata and populates this section. The template should show the conditional pattern so the orchestrator knows what to insert.\n+\n+## Change 2: Design Template\n+\n+**File:** `skills/mission/templates/design-template.md`\n+**Location:** Module Inventory section (around line 56-62)\n+\n+After the existing Module Inventory table format, add a paragraph for frontend modules:\n+\n+```markdown\n+### Frontend Module Guidance\n+\n+For React frontend modules, describe:\n+- **Prop interface:** how many semantic concepts the caller must understand (count props + context + URL params + cache dependencies, not raw prop count)\n+- **State/effects encapsulated:** what state management and effects the component hides behind its interface\n+- **Classification:** deep component (owns a workflow end-to-end) or allowed-shallow exception (design system leaf, route/layout glue, adapter, headless behavior primitive) with the reason for the classification\n+\n+Reference `/frontend` skill's DEEP-COMPONENTS.md for the four deep-component rules and allowed-shallow categories.\n+```\n+\n+## Change 3: Mission Config Template\n+\n+**File:** `skills/mission/SKILL.md`\n+**Location:** Phase 6 config.yaml template (search for the `config.yaml` section that defines the engines)\n+\n+Add `browser_tools: false` to the config.yaml template, and add a comment explaining it:\n+\n+```yaml\n+engines:\n+  worker: codex\n+  scrutiny_validator: claude\n+  usertest_validator: claude\n+  adversarial_reviewer_a: codex\n+  adversarial_reviewer_b: claude\n+  demo_video: claude\n+\n+browser_tools: false\n+```\n+\n+Note: The orchestrator auto-sets this to `true` during Phase 4.3a when any task has `Skill: /frontend`.\n+\n+## Change 4: Orchestrator Behaviors in Mission SKILL.md\n+\n+**File:** `skills/mission/SKILL.md`\n+\n+Add the following orchestrator behaviors. Find the appropriate locations in the existing phases:\n+\n+### In Phase 4.3a (Task Strategy Approval section):\n+\n+Add after the existing decomposition approach guidance:\n+\n+```markdown\n+#### Frontend Task Decomposition (TypeScript React projects only)\n+\n+For TypeScript React projects, use the specific task layer vocabulary:\n+\n+| Layer | Skill | Rationale |\n+|---|---|---|\n+| `frontend/component` | `/frontend` | Visual React component work |\n+| `frontend/page` | `/frontend` | Page composition |\n+| `frontend/layout` | `/frontend` | Visual structure |\n+| `frontend/hooks` | `/tdd` | Hooks have testable interfaces |\n+| `backend` | `/tdd` | APIs, server logic |\n+| `shared/types` | `/tdd` | Type contracts |\n+| `shared/schema` | `/tdd` | Zod validation, pure logic |\n+| `shared/utils` | `/tdd` | Pure utility functions |\n+\n+**Mechanical rule:** `/frontend` only when the layer starts with `frontend/` AND is not `frontend/hooks`. Everything else gets `/tdd`.\n+\n+Auto-set `browser_tools: true` in config.yaml when any task has `Skill: /frontend`.\n+\n+When a frontend feature contains complex logic (validation, state machines, data transformation), split it: one `/tdd` task for the logic as a hook/utility, one `/frontend` task for the component that consumes it. The `/tdd` task comes first in the task list.\n+```\n+\n+### In Phase 4.4 (Generate and Review Tasks section):\n+\n+Add after the existing Task Topology format:\n+\n+```markdown\n+#### Skill and Constraint Validation (TypeScript React projects only)\n+\n+Task topology for TypeScript React projects includes two additional fields:\n+\n+```\n+Skill: </tdd or /frontend>\n+Constraints: </ui-system, /react-perf, or \"none\">\n+```\n+\n+Validation rules:\n+- Exactly one `Skill:` value per task — either `/tdd` or `/frontend`\n+- Zero or more `Constraints:` values\n+- `/ui-system` and `/react-perf` are only valid with `Skill: /frontend`\n+- Flag invalid combinations during Phase 4.4 human review\n+```\n+\n+### In Step 2 (Dispatch Worker section):\n+\n+Add a pre-flight check:\n+\n+```markdown\n+#### Browser Tools Pre-flight (Skill: /frontend tasks only)\n+\n+Before dispatching a `/frontend` task, check that chrome-devtools-mcp is available:\n+- If available: proceed with dispatch, include visual verification in the brief\n+- If unavailable: block dispatch. Log to progress.md: `<timestamp> -- Task N: chrome-devtools-mcp unavailable at dispatch. Pausing.` Surface to human with options: retry (check again), skip visual verify for this task, or abort mission\n+```\n+\n+### In Step 1 (Assemble Brief section):\n+\n+Add:\n+\n+```markdown\n+#### Browser Tools Override\n+\n+If `browser_tools: false` in config.yaml (human override), omit visual verification procedures from the worker brief even for `/frontend` tasks. The worker follows the `/frontend` workflow but skips the chrome-devtools-mcp visual verify step in the Build phase.\n+```\n+\n+## Change 5: Mission-Init Update\n+\n+**File:** `skills/mission-init/SKILL.md`\n+\n+Add a new check in Step 3 (Verify CLI Dependencies) or as a new step:\n+\n+```markdown\n+### Browser Tools Check (conditional)\n+\n+If `browser_tools: true` in the mission's config.yaml (or if any task in the current mission has `Skill: /frontend`), check that chrome-devtools-mcp is registered:\n+\n+```bash\n+# Check if chrome-devtools MCP tools are available\n+# The exact check depends on the MCP registration mechanism\n+```\n+\n+If chrome-devtools-mcp is not registered:\n+- Report: `[!] chrome-devtools-mcp - not registered (required when browser_tools: true)`\n+- Fix: Install chrome-devtools-mcp from https://github.com/nichochar/chrome-devtools-mcp and add it to MCP configuration\n+- This blocks mission launch for missions with `/frontend` tasks\n+\n+If `browser_tools: false` or no `/frontend` tasks exist, skip this check.\n+```\n+\n+## Project Context\n+\n+These changes wire the new frontend skills into the mission orchestrator. After this task, the orchestrator knows how to assign `/frontend` vs `/tdd`, validate constraints, check browser tools, and assemble the right worker briefs.\n+\n+## Architecture\n+\n+All changes are to existing markdown files in `skills/mission/` and `skills/mission-init/`. No new files.\n+\n+## Key Terms\n+\n+- **Methodology**: /tdd or /frontend, mutually exclusive per task\n+- **Constraint**: /ui-system or /react-perf, additive, only with /frontend\n+- **Task layer**: Vocabulary value in topology that determines methodology\n+- **Browser tools**: Config flag for chrome-devtools-mcp availability\n+- **Visual verification**: chrome-devtools-mcp usage during /frontend Build phase\n+\n+## What Previous Tasks Built\n+\n+### Tasks 1-4: /frontend skill (complete)\n+- skills/frontend/: SKILL.md, DEEP-COMPONENTS.md, STACK.md, PATTERNS.md, TESTING.md\n+\n+### Task 2: Scrutiny validator\n+- Gate 7 (Frontend depth review) inserted, gates renumbered 1-15, gate 1 methodology-aware\n+\n+### Tasks 5-6: Supplementary skills\n+- skills/ui-system/SKILL.md: ShadCN/Radix component guidelines\n+- skills/react-perf/SKILL.md: Vercel React performance best practices\n+\n+## Downstream Consumers\n+\n+- Task 8 (smoke test) verifies all these changes\n+- Every future mission uses the updated templates and orchestrator behaviors\n+\n+## Procedures\n+\n+- Use `/tdd` to implement this task\n+- Commit all changes in a single commit with message: \"[task-7] Wire frontend skills into mission infrastructure\"\n+- Write your handoff report to openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/mission/handoffs/task-7.md\n+\n+## Handoff Report Format\n+\n+- Task: Task 7 - Template modifications, config, and mission-init\n+- Commit SHA: <the full SHA>\n+- Approach: <brief explanation>\n+- Commands run: <any commands and their exit codes>\n+- Concerns: <anything uncertain>\ndiff --git a/openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/mission/config.yaml b/openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/mission/config.yaml\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..ffd5988\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/mission/config.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@\n+engines:\n+  worker: codex\n+  scrutiny_validator: claude\n+  usertest_validator: claude\n+  adversarial_reviewer_a: codex\n+  adversarial_reviewer_b: claude\n+  demo_video: claude\n+\n+browser_tools: false\n+base_branch: main\ndiff --git a/openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/mission/handoffs/task-1.md b/openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/mission/handoffs/task-1.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..44506e4\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/mission/handoffs/task-1.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@\n+Implemented Task 1 and committed the docs/test files.\n+\n+Commit: `ea9c876116842586f8346235c81d3d84e6cbb89b`\n+\n+Added:\n+- [DEEP-COMPONENTS.md](/Users/stuart/.darkfactory/skills/frontend/DEEP-COMPONENTS.md)\n+- [STACK.md](/Users/stuart/.darkfactory/skills/frontend/STACK.md)\n+- [test-task-1.sh](/Users/stuart/.darkfactory/openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/mission/tests/test-task-1.sh)\n+\n+Handoff written to [task-1.md](/Users/stuart/.darkfactory/openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/mission/handoffs/task-1.md). It is intentionally uncommitted so it can name the final commit SHA.\n+\n+Checks run:\n+- `openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/mission/tests/test-task-1.sh` -> pass\n+- `git diff --check -- ...` -> pass\n+- ASCII check -> pass\n\\ No newline at end of file\ndiff --git a/openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/mission/handoffs/task-2.md b/openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/mission/handoffs/task-2.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..5ec5b0f\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/mission/handoffs/task-2.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@\n+Implemented and committed the validator update.\n+\n+Commit: `43d68103f290813bc3b2a3b047e93b3cbf903d4f`\n+\n+Changed [scrutiny-validator.md](/Users/stuart/.darkfactory/skills/mission/prompts/scrutiny-validator.md:113):\n+- Gate 1 is now methodology-aware for `/tdd` and `/frontend`.\n+- Added new Gate 7: Frontend depth review.\n+- Renumbered old gates 7-14 to 8-15.\n+- Updated the output table through Gate 15.\n+\n+Wrote the handoff report at [task-2.md](/Users/stuart/.darkfactory/openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/mission/handoffs/task-2.md:1). It is uncommitted because it needed the final commit SHA.\n+\n+Checks run:\n+- Red text check before edit: expected fail.\n+- Sequential gate numbering assertion: pass.\n+- Required text assertions with `rg`: pass.\n+- `test -f skills/frontend/DEEP-COMPONENTS.md`: pass.\n+- `git diff --check`: pass after removing one trailing space.\n+\n+Skipped full build/tests because this was a markdown-only validator prompt change.\n\\ No newline at end of file\ndiff --git a/openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/mission/handoffs/task-3.md b/openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/mission/handoffs/task-3.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..7898cba\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/mission/handoffs/task-3.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@\n+Implemented and committed [skills/frontend/SKILL.md](/Users/stuart/.darkfactory/skills/frontend/SKILL.md:1).\n+\n+Commit: `794e93914aabeb97040396ceef994750ae5a4381`\n+\n+Wrote the handoff at [task-3.md](/Users/stuart/.darkfactory/openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/mission/handoffs/task-3.md:1). It is uncommitted, matching the prior handoff pattern, so it can contain the final commit SHA.\n+\n+Checks run:\n+- Red check: `test -f skills/frontend/SKILL.md` failed as expected before creation.\n+- Exact frontmatter `diff -u` check passed.\n+- Required workflow/link string validation passed.\n+- `git diff --cached --check -- skills/frontend/SKILL.md` passed.\n+\n+Skipped full build/tests because this was a markdown-only skill file.\n\\ No newline at end of file\ndiff --git a/openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/mission/handoffs/task-4.md b/openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/mission/handoffs/task-4.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..904f282\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/mission/handoffs/task-4.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,