dance focused on user-visible behavior and refactor-resistant tests.\\n\\nCommands run:\\n\\n- `sed -n '1,220p' /Users/stuart/.darkfactory/skills/tdd/SKILL.md && pwd && rg --files skills/frontend openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/mission/handoffs 2>/dev/null` - exit 0\\n- `sed -n '1,240p' skills/frontend/SKILL.md` - exit 0\\n- `sed -n '1,260p' skills/frontend/DEEP-COMPONENTS.md` - exit 0\\n- `sed -n '1,220p' skills/frontend/STACK.md` - exit 0\\n- `git status --short` - exit 0\\n- `rg -n \\\"FilesDrawer|BrowserPane|Button|CardHeader|useChatScroll|Anti-pattern|Core Principle|What Not to Test|Hook Logic Boundary|Test Survival Rule\\\" skills/frontend/PATTERNS.md skills/frontend/TESTING.md` - exit 0\\n- `git diff -- skills/frontend/PATTERNS.md skills/frontend/TESTING.md` - exit 0\\n- `git status --short -- skills/frontend/PATTERNS.md skills/frontend/TESTING.md openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/mission/handoffs/task-4.md` - exit 0\\n- `sed -n '1,240p' skills/frontend/PATTERNS.md && sed -n '1,180p' skills/frontend/TESTING.md` - exit 0\\n- `sed -n '1,120p' openspec/changes/frontend-architecture-skill/mission/handoffs/task-3.md 2>/dev/null || true` - exit 0\\n- `test -f skills/frontend/PATTERNS.md` - exit 0\\n- `test -f skills/frontend/TESTING.md` - exit 0\\n- `git add skills/frontend/PATTERNS.md skills/frontend/TESTING.md && git diff --cached --check -- skills/frontend/PATTERNS.md skills/frontend/TESTING.md && git diff --cached --stat -- skills/frontend/PATTERNS.md skills/frontend/TESTING.md` - exit 0\\n- `git diff --cached -- skills/frontend/PATTERNS.md skills/frontend/TESTING.md` - exit 0\\n- `git diff --cached --name-only && git status --short` - exit 0\\n- `git commit -m \\\"[task-4] Add PATTERNS.md and TESTING.md\\\"` - exit 0\\n- `git rev-parse HEAD` - exit 0\\n\\nConcerns: No code or test suite was changed, so I did not run a frontend build or Vitest. The handoff is intentionally uncommitted so it can contain the final commit SHA, matching `tas