in Step 2 before  [... omitted end of long line]\\nskills/mission/SKILL.md:716:5. **If more tasks remain:** Go back to Step 1 for the next task.\\nskills/mission/SKILL.md:787:- **Reviewer A** (engine from `adversarial_reviewer_a` in config.yaml, default: codex) -- dispatched via Bash with `run_in_background: true`\\nskills/mission/SKILL.md:788:- **Reviewer B** (engine from `adversarial_reviewer_b` in config.yaml, default: claude) -- dispatched via Agent tool\\nskills/mission/SKILL.md:792:Before dispatching either reviewer, read `base_branch` from `openspec/changes/<change-name>/mission/config.yaml` and use it in place of `<base-branch> [... omitted end of long line]\\nskills/mission/SKILL.md:795:BASE_BRANCH=$(awk -F: '/^[[:space:]]*base_branch[[:space:]]*:/ { gsub(/^[[:space:]]+|[[:space:]]+$/, \\\"\\\", $2); print $2; exit }' openspec/changes/<chan [... omitted end of long line]\\nskills/mission/SKILL.md:797:  echo \\\"ABORT: base_branch missing from openspec/changes/<change-name>/mission/config.yaml\\\"\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"tool_end\",\"dispatch_id\":\"01KQR4JYYSZS01CS01QFAKE5E0\",\"ts\":\"2026-05-04T00:00:59Z\",\"tool\":\"command_execution\"}\n+{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_7\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"The worktree already has many unrelated mission files and one modified glossary. I’ll leave those alone and stage only the four requested markdown files plus the task handoff I create.\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_8\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '202,252p' skills/mission/SKILL.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"command_run\",\"dispatch_id\":\"01KQR4JYYSZS01CS01QFAKE5E0\",\"ts\":\"2026-05-04T00:01:05Z\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '202,252p' skills/mission/SKILL.md\\\"\"}\n+{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_8\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '202,252p' skills/mission/SKILL.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"### Phase 4.3a: Task Strategy Approval\\n\\nBefore generating tasks.md, present a task decomposition strategy for human approval:\\n\\n1. **Decomposition approach:** layered (types and domain logic first, then transport/CLI), vertical (each task cuts end-to-end through all layers), or hybrid (foundation layer first, then vertical slices). State which and why.\\n2. **Target task count range:** e.g., \\\"6-8 feature tasks + 4-5 closing tasks.\\\" Justify the range based on the module inventory from design.md.\\n3. **Dependency ordering rationale:** which tasks must come first and why (e.g., \\\"Task 1 defines core types that all subsequent tasks import\\\").\\n\\nThe human approves this strategy before tasks.md is generated. If rejected, revise and re-present.\\n\\nAfter approval, populate the task decomposition strategy anchor in the plan's Deterministic Anchors section.\\n\\nIf approved, proceed to Phase 4.4.\\n\\n### Phase 4.4: Generate and Review Tasks\\n\\nGenerate `tasks.md` (ordered checklist of implementation tasks).\\n\\n#### Task Quality Standard\\n\\nEach task must produce a concrete, testable output. When the approved strategy (Phase 4.3a) is vertical, tasks cross all layers. When the strategy is layered or hybrid, tasks may be scoped to a single layer, provided each task still has a clear done state and a test surface.\\n\\n**One task = one worker = one commit = one validation cycle.**\\n\\nA task is good if you can demo it and verify it independently after it lands.\\n\\n#### Task Topology\\n\\nEach task in tasks.md must include topology metadata in this fixed format:\\n\\n```markdown\\n- [ ] Task N: <name>\\n  Depends on: <prior task numbers, or \\\"none\\\">\\n  Consumes: <surfaces from prior tasks -- types, interfaces, endpoints>\\n  Produces: <surfaces this task creates -- types, modules, interfaces, endpoints>\\n  Layers: <logical architectural layers touched, e.g. domain, transport, storage>\\n```\\n\\nLayers are logical groupings of modules (domain, transport, storage, configuration, etc.) defined in the design narrative, not columns from the Module Inventory table.\\n\\nWhen the approved strategy (Phase 4.3a) is layered or hybrid and a task's Layers field lists more than 2 architectural layers, flag the task for human review with a recommendation to split or approve as-is. When the approved strategy is vertical, the layer count flag does not apply since vertical tasks are expected to cross all layers.\\n\\nWhen a task adds public surface area to a module (new exports, API endpoints, CLI flags), include the implementation behind that surface in the same task. Do not split a module's interface from its implementation across tasks -- the per-task validator judges depth from a single diff and will flag an interface without the work behind it.\\n\\n#### Mandatory Closing Tasks\\n\\nEvery mission's tasks.md MUST include these closing tasks after all feature tasks:\\n\\n1. **Smoke test (mandatory).** Write or update one end-to-end test that runs the project's primary user flow against real dependencies. No project-internal mocks. Place it where the project's standard test command runs it. If the mission produces no runnable user flow, note that in the handoff.\\n\\n2. **Cleanup task (mandatory).** Remove unused dependencies, dead code, leftover scaffolding, temporary artifacts, and any backwards-compatibility shims. Workers sometimes leave debris that per-task validation does not catch. This task cleans up the codebase before the shape re-check so the re-check does not flag soon-to-be-deleted surface area.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"tool_end\",\"dispatch_id\":\"01KQR4JYYSZS01CS01QFAKE5E0\",\"ts\":\"2026-05-04T00:01:05Z\",\"tool\":\"command_execution\"}\n+{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_9\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '505,535p' skills/mission/SKILL.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"command_run\",\"dispatch_id\":\"01KQR4JYYSZS01CS01QFAKE5E0\",\"ts\":\"2026-05-04T00:01:05Z\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '505,535p' skills/mission/SKILL.md\\\"\"}\n+{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_10\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '1,180p' skills/mission-init/SKILL.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"command_run\",\"dispatch_id\":\"01KQR4JYYSZS01CS01QFAKE5E0\",\"ts\":\"2026-05-04T00:01:05Z\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '1,180p' skills/mission-init/SKILL.md\\\"\"}\n+{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_9\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '505,535p' skills/mission/SKILL.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"> **Inputs:** tasks.md, contract.md, design.md, proposal.md, config.yaml, UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md\\n> **Outputs:** Committed code per task, validation reports in mission/validations/. Codebase deltas are internal (populate subsequent task briefs within this phase).\\n\\nFor each unchecked task (`- [ ]`) in tasks.md, run Steps 1-7. Process tasks in order, one at a time (serial execution). Skip tasks marked `- [~]` (skipped) and `- [x]` (complete).\\n\\n### Step 1: Assemble Brief\\n\\nWrite a brief to `mission/briefs/task-N.md`.\\n\\n#### Brief Template\\n\\nRead [templates/worker-brief.md](templates/worker-brief.md).\\n\\n**The brief NEVER contains contract.md content.** \\n\\n### Step 2: Dispatch Worker\\n\\nRead the engine from `mission/config.yaml`.\\n\\n#### If engine is `codex`:\\n\\nBefore dispatching, run `git rev-parse HEAD` and store the result as `PRE_TASK_SHA`. This value is used in Step 7 to generate the codebase delta — store it somewhere you can reference after the background worker returns (e.g. in the plan file or a local variable).\\n\\nUse the Bash tool with `run_in_background: true` to run the worker. Use this exact bash script:\\n\\n```bash\\nBRIEF_PATH=\\\"<absolute path to mission/briefs/task-N.md>\\\"\\nHANDOFF_PATH=\\\"<absolute path to mission/handoffs/task-N.md>\\\"\\nLOG_PATH=\\\"<absolute path to mission/logs/task-N-codex.log>\\\"\\nPRE_TASK_SHA=$(git rev-parse HEAD)\\n# Clean stale temp files and directories from previous workers to avoid filling /tmp\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"tool_end\",\"dispatch_id\":\"01KQR4JYYSZS01CS01QFAKE5E0\",\"ts\":\"2026-05-04T00:01:05Z\",\"tool\":\"command_execution\"}\n+{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_11\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '437,455p' skills/mission/SKILL.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"command_run\",\"dispatch_id\":\"01KQR4JYYSZS01CS01QFAKE5E0\",\"ts\":\"2026-05-04T00:01:05Z\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '437,455p' skills/mission/SKILL.md\\\"\"}\n+{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_11\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '437,455p' skills/mission/SKILL.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"### config.yaml\\n\\n```yaml\\nengines:\\n  worker: codex\\n  scrutiny_validator: claude\\n  usertest_validator: claude\\n  adversarial_reviewer_a: codex\\n  adversarial_reviewer_b: claude\\n  demo_video: claude\\n```\\n\\n### progress.md\\n\\n```markdown\\n# Mission: <change-name>\\n\\nStarted: <ISO 8601 timestamp>\\n\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"tool_end\",\"dispatch_id\":\"01KQR4JYYSZS01CS01QFAKE5E0\",\"ts\":\"2026-05-04T00:01:05Z\",\"tool\":\"command_execution\"}\n+{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_10\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '1,180p' skills/mission-init/SKILL.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"---\\nname: mission-init\\nuser-invokable: true\\ndescription: Verify that all Darkfactory skills are installed and required CLI tools are available. Run from any project before starting a mission.\\n---\\n\\n# Mission Init\\n\\nVerify the current project is ready to run `/mission`. Check skill symlinks, initialize OpenSpec if needed, verify required CLI tools, detect the coverage tool, and print one setup report.\\n\\n## Step 1: Check Skill Symlinks\\n\\nCheck these 12 owned skills:\\n\\n```bash\\nmission mission-resume mission-status mission-init grill prd language tdd test-quality security adversarial dispatch\\n```\\n\\nFor each skill, verify:\\n\\n1. `$HOME/.claude/skills/<name>` exists as a symlink, not a regular file or directory.\\n2. The symlink target exists.\\n3. `readlink \\\"$HOME/.claude/skills/<name>\\\"` equals `$HOME/.darkfactory/skills/<name>`.\\n\\nUse this status format:\\n\\n```text\\n  [x] /mission - symlink OK\\n  [ ] /adversarial - missing (symlink does not exist)\\n  [!] /dispatch - broken (symlink exists but target missing)\\n  [!] /prd - wrong target\\n```\\n\\nUse a Bash pattern that always exits 0:\\n\\n```bash\\nfor skill in mission mission-resume mission-status mission-init grill prd language tdd test-quality security adversarial dispatch; do\\n  link=\\\"$HOME/.claude/skills/$skill\\\"\\n  expected=\\\"$HOME/.darkfactory/skills/$skill\\\"\\n\\n  if [ ! -L \\\"$link\\\" ]; then\\n    echo \\\"[ ] /$skill - missing (symlink does not exist)\\\"\\n  elif [ ! -e \\\"$link\\\" ]; then\\n    echo \\\"[!] /$skill - broken (symlink exists but target missing)\\\"\\n  else\\n    target=\\\"$(readlink \\\"$link\\\" 2>/dev/null || true)\\\"\\n    if [ \\\"$target\\\" != \\\"$expected\\\" ]; then\\n      echo \\\"[!] /$skill - wrong target\\\"\\n    else\\n      echo \\\"[x] /$skill - symlink OK\\\"\\n    fi\\n  fi\\ndone\\n```\\n\\nIf any required skill is missing, broken, or points to the wrong target, instruct the user to run:\\n\\n```bash\\n~/.darkfactory/install.sh\\n```\\n\\nThen tell them to restart Claude Code and re-run `/mission-init`. Stop after reporting the missing skill fixes.\\n\\nIf all 12 skills are present and resolve correctly, report:\\n\\n```text\\nAll 12 skills: OK\\n```\\n\\nThen continue.\\n\\n## Step 2: Initialize OpenSpec\\n\\nCheck for `openspec/config.yaml` in the current directory.\\n\\nIf it exists, report:\\n\\n```text\\nOpenSpec: already initialized.\\n```\\n\\nIf it does not exist, first check whether the `openspec` CLI is available:\\n\\n```bash\\nopenspec --version 2>/dev/null || echo \\\"NOT_INSTALLED\\\"\\n```\\n\\nIf `openspec` is not installed, report:\\n\\n```text\\nOpenSpec CLI not installed. Run: `npm install -g @fission-ai/openspec`\\n```\\n\\nIf it is installed, run:\\n\\n```bash\\nopenspec init --tools claude,codex --force\\n```\\n\\nAfter a first-time init, tell the user to restart Claude Code so `/opsx:` commands can register.\\n\\n## Step 3: Verify CLI Dependencies\\n\\nRun these checks. Each command must always exit 0 so parallel Bash calls do not cancel each other:\\n\\n```bash\\ncodex --version 2>/dev/null || echo \\\"NOT_INSTALLED\\\"\\ndarkfactory-dispatch --version 2>/dev/null || echo \\\"NOT_INSTALLED\\\"\\ngh --version 2>/dev/null || echo \\\"NOT_INSTALLED\\\"\\ngh auth status 2>/dev/null || echo \\\"NOT_INSTALLED\\\"\\nopenspec --version 2>/dev/null || echo \\\"NOT_INSTALLED\\\"\\njq --version 2>/dev/null || echo \\\"NOT_INSTALLED\\\"\\n```\\n\\nReport each tool as installed, not installed, or not authenticated.\\n\\n- `codex`: if missing, fix with `npm install -g @openai/codex`. If installed but a Codex command reports an auth failure, fix with `codex login`.\\n- `darkfactory-dispatch`: if missing, fix with `cd ~/.darkfactory/tools/darkfactory-dispatch && make install`.\\n- `gh`: if `gh --version` is missing, fix with `brew install gh`. If `gh auth status` fails while `gh` is installed, fix with `gh auth login`.\\n- `openspec`: if missing, fix with `npm install -g @fission-ai/openspec`.\\n- `jq`: if missing, fix with `brew install jq`.\\n\\n## Step 4: Coverage Tool Detection\\n\\nDetect the project language from build files at the project root:\\n\\n- `Cargo.toml` means Rust.\\n- `package.json` means TypeScript/Node.\\n- `pyproject.toml` or `requirements.txt` means Python.\\n\\nCheck the matching coverage tool.\\n\\nFor Rust:\\n\\n```bash\\ncargo tarpaulin --version 2>/dev/null || echo \\\"NOT_INSTALLED\\\"\\n```\\n\\nIf missing, suggest:\\n\\n```bash\\ncargo install cargo-tarpaulin\\n```\\n\\nFor TypeScript/Node, check `package.json` for `c8`, `jest`, or `istanbul` in `dependencies` or `devDependencies`. Use an exit-0 pattern:\\n\\n```bash\\nnode -e 'const p=require(\\\"./package.json\\\"); const d={...(p.dependencies||{}), ...(p.devDependencies||{})}; console.log([\\\"c8\\\",\\\"jest\\\",\\\"istanbul\\\"].some((k)=>d[k]) ? \\\"FOUND\\\" : \\\"NOT_INSTALLED\\\")' 2>/dev/null || echo \\\"NOT_INSTALLED\\\"\\n```\\n\\nIf missing, suggest:\\n\\n```bash\\nnpm install -D c8\\n```\\n\\nFor Python:\\n\\n```bash\\npip show pytest-cov 2>/dev/null || echo \\\"NOT_INSTALLED\\\"\\n```\\n\\nIf missing, suggest:\\n\\n```bash\\npip install pytest-cov\\n```\\n\\nIf no recognized build file exists, report:\\n\\n```text\\nNo recognized language detected - coverage tool check skipped.\\n```\\n\\n## Step 5: Report Status\\n\\nPrint a structured report:\\n\\n```text\\nDarkfactory Setup Report\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"tool_end\",\"dispatch_id\":\"01KQR4JYYSZS01CS01QFAKE5E0\",\"ts\":\"2026-05-04T00:01:05Z\",\"tool\":\"command_execution\"}\n+{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_12\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '180,320p' skills/mission-init/SKILL.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"command_run\",\"dispatch_id\":\"01KQR4JYYSZS01CS01QFAKE5E0\",\"ts\":\"2026-05-04T00:01:07Z\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '180,320p' skills/mission-init/SKILL.md\\\"\"}\n+{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_12\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '180,320p' skills/mission-init/SKILL.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"Darkfactory Setup Report\\n========================\\n\\nSkills (via ~/.claude/skills/ symlinks):\\n  [x] /mission\\n  [x] /mission-resume\\n  [x] /mission-status\\n  [x] /mission-init\\n  [x] /grill\\n  [x] /prd\\n  [x] /language\\n  [x] /tdd\\n  [x] /test-quality\\n  [x] /security\\n  [x] /adversarial\\n  [x] /dispatch\\n\\nOptional standalone skills:\\n  [ ] /arch-review (optional - standalone)\\n  [ ] /domain-model (optional - standalone)\\n  [ ] /module-design (optional - standalone)\\n  [ ] /qa (optional - standalone)\\n  [ ] /write-a-skill (optional - standalone)\\n\\nOptional project skills:\\n  [ ] /test-app (optional - project-specific)\\n  [ ] /demo-video (optional - project-specific)\\n\\nCLI tools:\\n  [x] codex (authenticated)\\n  [x] darkfactory-dispatch\\n  [x] gh (authenticated)\\n  [x] openspec\\n  [x] jq\\n\\nCoverage:\\n  [x] cargo-tarpaulin (Rust detected)\\n\\nOpenSpec:\\n  [x] Initialized\\n\\nReady: run /mission to start.\\n```\\n\\nAlso check optional standalone skills at these locations:\\n\\n- `$HOME/.claude/skills/arch-review`\\n- `$HOME/.claude/skills/domain-model`\\n- `$HOME/.claude/skills/module-design`\\n- `$HOME/.claude/skills/qa`\\n- `$HOME/.claude/skills/write-a-skill`\\n\\nAnd optional project skills at these locations:\\n\\n- `$HOME/.claude/skills/test-app`\\n- `$HOME/.claude/skills/demo-video`\\n- `.claude/skills/test-app`\\n- `.claude/skills/demo-video`\\n\\nOptional skills never block readiness.\\n\\nIf any required skill or tool is missing, list the needed fix commands at the bottom under:\\n\\n```text\\nFix commands:\\n```\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"tool_end\",\"dispatch_id\":\"01KQR4JYYSZS01CS01QFAKE5E0\",\"ts\":\"2026-05-04T00:01:07Z\",\"tool\":\"command_execution\"}\n+{\"type\":\"heartbeat\",\"dispatch_id\":\"01KQR4JYYSZS01CS01QFAKE5E0\",\"ts\":\"2026-05-04T00:01:10Z\",\"elapsed_s\":30,\"last_activity\":\"tool ended: command_execution\",\"interval_s\":15}\n+{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_13\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"I found the insertion points. Next I’m patching the templates and mission docs in place, keeping the wording close to the requested contract so downstream smoke tests can match it.\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"heartbeat\",\"dispatch_id\":\"01KQR4JYYSZS01CS01QFAKE5E0\",\"ts\":\"2026-05-04T00:01:25Z\",\"elapsed_s\":45,\"last_activity\":\"agent response\",\"interval_s\":15}\n+{\"type\":\"heartbeat\",\"dispatch_id\":\"01KQR4JYYSZS01CS01QFAKE5E0\",\"ts\":\"2026-05-04T00:01:40Z\",\"elapsed_s\":60,\"last_activity\":\"agent response\",\"interval_s\":15}\n+{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_14\",\"type\":\"file_change\",\"changes\":[{\"path\":\"/Users/stuart/.darkfactory/skills/mission-init/SKILL.md\",\"kind\":\"update\"},{\"path\":\"/Users/stuart/.darkfactory/skills/mission/SKILL.md\",\"kind\":\"update\"},{\"path\":\"/Users/stuart/.darkfactory/skills/mission/templates/design-template.md\",\"kind\":\"update\"},{\"path\":\"/Users/stuart/.darkfactory/skills/mission/templates/worker-brief.md\",\"kind\":\"update\"}],\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"tool_start\",\"dispatch_id\":\"01KQR4JYYSZS01CS01QFAKE5E0\",\"ts\":\"2026-05-04T00:01:51Z\",\"tool\":\"file_change\"}\n+{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_14\",\"type\":\"file_change\",\"changes\":[{\"path\":\"/Users/stuart/.darkfactory/skills/mission-init/SKILL.md\",\"kind\":\"update\"},{\"path\":\"/Users/stuart/.darkfactory/skills/mission/SKILL.md\",\"kind\":\"update\"},{\"path\":\"/Users/stuart/.darkfactory/skills/mission/templates/design-template.md\",\"kind\":\"update\"},{\"path\":\"/Users/stuart/.darkfactory/skills/mission/templates/worker-brief.md\",\"kind\":\"update\"}],\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"heartbeat\",\"dispatch_id\":\"01KQR4JYYSZS01CS01QFAKE5E0\",\"ts\":\"2026-05-04T00:01:55Z\",\"elapsed_s\":75,\"last_activity\":\"tool started: file_change\",\"interval_s\":15}\n+{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_15\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"The main patch is in. I’m checking the exact rendered sections now, including the new topology fields and the config default.\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_16\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '45,75p' skills/mission/templates/worker-brief.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"command_run\",\"dispatch_id\":\"01KQR4JYYSZS01CS01QFAKE5E0\",\"ts\":\"2026-05-04T00:02:02Z\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '45,75p' skills/mission/templates/worker-brief.md\\\"\"}\n+{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_17\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '55,85p' skills/mission/templates/design-template.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"command_run\",\"dispatch_id\":\"01KQR4JYYSZS01CS01QFAKE5E0\",\"ts\":\"2026-05-04T00:02:02Z\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '55,85p' skills/mission/templates/design-template.md\\\"\"}\n+{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_16\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '45,75p' skills/mission/templates/worker-brief.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"- Exports: requireAuth (Express middleware, attaches req.user: User)\\n- Endpoints: POST /api/auth/login (body: {email, password}) → 200 {token: string}\\n>\\n\\n## Downstream Consumers\\n<Which later tasks in tasks.md will call this code? For each, name one minimum integration test that proves the call path works. Leave empty if no later task consumes this one.>\\n\\n## Procedures\\n- Use `<Skill from task topology>` to implement this task\\n  - If Skill: /frontend -- \\\"Use `/frontend` to implement this task\\\"\\n  - If Skill: /tdd -- \\\"Use `/tdd` to implement this task\\\"\\n- <For each Constraint in task topology, append:>\\n  - \\\"Also follow `/ui-system` for component selection and token discipline\\\"\\n  - \\\"Also follow `/react-perf` for performance optimization patterns\\\"\\n- Commit all changes (code + tests) in a single commit with message: \\\"[task-N] <description>\\\"\\n- Write your handoff report to openspec/changes/<change-name>/mission/handoffs/task-N.md\\n\\n## Handoff Report Format\\n- Task: Task N - <name>\\n- Commit SHA: <the full SHA>\\n- Approach: <brief explanation of what you did and why>\\n- Commands run: <any commands and their exit codes>\\n- Concerns: <anything you're uncertain about>\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"tool_end\",\"dispatch_id\":\"01KQR4JYYSZS01CS01QFAKE5E0\",\"ts\":\"2026-05-04T00:02:02Z\",\"tool\":\"command_execution\"}\n+{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_17\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '55,85p' skills/mission/templates/design-template.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\\n## Module Inventory\\n\\nList each planned module or major component. Use this table format:\\n\\n| Module name | Interface width | What it hides | Why this boundary |\\n|-------------|-----------------|---------------|-------------------|\\n| `<module>` | Narrow / moderate / broad, with the public entry points named | Implementation details callers do not need to know | Reason this responsibility belongs behind this boundary |\\n\\n### Frontend Module Guidance\\n\\nFor React frontend modules, describe:\\n- **Prop interface:** how many semantic concepts the caller must understand (count props + context + URL params + cache dependencies, not raw prop count)\\n- **State/effects encapsulated:** what state management and effects the component hides behind its interface\\n- **Classification:** deep component (owns a workflow end-to-end) or allowed-shallow exception (design system leaf, route/layout glue, adapter, headless behavior primitive) with the reason for the classification\\n\\nReference `/frontend` skill's DEEP-COMPONENTS.md for the four deep-component rules and allowed-shallow categories.\\n\\n## Type Catalog\\n\\nList domain types only. Type names must come from `UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md` when the term exists there. Do not include field-level detail.\\nDomain types model the problem space; exclude technical helpers such as CLI parsers, test fixtures, and generic containers unless they are public compatibility surfaces.\\n\\n| Type name | Purpose | Owning module |\\n|-----------|---------|---------------|\\n| `<type>` | One-line purpose | `<module>` |\\n\\n## Error Strategy\\n\\nDefine:\\n- Error type hierarchy\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"tool_end\",\"dispatch_id\":\"01KQR4JYYSZS01CS01QFAKE5E0\",\"ts\":\"2026-05-04T00:02:02Z\",\"tool\":\"command_execution\"}\n+{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_18\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '202,275p' skills/mission/SKILL.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"command_run\",\"dispatch_id\":\"01KQR4JYYSZS01CS01QFAKE5E0\",\"ts\":\"2026-05-04T00:02:02Z\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '202,275p' skills/mission/SKILL.md\\\"\"}\n+{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_19\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '437,458p' skills/mission/SKILL.md && sed -n '510,540p' skills/mission/SKILL.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"command_run\",\"dispatch_id\":\"01KQR4JYYSZS01CS01QFAKE5E0\",\"ts\":\"2026-05-04T00:02:02Z\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '437,458p' skills/mission/SKILL.md && sed -n '510,540p' skills/mission/SKILL.md\\\"\"}\n+{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_18\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '202,275p' skills/mission/SKILL.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"### Phase 4.3a: Task Strategy Approval\\n\\nBefore generating tasks.md, present a task decomposition strategy for human approval:\\n\\n1. **Decomposition approach:** layered (types and domain logic first, then transport/CLI), vertical (each task cuts end-to-end through all layers), or hybrid (foundation layer first, then vertical slices). State which and why.\\n2. **Target task count range:** e.g., \\\"6-8 feature tasks + 4-5 closing tasks.\\\" Justify the range based on the module inventory from design.md.\\n3. **Dependency ordering rationale:** which tasks must come first and why (e.g., \\\"Task 1 defines core types that all subsequent tasks import\\\").\\n\\n#### Frontend Task Decomposition (TypeScript React projects only)\\n\\nFor TypeScript React projects, use the specific task layer vocabulary:\\n\\n| Layer | Skill | Rationale |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `frontend/component` | `/frontend` | Visual React component work |\\n| `frontend/page` | `/frontend` | Page composition |\\n| `frontend/layout` | `/frontend` | Visual structure |\\n| `frontend/hooks` | `/tdd` | Hooks have testable interfaces |\\n| `backend` | `/tdd` | APIs, server logic |\\n| `shared/types` | `/tdd` | Type contracts |\\n| `shared/schema` | `/tdd` | Zod validation, pure logic |\\n| `shared/utils` | `/tdd` | Pure utility functions |\\n\\n**Mechanical rule:** `/frontend` only when the layer starts with `frontend/` AND is not `frontend/hooks`. Everything else gets `/tdd`.\\n\\nAuto-set `browser_tools: true` in config.yaml when any task has `Skill: /frontend`.\\n\\nWhen a frontend feature contains complex logic (validation, state machines, data transformation), split it: one `/tdd` task for the logic as a hook/utility, one `/frontend` task for the component that consumes it. The `/tdd` task comes first in the task list.\\n\\nThe human approves this strategy before tasks.md is generated. If rejected, revise and re-present.\\n\\nAfter approval, populate the task decomposition strategy anchor in the plan's Deterministic Anchors section.\\n\\nIf approved, proceed to Phase 4.4.\\n\\n### Phase 4.4: Generate and Review Tasks\\n\\nGenerate `tasks.md` (ordered checklist of implementation tasks).\\n\\n#### Task Quality Standard\\n\\nEach task must produce a concrete, testable output. When the approved strategy (Phase 4.3a) is vertical, tasks cross all layers. When the strategy is layered or hybrid, tasks may be scoped to a single layer, provided each task still has a clear done state and a test surface.\\n\\n**One task = one worker = one commit = one validation cycle.**\\n\\nA task is good if you can demo it and verify it independently after it lands.\\n\\n#### Task Topology\\n\\nEach task in tasks.md must include topology metadata in this fixed format:\\n\\n```markdown\\n- [ ] Task N: <name>\\n  Depends on: <prior task numbers, or \\\"none\\\">\\n  Consumes: <surfaces from prior tasks -- types, interfaces, endpoints>\\n  Produces: <surfaces this task creates -- types, modules, interfaces, endpoints>\\n  Layers: <logical architectural layers touched, e.g. domain, transport, storage>\\n```\\n\\n#### Skill and Constraint Validation (TypeScript React projects only)\\n\\nTask topology for TypeScript React projects includes two additional fields:\\n\\n```markdown\\nSkill: </tdd or /frontend>\\nConstraints: </ui-system, /react-perf, or \\\"none\\\">\\n```\\n\\nValidation rules:\\n- Exactly one `Skill:` value per task -- either `/tdd` or `/frontend`\\n- Zero or more `Constraints:` values\\n- `/ui-system` and `/react-perf` are only valid with `Skill: /frontend`\\n- Flag invalid combinations during Phase 4.4 human review\\n\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"tool_end\",\"dispatch_id\":\"01KQR4JYYSZS01CS01QFAKE5E0\",\"ts\":\"2026-05-04T00:02:02Z\",\"tool\":\"command_execution\"}\n+{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_19\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '437,458p' skills/mission/SKILL.md && sed -n '510,540p' skills/mission/SKILL.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"- Do not re-review the entire contract\\n\\nLog the testability breakdown to progress.md: `<timestamp> -- Contract testability pre-flight: <N> execution, <M> output, <P> inspection (<Q>% inspection).`\\n\\nUpdate the plan with the contract path after approval.\\n\\n**Gate -- proceed when:**\\n- [ ] contract.md human-approved\\n- [ ] Testability pre-flight passed (inspection checks <=20%)\\n- [ ] Testability breakdown logged to progress.md\\n- [ ] Plan updated with contract path\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Phase 6: Create Mission Directory\\n\\n> **Rules:** 5\\n> **Goal:** Create the mission directory with config and progress tracking files.\\n> **Inputs:** Change name (from plan), engine preferences (from plan's Engine Config section, or defaults below)\\n> **Outputs:** mission/ directory with config.yaml, progress.md, and subdirectories\\n\\nRead the engine preferences from the plan's Engine Config section. If not set by the human, use the defaults shown below.\\n- [ ] briefs/, handoffs/, validations/, issues/, logs/ subdirectories created\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Phase 7: Launch Confirmation\\n\\n> **Rules:** 5\\n> **Goal:** Get human confirmation before starting the build.\\n> **Inputs:** tasks.md, contract.md, coverage-audit.md, config.yaml\\n> **Outputs:** Human approval, progress.md updated, plan status = BUILDING\\n\\nEnsure a feature branch. If `git rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD` equals `gh api repos/{owner}/{repo} --jq .default_branch` (abort Phase 7 if that gh call fails -- it means no GitHub remote or bad auth), run `git checkout -b mission/<change-name>` -- if that branch already exists, use `mission/<change-name>-$(date -u +%Y%m%d%H%M%S)`. Log the checkout to progress.md.\\n\\nShow the user a summary dashboard:\\n1. **Mission overview** -- change name, total tasks (feature + closing), total contract checks\\n2. **Coverage audit result** -- number of PRD requirements covered, any deferred/skipped items\\n3. **Engine config** -- which engine runs each role (from config.yaml)\\n\\nAsk: \\\"Everything has been reviewed. Ready to start the build?\\\"\\n\\n- If yes: append `<timestamp> -- Plan approved. <N> tasks, <M> checks in contract.` to progress.md. Update plan status to BUILDING. Post a comment on the PRD issue: `gh issue comment <number> --body \\\"Mission dispatched. <N> tasks, <M> checks. Draft PR will link back on completion.\\\"` Proceed to Phase 8.\\n- If the human wants to revisit something: loop back to the specific phase they name. Do not re-review everything.\\n\\n**Gate -- proceed when:**\\n- [ ] Human confirms \\\"ready to start the build\\\"\\n- [ ] progress.md updated with approval timestamp and task/check counts\\n- [ ] Plan status = BUILDING\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Phase 8: Build Loop\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"tool_end\",\"dispatch_id\":\"01KQR4JYYSZS01CS01QFAKE5E0\",\"ts\":\"2026-05-04T00:02:02Z\",\"tool\":\"command_execution\"}\n+{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_20\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '100,170p' skills/mission-init/SKILL.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"command_run\",\"dispatch_id\":\"01KQR4JYYSZS01CS01QFAKE5E0\",\"ts\":\"2026-05-04T00:02:02Z\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '100,170p' skills/mission-init/SKILL.md\\\"\"}\n+{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_20\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '100,170p' skills/mission-init/SKILL.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"After a first-time init, tell the user to restart Claude Code so `/opsx:` commands can register.\\n\\n## Step 3: Verify CLI Dependencies\\n\\nRun these checks. Each command must always exit 0 so parallel Bash calls do not cancel each other:\\n\\n```bash\\ncodex --version 2>/dev/null || echo \\\"NOT_INSTALLED\\\"\\ndarkfactory-dispatch --version 2>/dev/null || echo \\\"NOT_INSTALLED\\\"\\ngh --version 2>/dev/null || echo \\\"NOT_INSTALLED\\\"\\ngh auth status 2>/dev/null || echo \\\"NOT_INSTALLED\\\"\\nopenspec --version 2>/dev/null || echo \\\"NOT_INSTALLED\\\"\\njq --version 2>/dev/null || echo \\\"NOT_INSTALLED\\\"\\n```\\n\\nReport each tool as installed, not installed, or not authenticated.\\n\\n- `codex`: if missing, fix with `npm install -g @openai/codex`. If installed but a Codex command reports an auth failure, fix with `codex login`.\\n- `darkfactory-dispatch`: if missing, fix with `cd ~/.darkfactory/tools/darkfactory-dispatch && make install`.\\n- `gh`: if `gh --version` is missing, fix with `brew install gh`. If `gh auth status` fails while `gh` is installed, fix with `gh auth login`.\\n- `openspec`: if missing, fix with `npm install -g @fission-ai/openspec`.\\n- `jq`: if missing, fix with `brew install jq`.\\n\\n## Step 4: Browser Tools Check (conditional)\\n\\nIf `browser_tools: true` in the mission's config.yaml (or if any task in the current mission has `Skill: /frontend`), check that chrome-devtools-mcp is registered:\\n\\n```bash\\n# Check if chrome-devtools MCP tools are available.\\n# The exact check depends on the MCP registration mechanism.\\n```\\n\\nIf chrome-devtools-mcp is not registered:\\n- Report: `[!] chrome-devtools-mcp - not registered (required when browser_tools: true)`\\n- Fix: Install chrome-devtools-mcp from https://github.com/nichochar/chrome-devtools-mcp and add it to MCP configuration\\n- This blocks mission launch for missions with `/frontend` tasks\\n\\nIf `browser_tools: false` or no `/frontend` tasks exist, skip this check.\\n\\n## Step 5: Coverage Tool Detection\\n\\nDetect the project language from build files at the project root:\\n\\n- `Cargo.toml` means Rust.\\n- `package.json` means TypeScript/Node.\\n- `pyproject.toml` or `requirements.txt` means Python.\\n\\nCheck the matching coverage tool.\\n\\nFor Rust:\\n\\n```bash\\ncargo tarpaulin --version 2>/dev/null || echo \\\"NOT_INSTALLED\\\"\\n```\\n\\nIf missing, suggest:\\n\\n```bash\\ncargo install cargo-tarpaulin\\n```\\n\\nFor TypeScript/Node, check `package.json` for `c8`, `jest`, or `istanbul` in `dependencies` or `devDependencies`. Use an exit-0 pattern:\\n\\n```bash\\nnode -e 'const p=require(\\\"./package.json\\\"); const d={...(p.dependencies||{}), ...(p.devDependencies||{})}; console.log([\\\"c8\\\",\\\"jest\\\",\\\"istanbul\\\"].some((k)=>d[k]) ? \\\"FOUND\\\" : \\\"NOT_INSTALLED\\\")' 2>/dev/null || echo \\\"NOT_INSTALLED\\\"\\n```\\n\\nIf missing, suggest:\\n\\n```bash\\nnpm install -D c8\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"tool_end\",\"dispatch_id\":\"01KQR4JYYSZS01CS01QFAKE5E0\",\"ts\":\"2026-05-04T00:02:02Z\",\"tool\":\"command_execution\"}\n+{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_21\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'rg -n -C 3 \\\"Browser tools:|chrome-devtools-mcp\\\" skills/mission-init/SKILL.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"command_run\",\"dispatch_id\":\"01KQR4JYYSZS01CS01QFAKE5E0\",\"ts\":\"2026-05-04T00:02:07Z\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'rg -n -C 3 \\\"Browser tools:|chrome-devtools-mcp\\\" skills/mission-init/SKILL.md'\"}\n+{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_22\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'rg -n -C 8 \\\"browser_tools: false|Browser Tools Override|Browser Tools Pre-flight\\\" skills/mission/SKILL.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"command_run\",\"dispatch_id\":\"01KQR4JYYSZS01CS01QFAKE5E0\",\"ts\":\"2026-05-04T00:02:07Z\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'rg -n -C 8 \\\"browser_tools: false|Browser Tools Override|Browser Tools Pre-flight\\\" skills/mission/SKILL.md'\"}\n+{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_21\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'rg -n -C 3 \\\"Browser tools:|chrome-devtools-mcp\\\" skills/mission-init/SKILL.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"122-\\n123-## Step 4: Browser Tools Check (conditional)\\n124-\\n125:If `browser_tools: true` in the mission's config.yaml (or if any task in the current mission has `Skill: /frontend`), check that chrome-devtools-mcp i [... omitted end of long line]\\n126-\\n127-```bash\\n128-# Check if chrome-devtools MCP tools are available.\\n129-# The exact check depends on the MCP registration mechanism.\\n130-```\\n131-\\n132:If chrome-devtools-mcp is not registered:\\n133:- Report: `[!] chrome-devtools-mcp - not registered (required when browser_tools: true)`\\n134:- Fix: Install chrome-devtools-mcp from https://github.com/nichochar/chrome-devtools-mcp and add it to MCP configuration\\n135-- This blocks mission launch for missions with `/frontend` tasks\\n136-\\n137-If `browser_tools: false` or no `/frontend` tasks exist, skip this check.\\n--\\n228-  [x] openspec\\n229-  [x] jq\\n230-\\n231:Browser tools:\\n232:  [-] chrome-devtools-mcp (skipped - browser_tools: false and no /frontend tasks)\\n233-\\n234-Coverage:\\n235-  [x] cargo-tarpaulin (Rust detected)\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"tool_end\",\"dispatch_id\":\"01KQR4JYYSZS01CS01QFAKE5E0\",\"ts\":\"2026-05-04T00:02:07Z\",\"tool\":\"command_execution\"}\n+{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_22\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'rg -n -C 8 \\\"browser_tools: false|Browser Tools Override|Browser Tools Pre-flight\\\" skills/mission/SKILL.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"477-  worker: codex\\n478-  scrutiny_validator: claude\\n479-  usertest_validator: claude\\n480-  adversarial_reviewer_a: codex\\n481-  adversarial_reviewer_b: claude\\n482-  demo_video: claude\\n483-\\n484-# Auto-set to true during Phase 4.3a when any task has Skill: /frontend.\\n485:browser_tools: false\\n486-```\\n487-\\n488-### progress.md\\n489-\\n490-```markdown\\n491-# Mission: <change-name>\\n492-\\n493-Started: <ISO 8601 timestamp>\\n--\\n551-Write a brief to `mission/briefs/task-N.md`.\\n552-\\n553-#### Brief Template\\n554-\\n555-Read [templates/worker-brief.md](templates/worker-brief.md).\\n556-\\n557-**The brief NEVER contains contract.md content.** \\n558-\\n559:#### Browser Tools Override\\n560-\\n561:If `browser_tools: false` in config.yaml (human override), omit visual verification procedures from the worker brief even for `/frontend` tasks. The w [... omitted end of long line]\\n562-\\n563-### Step 2: Dispatch Worker\\n564-\\n565-Read the engine from `mission/config.yaml`.\\n566-\\n567:#### Browser Tools Pre-flight (Skill: /frontend tasks only)\\n568-\\n569-Before dispatching a `/frontend` task, check that chrome-devtools-mcp is available:\\n570-- If available: proceed with dispatch, include visual verification in the brief\\n571-- If unavailable: block dispatch. Log to progress.md: `<timestamp> -- Task N: chrome-devtools-mcp unavailable at dispatch. Pausing.` Surface to human  [... omitted end of long line]\\n572-\\n573-#### If engine is `codex`:\\n574-\\n575-Before dispatching, run `git rev-parse HEAD` and store the result as `PRE_TASK_SHA`. This value is used in Step 7 to generate the codebase delta — sto [... omitted end of long line]\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"tool_end\",\"dispatch_id\":\"01KQR4JYYSZS01CS01QFAKE5E0\",\"ts\":\"2026-05-04T00:02:07Z\",\"tool\":\"command_execution\"}\n+{\"type\":\"heartbeat\",\"dispatch_id\":\"01KQR4JYYSZS01CS01QFAKE5E0\",\"ts\":\"2026-05-04T00:02:10Z\",\"elapsed_s\":90,\"last_activity\":\"tool ended: command_execution\",\"interval_s\":15}\n+{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_23\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'rg -n \\\"Use `<Skill from task topology>`|Frontend Module Guidance|Frontend Task Decomposition|Skill and Constraint Validation|browser_tools: false|Browser Tools Override|Browser Tools Pre-flight|Browser Tools Check\\\" skills/mission/templates/worker-brief.md skills/mission/templates/design-template.md skills/mission/SKILL.md skills/mission-init/SKILL.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"command_run\",\"dispatch_id\":\"01KQR4JYYSZS01CS01QFAKE5E0\",\"ts\":\"2026-05-04T00:02:18Z\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'rg -n \\\"Use `<Skill from task topology>`|Frontend Module Guidance|Frontend Task Decomposition|Skill and Constraint Validation|browser_tools: false|Browser Tools Override|Browser Tools Pre-flight|Browser Tools Check\\\" skills/mission/templates/worker-brief.md skills/mission/templates/design-template.md skills/mission/SKILL.md skills/mission-init/SKILL.md'\"}\n+{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_23\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'rg -n \\\"Use `<Skill from task topology>`|Frontend Module Guidance|Frontend Task Decomposition|Skill and Constraint Validation|browser_tools: false|Browser Tools Override|Browser Tools Pre-flight|Browser Tools Check\\\" skills/mission/templates/worker-brief.md skills/mission/templates/design-template.md skills/mission/SKILL.md skills/mission-init/SKILL.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"zsh:1: parse error near `>'\\nzsh:1: parse error in command substitution\\n\",\"exit_code\":1,\"status\":\"failed\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"tool_end\",\"dispatch_id\":\"01KQR4JYYSZS01CS01QFAKE5E0\",\"ts\":\"2026-05-04T00:02:18Z\",\"tool\":\"command_execution\"}\n+{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_24\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'git diff -- skills/mission/templates/worker-brief.md skills/mission/templates/design-template.md skills/mission/SKILL.md skills/mission-init/SKILL.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"command_run\",\"dispatch_id\":\"01KQR4JYYSZS01CS01QFAKE5E0\",\"ts\":\"2026-05-04T00:02:18Z\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'git diff -- skills/mission/templates/worker-brief.md skills/mission/templates/design-template.md skills/mission/SKILL.md skills/mission-init/SKILL.md'\"}\n+{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_24\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'git diff -- skills/mission/templates/worker-brief.md skills/mission/templates/design-template.md skills/mission/SKILL.md skills/mission-init/SKILL.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"diff --git a/skills/mission-init/SKILL.md b/skills/mission-init/SKILL.md\\nindex d057fc4..ab6ace3 100644\\n--- a/skills/mission-init/SKILL.md\\n+++ b/skills/mission-init/SKILL.md\\n@@ -120,7 +120,23 @@ Report each tool as installed, not installed, or not authenticated.\\n - `openspec`: if missing, fix with `npm install -g @fission-ai/openspec`.\\n - `jq`: if missing, fix with `brew install jq`.\\n \\n-## Step 4: Coverage Tool Detection\\n+## Step 4: Browser Tools Check (conditional)\\n+\\n+If `browser_tools: true` in the mission's config.yaml (or if any task in the current mission has `Skill: /frontend`), check that chrome-devtools-mcp is registered:\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+# Check if chrome-devtools MCP tools are available.\\n+# The exact check depends on the MCP registration mechanism.\\n+```\\n+\\n+If chrome-devtools-mcp is not registered:\\n+- Report: `[!] chrome-devtools-mcp - not registered (required when browser_tools: true)`\\n+- Fix: Install chrome-devtools-mcp from https://github.com/nichochar/chrome-devtools-mcp and add it to MCP configuration\\n+- This blocks mission launch for missions with `/frontend` tasks\\n+\\n+If `browser_tools: false` or no `/frontend` tasks exist, skip this check.\\n+\\n+## Step 5: Coverage Tool Detection\\n \\n Detect the project language from build files at the project root:\\n \\n@@ -172,7 +188,7 @@ If no recognized build file exists, report:\\n No recognized language detected - coverage tool check skipped.\\n ```\\n \\n-## Step 5: Report Status\\n+## Step 6: Report Status\\n \\n Print a structured report:\\n \\n@@ -212,6 +228,9 @@ CLI tools:\\n   [x] openspec\\n   [x] jq\\n \\n+Browser tools:\\n+  [-] chrome-devtools-mcp (skipped - browser_tools: false and no /frontend tasks)\\n+\\n Coverage:\\n   [x] cargo-tarpaulin (Rust detected)\\n \\ndiff --git a/skills/mission/SKILL.md b/skills/mission/SKILL.md\\nindex 179f5c1..80b7bbf 100644\\n--- a/skills/mission/SKILL.md\\n+++ b/skills/mission/SKILL.md\\n@@ -207,6 +207,27 @@ Before generating tasks.md, present a task decomposition strategy for human appr\\n 2. **Target task count range:** e.g., \\\"6-8 feature tasks + 4-5 closing tasks.\\\" Justify the range based on the module inventory from design.md.\\n 3. **Dependency ordering rationale:** which tasks must come first and why (e.g., \\\"Task 1 defines core types that all subsequent tasks import\\\").\\n \\n+#### Frontend Task Decomposition (TypeScript React projects only)\\n+\\n+For TypeScript React projects, use the specific task layer vocabulary:\\n+\\n+| Layer | Skill | Rationale |\\n+|---|---|---|\\n+| `frontend/component` | `/frontend` | Visual React component work |\\n+| `frontend/page` | `/frontend` | Page composition |\\n+| `frontend/layout` | `/frontend` | Visual structure |\\n+| `frontend/hooks` | `/tdd` | Hooks have testable interfaces |\\n+| `backend` | `/tdd` | APIs, server logic |\\n+| `shared/types` | `/tdd` | Type contracts |\\n+| `shared/schema` | `/tdd` | Zod validation, pure logic |\\n+| `shared/utils` | `/tdd` | Pure utility functions |\\n+\\n+**Mechanical rule:** `/frontend` only when the layer starts with `frontend/` AND is not `frontend/hooks`. Everything else gets `/tdd`.\\n+\\n+Auto-set `browser_tools: true` in config.yaml when any task has `Skill: /frontend`.\\n+\\n+When a frontend feature contains complex logic (validation, state machines, data transformation), split it: one `/tdd` task for the logic as a hook/utility, one `/frontend` task for the component that consumes it. The `/tdd` task comes first in the task list.\\n+\\n The human approves this strategy before tasks.md is generated. If rejected, revise and re-present.\\n \\n After approval, populate the task decomposition strategy anchor in the plan's Deterministic Anchors section.\\n@@ -237,6 +258,21 @@ Each task in tasks.md must include topology metadata in this fixed format:\\n   Layers: <logical architectural layers touched, e.g. domain, transport, storage>\\n ```\\n \\n+#### Skill and Constraint Validation (TypeScript React projects only)\\n+\\n+Task topology for TypeScript React projects includes two additional fields:\\n+\\n+```markdown\\n+Skill: </tdd or /frontend>\\n+Constraints: </ui-system, /react-perf, or \\\"none\\\">\\n+```\\n+\\n+Validation rules:\\n+- Exactly one `Skill:` value per task -- either `/tdd` or `/frontend`\\n+- Zero or more `Constraints:` values\\n+- `/ui-system` and `/react-perf` are only valid with `Skill: /frontend`\\n+- Flag invalid combinations during Phase 4.4 human review\\n+\\n Layers are logical groupings of modules (domain, transport, storage, configuration, etc.) defined in the design narrative, not columns from the Module Inventory table.\\n \\n When the approved strategy (Phase 4.3a) is layered or hybrid and a task's Layers field lists more than 2 architectural layers, flag the task for human review with a recommendation to split or approve as-is. When the approved strategy is vertical, the layer count flag does not apply since vertical tasks are expected to cross all layers.\\n@@ -444,6 +480,9 @@ engines:\\n   adversarial_reviewer_a: codex\\n   adversarial_reviewer_b: claude\\n   demo_video: claude\\n+\\n+# Auto-set to true during Phase 4.3a when any task has Skill: /frontend.\\n+browser_tools: false\\n ```\\n \\n ### progress.md\\n@@ -517,10 +556,20 @@ Read [templates/worker-brief.md](templates/worker-brief.md).\\n \\n **The brief NEVER contains contract.md content.** \\n \\n+#### Browser Tools Override\\n+\\n+If `browser_tools: false` in config.yaml (human override), omit visual verification procedures from the worker brief even for `/frontend` tasks. The worker follows the `/frontend` workflow but skips the chrome-devtools-mcp visual verify step in the Build phase.\\n+\\n ### Step 2: Dispatch Worker\\n \\n Read the engine from `mission/config.yaml`.\\n \\n+#### Browser Tools Pre-flight (Skill: /frontend tasks only)\\n+\\n+Before dispatching a `/frontend` task, check that chrome-devtools-mcp is available:\\n+- If available: proceed with dispatch, include visual verification in the brief\\n+- If unavailable: block dispatch. Log to progress.md: `<timestamp> -- Task N: chrome-devtools-mcp unavailable at dispatch. Pausing.` Surface to human with options: retry (check again), skip visual verify for this task, or abort mission\\n+\\n #### If engine is `codex`:\\n \\n Before dispatching, run `git rev-parse HEAD` and store the result as `PRE_TASK_SHA`. This value is used in Step 7 to generate the codebase delta — store it somewhere you can reference after the background worker returns (e.g. in the plan file or a local variable).\\ndiff --git a/skills/mission/templates/design-template.md b/skills/mission/templates/design-template.md\\nindex b81bddd..3e8dbf3 100644\\n--- a/skills/mission/templates/design-template.md\\n+++ b/skills/mission/templates/design-template.md\\n@@ -61,6 +61,15 @@ List each planned module or major component. Use this table format:\\n |-------------|-----------------|---------------|-------------------|\\n | `<module>` | Narrow / moderate / broad, with the public entry points named | Implementation details callers do not need to know | Reason this responsibility belongs behind this boundary |\\n \\n+### Frontend Module Guidance\\n+\\n+For React frontend modules, describe:\\n+- **Prop interface:** how many semantic concepts the caller must understand (count props + context + URL params + cache dependencies, not raw prop count)\\n+- **State/effects encapsulated:** what state management and effects the component hides behind its interface\\n+- **Classification:** deep component (owns a workflow end-to-end) or allowed-shallow exception (design system leaf, route/layout glue, adapter, headless behavior primitive) with the reason for the classification\\n+\\n+Reference `/frontend` skill's DEEP-COMPONENTS.md for the four deep-component rules and allowed-shallow categories.\\n+\\n ## Type Catalog\\n \\n List domain types only. Type names must come from `UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md` when the term exists there. Do not include field-level detail.\\ndiff --git a/skills/mission/templates/worker-brief.md b/skills/mission/templates/worker-brief.md\\nindex b3c1211..2c1e19d 100644\\n--- a/skills/mission/templates/worker-brief.md\\n+++ b/skills/mission/templates/worker-brief.md\\n@@ -50,7 +50,12 @@ Example:\\n <Which later tasks in tasks.md will call this code? For each, name one minimum integration test that proves the call path works. Leave empty if no later task consumes this one.>\\n \\n ## Procedures\\n-- Use `/tdd` to implement this task\\n+- Use `<Skill from task topology>` to implement this task\\n+  - If Skill: /frontend -- \\\"Use `/frontend` to implement this task\\\"\\n+  - If Skill: /tdd -- \\\"Use `/tdd` to implement this task\\\"\\n+- <For each Constraint in task topology, append:>\\n+  - \\\"Also follow `/ui-system` for component selection and token discipline\\\"\\n+  - \\\"Also follow `/react-perf` for performance optimization patterns\\\"\\n - Commit all changes (code + tests) in a single commit with message: \\\"[task-N] <description>\\\"\\n - Write your handoff report to openspec/changes/<change-name>/mission/handoffs/task-N.md\\n \\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"tool_end\",\"dispatch_id\":\"01KQR4JYYSZS01CS01QFAKE5E0\",\"ts\":\"2026-05-04T00:02:18Z\",\"tool\":\"command_execution\"}\n+{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_25\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"The diff matches the requested shape. One veri