erride), omit visual verification...skips the chrome-devtools-mcp visual verify step` |\n+| 12 | mission-init/SKILL.md contains \"chrome-devtools\" or \"browser_tools\" (init availability check) | PASS | Line 125: `browser_tools: true` and `chrome-devtools-mcp is registered`; line 133: `chrome-devtools-mc| **Brief** | A self-contained markdown file the orchestrator writes for a worker, containing the task description, project context, and procedures | Prompt, instructions, spec |\\n    19\\t| **Handoff** | A structured report a worker writes to disk after completing a task, including the commit SHA, approach taken, and any concerns | Report, summary, output |\\n    20\\t| **Vertical slice** | The default task quality standard. Each task must produce a concrete, testable output. When the approved strategy is vertical, tasks cross all layers. When layered or hybrid, tasks may be scoped to a single layer with a clear done state and test surface. | Horizontal slice, layer |\\n    21\\t| **Deviation classification** | Categorization of spec deviations during the coverage audit as Interpretation (ambiguous spec, reasonable reading), Substitution (replacing specified approach with a different one), or Removal (not implementing a specified feature). Substitutions and removals require explicit human approval. | Deviation type, deviation level |\\n    22\\t| **Spec delta check** | A post-build verification step (Phase 9) where a Claude subagent checks that every item marked COVERED in the coverage audit is actually present in the built codebase. APPROVED-DEVIATION items are listed but not re-litigated. | Final spec check, compliance check, coverage verification |\\n    23\\t\\n    24\\t## Validation\\n    25\\t\\n    26\\t| Term | Definition | Aliases to avoid |\\n    27\\t| --- | --- | --- |\\n    28\\t| **Scrutiny validator** | The first validator type that runs build, test, lint, code review, code simplify, and test health checks against the contract | Code reviewer, linter, static validator |\\n    29\\t| **User-test validator** | The second validator type that tests behavior by hitting the API (HTTP tests) or driving a browser (agent-browser) | QA, E2E tester, integration tester |\\n    30\\t| **Behavioral conformance** | A scrutiny validator check (check 11) that verifies observable behavior by writing and executing a test script rather than reading the code. Falls back to \\\"verified by inspection\\\" if execution is inconclusive. | Behavioral test, execution test, runtime check |\\n    31\\t| **Final gates** | Whole-repo build, test, lint, and format checks run after the last task completes but before PR creation. Catches regressions introduced by later tasks (e.g., documentation or CI tasks) after the cleanup task ran. | Final checks, post-build gates, repo gates |\\n    32\\t| **Module shape re-check** | A mandatory closing task that compares design.md module descriptions and Type Catalog names to what the code actually exposes, catching cumulative drift across tasks that per-task scrutiny cannot see | Shape check, surface audit, drift check |\\n    33\\t| **Demo video** | A recording of frontend functionality captured after both validators pass, created for human review | Screencast, screen recording |\\n    34\\t| **Fix loop** | The cycle where a validation failure spawns a fix worker, then both validators re-run, up to 3 attempts before asking the human | Retry, repair cycle |\\n    35\\t| **Circuit breaker** | The rule that stops the fix loop after 3 failed attempts on the same task and asks the human for guidance | Retry limit, fail-safe |\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"tool_end\",\"dispatch_id\":\"01KQHY4S39BX9YXXDX9GXCFD3Q\",\"ts\":\"2026-05-01T14:14:47Z\",\"tool\":\"command_execution\"}\n+{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_51\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'git diff --cached --name-only'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status