+{\"type\":\"tool_end\",\"dispatch_id\":\"01KQHY4S39BX9YXXDX9GXCFD3Q\",\"ts\":\"2026-05-01T14:15:04Z\",\"tool\":\"command_execution\"}\n+{\"type\":\"heartbeat\",\"dispatch_id\":\"01KQHY4S39BX9YXXDX9GXCFD3Q\",\"ts\":\"2026-05-01T14:15:08Z\",\"elapsed_s\":150,\"last_activity\":\"tool ended: command_execution\",\"interval_s\":15}\n+{\"type\":\"heartbeat\",\"dispatch_id\":\"01KQHY4S39BX9YXXDX9GXCFD3Q\",\"ts\":\"2026-05-01T14:15:23Z\",\"elapsed_s\":165,\"last_activity\":\"tool ended: command_execution\",\"interval_s\":15}\n+{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_57\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba docs/reference_factory_talk.md | sed -n '1,35p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"command_run\",\"dispatch_id\":\"01KQHY4S39BX9YXXDX9GXCFD3Q\",\"ts\":\"2026-05-01T14:15:26Z\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba docs/reference_factory_talk.md | sed -n '1,35p'\\\"\"}\n+{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_58\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba docs/provenance.md | sed -n '1,30p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"command_run\",\"dispatch_id\":\"01KQHY4S39BX9YXXDX9GXCFD3Q\",\"ts\":\"2026-05-01T14:15:26Z\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba docs/provenance.md | sed -n '1,30p'\\\"\"}\n+{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_57\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba docs/reference_factory_talk.md | sed -n '1,35p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t---\\n     2\\tname: factory-missions-talk-reference\\n     3\\tdescription: Reference material from Factory's \\\"Assembling Agent Teams\\\" talk at AI Engineer Europe -- core architecture details for the Missions multi-agent system\\n     4\\ttype: reference\\n     5\\toriginSessionId: d0be7010-3858-4b92-8153-32045af7ab9b\\n     6\\t---\\n     7\\tSource: Talk by Factory's core agent harness lead at AI Engineer Europe (April 2026). Slide images in `/Users/stuart/Downloads/talkimages/` (13 JPEGs). Full transcript and summary provided by Stuart in the initial conversation.\\n     8\\t\\n     9\\t## Key Architecture Details\\n    10\\t\\n    11\\t**Five multi-agent strategies (taxonomy):**\\n    12\\t1. Delegation -- parent spawns sub-agents\\n    13\\t2. Creator-Verifier -- separate agents for building vs checking\\n    14\\t3. Direct Communication -- agents talk without coordinator (fragile)\\n    15\\t4. Negotiation -- agents coordinate over shared resources\\n    16\\t5. Broadcast -- one agent sends info to many\\n    17\\t\\n    18\\t**Missions combine 4 of 5** (delegation, creator-verifier, broadcast, negotiation) into a single workflow.\\n    19\\t\\n    20\\t**Three-role architecture:**\\n    21\\t- **Orchestrators** -- plan features/milestones, ask clarifying questions, produce a \\\"validation contract\\\" (defines done before coding starts, can be hundreds of checks)\\n    22\\t- **Workers** -- implement one feature at a time with clean context, commit to git, structured handoff report (what was done, what's undone, commands/exit codes, issues, procedure compliance)\\n    23\\t- **Validators** -- two types:\\n    24\\t  - *Scrutiny Validator* -- test suite, type checking, lint, dedicated code review agents per feature\\n    25\\t  - *User Testing Validator* -- QA engine that spawns the app, interacts via computer use, fills forms, clicks buttons, checks flows end-to-end\\n    26\\t\\n    27\\t**Execution model:**\\n    28\\t- Serial feature execution (one worker at a time) to avoid conflicts\\n    29\\t- Parallelization only for read-only ops (code search, API research) and within validators\\n    30\\t- Correctness compounds over multi-day runs\\n    31\\t\\n    32\\t**Model strategy:**\\n    33\\t- Model-agnostic: different LLMs for planning (slow reasoning), implementation (fast code fluency), validation (precise instruction following)\\n    34\\t- Structure compensates for non-frontier models\\n    35\\t- Almost all orchestration logic is in ~700 lines of prompts/skills, not hard-coded\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"tool_end\",\"dispatch_id\":\"01KQHY4S39BX9YXXDX9GXCFD3Q\",\"ts\":\"2026-05-01T14:15:26Z\",\"tool\":\"command_execution\"}\n+{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_58\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba docs/provenance.md | sed -n '1,30p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t# Provenance\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\tHow Darkfactory relates to its two original sources: Factory.ai's multi-agent mission\\n     4\\tarchitecture and Matt Pocock's AI development skills. Reviewed against the current\\n     5\\timplementation (SKILL.md) as of 2026-04-12.\\n     6\\t\\n     7\\t---\\n     8\\t\\n     9\\t## Factory.ai\\n    10\\t\\n    11\\tSource: [docs/reference_factory_talk.md](reference_factory_talk.md)\\n    12\\t\\n    13\\t### Faithfully implemented\\n    14\\t\\n    15\\t| Concept | Factory description | Darkfactory implementation |\\n    16\\t|---------|--------------------|----------------------------|\\n    17\\t| Three-role architecture | Orchestrator, worker, validator as distinct roles | Orchestrator is the /mission session. Workers are dispatched subagents. Validators are separate subagents with isolated prompts. |\\n    18\\t| Validation contract | \\\"Defines done before coding starts, can be hundreds of checks\\\" | contract.md (Phase 5), written after specs/tasks but before the build loop. Workers never see it. |\\n    19\\t| Adversarial separation | Workers don't see the contract, validators don't see the plan | Stricter than Factory: workers never see contract.md, validators never see proposal.md or design.md. |\\n    20\\t| Serial execution | One worker at a time to avoid conflicts | Rule 1: \\\"One worker at a time. Never dispatch two workers in parallel.\\\" |\\n    21\\t| Structured handoffs | Workers produce reports with what was done, commands, exit codes, issues | Handoff template: commit SHA, approach, commands run, concerns. |\\n    22\\t| Two validator types | Scrutiny validator (tests, lint, review) and user-testing validator (spawns app, interacts) | Scrutiny (Phase 8 Step 4): build/test/lint/review/standards/simplify/security/checks/behavioral conformance. User-test (Phase 8 Step 6): HTTP tests or browser. |\\n    23\\t| Multi-model strategy | Different LLMs for different roles | config.yaml: workers default to Codex (GPT-5.4), validators to Claude, adversarial reviewers use one of each. |\\n    24\\t| Read-only parallelization | Only parallelize read-only operations | Only parallel dispatch is the two adversarial reviewers in Phase 9, which are read-only. |\\n    25\\t\\n    26\\t### Implemented differently\\n    27\\t\\n    28\\t| Concept | Factory description | Darkfactory difference |\\n    29\\t|---------|--------------------|-----------------------|\\n    30\\t| User-test validator | \\\"Computer use\\\" QA engine that spawns the app and interacts | Uses HTTP tests and browser automation (/test-app). Same concept, less sophisticated execution. |\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"tool_end\",\"dispatch_id\":\"01KQHY4S39BX9YXXDX9GXCFD3Q\",\"ts\":\"2026-05-01T14:15:26Z\",\"tool\":\"command_execution\"}\n+{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_59\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"git show f0102913d3b0c67c0b96ffc6d2ce37dde4755a9c:docs/provenance.md | nl -ba | sed -n '1,30p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"command_run\",\"dispatch_id\":\"01KQHY4S39BX9YXXDX9GXCFD3Q\",\"ts\":\"2026-05-01T14:15:26Z\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"git show f0102913d3b0c67c0b96ffc6d2ce37dde4755a9c:docs/provenance.md | nl -ba | sed -n '1,30p'\\\"\"}\n+{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_60\",\"type\":\"comm