, present them to the human: each line is a SKIP'd assertion from an earlier [... omitted end of long line]\\n747:**If all gates pass:** Log to progress.md: `<timestamp> -- Final gates PASSED.` Proceed to the spec delta check.\\n755:### Spec Delta Check\\n761:Read the delta check report from `mission/validations/spec-delta.md`.\\n763:**If CLEAN (no discrepancies):** Log to progress.md: `<timestamp> -- Spec delta check CLEAN. <N> items verified, <M> approved deviations listed.` Proc [... omitted end of long line]\\n766:- **Add fix task** -- create a new task to implement the missing item. Write assertions for this task and append them to contract.md (present to human [... omitted end of long line]\\n899:- [ ] Spec delta check clean (no unresolved discrepancies)\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"tool_end\",\"dispatch_id\":\"01KQHVAYVC7X3WRCNBHQ6REC4Q\",\"ts\":\"2026-05-01T13:23:58Z\",\"tool\":\"command_execution\"}\n+{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_10\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"rg -n \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\b[Cc]heck(s|ed|ing)?\\\\\\\\b|check [0-9]|Check Sequence|Check Results|Code standards check\\\\\\\" skills/mission/prompts/scrutiny-validator.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"11:Before starting the check sequence, gather deterministic facts from the repository and the task diff. Store the results under the exact named facts be [... omitted end of long line]\\n98:This named fact is declared before the check sequence, then filled immediately after check 3 runs the project test command. Parse the captured test st [... omitted end of long line]\\n109:## Check Sequence\\n111:Run these checks in order. For each, report PASS or FAIL with evidence.\\n113:1. **Test presence gate:** Run `git show <commit-sha> --stat` and check if any test files were added or modified. If the diff contains zero test files [... omitted end of long line]\\n127:5. **Code review:** Run /review against the diff (this includes reading the full diff). Check specifically for:\\n144:   - Exclude standalone test files from the 900-line check: files in `tests/` directories, `*.test.ts`, `*.spec.ts`, `test_*.py`, and `*_test.py`.\\n161:7. **Code standards check:** Review the diff for these specific anti-patterns. Flag any found:\\n174:   - Belt-and-suspenders: redundant validation that duplicates what the framework, DB, or upstream already guarantees (re-checking auth after middlewa [... omitted end of long line]\\n176:   - Defensive handling of impossible states: catch blocks or null checks for conditions that cannot occur given current code paths.\\n185:    - CLI flag assertion: run the binary with the flag, check output\\n186:    - Exit code assertion: run the command, check `$?`\\n187:    - Shell alias assertion: source the alias, run `type <name>`, check the definition\\n188:    - API response assertion: curl the endpoint, check the response body\\n192:    If a behavioral test is inconclusive (e.g., the test script errors out, the environment lacks a dependency), mark it as \\\"verified by inspection (e [... omitted end of long line]\\n270:## Check Results\\n271:| Check | Result | Notes |\\n301:IMPORTANT: The overall result is FAIL if ANY check fails or ANY contract assertion fails. Be strict. A near-miss is still a FAIL.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"tool_end\",\"dispatch_id\":\"01KQHVAYVC7X3WRCNBHQ6REC4Q\",\"ts\":\"2026-05-01T13:23:58Z\",\"tool\":\"command_execution\"}\n+{\"type\":\"heartbeat\",\"dispatch_id\":\"01KQHVAYVC7X3WRCNBHQ6REC4Q\",\"ts\":\"2026-05-01T13:24:04Z\",\"elapsed_s\":30,\"last_activity\":\"tool ended: command_execution\",\"interval_s\":15}\n+{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_11\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"I’m going to patch only the validator prompt and the mission manual references that name the validator steps. I’m leaving ordinary verb uses of “check”, “re-check”, and contract assertion language al