  - Demo: SKIPPED\n+  - Fix attempts: 0 (PNG revert was orchestrator fix, not validation failure)\n+- 2026-05-01T00:50:00Z -- Task 4: worker completed. Commit: ff26bb1.\n+- 2026-05-01T00:52:00Z -- Task 4: scrutiny FAIL (check 5: awkward phrasings). Fixed in orchestrator commit.\n+- 2026-05-01T00:55:00Z -- Task 4: scrutiny validation PASSED (v2).\n+- 2026-05-01T00:56:00Z -- Task 4: user-test validation PASSED.\n+- 2026-05-01T00:56:00Z -- Task 4 complete.\n+  - Commit: orchestrator fix on top of ff26bb1\n+  - Scrutiny: PASS (v2)\n+  - User-test: PASS\n+  - Demo: SKIPPED\n+  - Fix attempts: 1\n+- 2026-05-01T00:30:00Z -- Task 2 complete.\n+  - Commit: 8d87791\n+  - Scrutiny: PASS\n+  - User-test: PASS (v2)\n+  - Demo: SKIPPED\n+  - Fix attempts: 0\n+- 2026-05-01T01:00:00Z -- Task 5: worker completed. No issues found. Commit: 593c063.\n+- 2026-05-01T01:02:00Z -- Task 5 complete.\n+  - Commit: 593c063\n+  - Scrutiny: PASS\n+  - User-test: PASS\n+  - Demo: SKIPPED\n+  - Fix attempts: 0\n+- 2026-05-01T01:05:00Z -- Task 6 complete. Module shape re-check: no drift. Commit: 06c1e27.\n+- 2026-05-01T01:06:00Z -- Task 7 complete. CLAUDE.md + ARCH.md already exist, not modified.\n+- 2026-05-01T01:08:00Z -- Task 8 complete. Documentation verified consistent. Commit: 3256b83.\n+- 2026-05-01T01:10:00Z -- All 8 tasks complete. Proceeding to Phase 9.\n+- 2026-05-01T01:12:00Z -- Final gates PASSED (markdown-only repo, no build/test/lint/format).\n+- 2026-05-01T01:14:00Z -- Spec delta check CLEAN. 13 items verified, 0 deviations.\n+- 2026-05-01T01:20:00Z -- Draft PR created: https://github.com/layercodedev/darkfactory/pull/140. Adversarial reviews complete.\ndiff --git a/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/mission/validations/adversarial-a.md b/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/mission/validations/adversarial-a.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..1c290f5\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/mission/validations/adversarial-a.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@\n+Wrote the adversarial report to [adversarial-a.md](/Users/stuart/.darkfactory/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/mission/validations/adversarial-a.md).\n+\n+Key findings:\n+- HIGH: `UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md` contains required glossary fixes only in the uncommitted worktree, while `HEAD` still has old assertion/check meanings.\n+- LOW: task-5 and task-6 handoffs point at rebased commits not contained in the current branch.\n+- LOW: source/provenance docs may have replaced source wording with project terminology.\n+\n+Checks run: commit-by-commit `git show --stat` and `git show`, final-state `rg` sweeps, `git diff`, `git show HEAD:UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md`, and report file verification.\n\\ No newline at end of file\ndiff --git a/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/mission/validations/adversarial-b.md b/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/mission/validations/adversarial-b.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..0c7a52f\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/mission/validations/adversarial-b.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,108 @@\n+# Adversarial Review B\n+\n+Reviewer: Claude Opus 4.6 (adversarial pass)\n+Scope: 11 commits from 5a6e618..3256b83\n+\n+## Findings\n+\n+### MEDIUM: Remaining awkward \"check whether the check\" phrasing in SKILL.md\n+\n+**File:** `skills/mission/SKILL.md`, line 397\n+\n+The task-4 fix (398775c) fixed two of the doubled-check phrasings flagged by the smoke test:\n+- \"check every check\" on line 351 became \"verify every check\"\n+- \"Check each contract check\" in usertest-validator.md became \"Verify each contract check\"\n+\n+A third instance was not fixed:\n+\n+```\n+3. **Inspection checks** (`[inspection]`) -- check whether the check could be rewritten\n+```\n+\n+The verb \"check\" immediately precedes the noun \"check\". This is the same awkward doubled pattern the task-4 fix was meant to eliminate. The smoke test (smoke-test.md section 4b, line 56) classified lines 395-397 as \"acceptable\" because the verb on line 395 is \"confirm\", not \"check\" -- but that reasoning only covers line 395. Line 397 uses \"check whether the check\" which is the same verb+noun collision as the two that were fixed.\n+\n+Suggested fix: \"determine whether the check could be rewritten\" or \"evaluate whether the check could be rewritten\".\n+\n+Severity: MEDIUM. The phrasing is technically correct but undermines the clarity goal of the rename mission.\n+\n+---\n+\n+### LOW: README uses \"check\" ambiguously for both validator steps and contract items\n+\n+**File:** `README.md`, lines 96-105\n+\n+The README describes the scrutiny validator's steps using informal \"check\" terminology:\n+\n+```\n+1. **Scrutiny validator** -- a thorough quality check that runs a sequence of checks:\n+   ...\n+   - Contract check -- does the code do what the contract says it should?\n+   - Execution check -- actually runs the code to confirm it works\n+   - Test health checks -- silent skip detection, diff coverage...\n+```\n+\n+Per the resolved ambiguity in UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md (line 183), a \"gate\" is a numbered step in the scrutiny validator's sequence, and a \"check\" is a single verifiable statement in a contract. The README uses \"check\" for both: \"Contract check\" (line 103), \"Execution check\" (line 104), \"Complexity check\" (line 101), and \"Code standards check\" (line 99) all describe validator steps (gates), not contract items.\n+\n+This is borderline. The README is written for a general audience and deliberately avoids formal internal terminology. The word \"check\" here functions as generic English (\"a thing we verify\"), not as the domain term \"Check\" (a contract item). But the three-way split was specifically designed to prevent this exact ambiguity, and someone reading the glossary alongside the README would notice the conflict.\n+\n+Severity: LOW. The README is user-facing prose where casual language is expected. No action needed unless the team wants strict glossary compliance in the README.\n+\n+---\n+\n+### INFO: Task-1 changed gate count from 11 to 14 -- correctness, not just a rename\n+\n+**File:** `skills/mission/SKILL.md`, line 594\n+\n+The task-1 diff (5a6e618) changed:\n+\n+```\n+-The prompt runs 11 checks: test presence, build, tests, lint, code review,\n+-module depth, code standards, simplify, security (if applicable), contract\n+-assertions, behavioral conformance.\n++The prompt runs 14 gates: test presence, build, tests, lint, code review,\n++module depth, code standards, simplify, security (if applicable), contract\n++checks, behavioral conformance, silent skip detection, diff coverage,\n++test quality review.\n+```\n+\n+This updated the count from 11 to 14 and added three gates that were missing from the original enumeration (silent skip detection, diff coverage, test quality review). The actual scrutiny-validator.md has had 14 gates since before this mission. This is a correctness fix bundled into a rename commit. The change is correct, but it goes beyond the task-1 scope (\"Rename scrutiny validator steps from check to gate\"). It was not caught by the per-task validator because the contract items only check for \"gate N\" naming and count, not for scope creep.\n+\n+Severity: INFO. The fix is correct. Noting it because scope creep in rename missions can mask unintended changes.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Cross-file consistency\n+\n+### Gate/Check/Assertion three-way split\n+\n+Verified across all in-scope files:\n+\n+| Context | Expected term | Files checked | Result |\n+|---------|--------------|---------------|--------|\n+| Numbered scrutiny validator steps | gate | scrutiny-validator.md, SKILL.md | PASS -- \"Gate N:\" format throughout, zero \"check [0-9]\" hits |\n+| Contract items | check | SKILL.md, scrutiny-validator.md, usertest-validator.md, adversarial-reviewer.md, contract.md, plan.md, pr-body.md, worker-fix-brief.md, mission-resume/SKILL.md, docs/, README.md | PASS -- \"assertion\" only in code-test context |\n+| Code test assertions | assertion | test-quality/SKILL.md, tdd/tests.md, scrutiny-validator.md (gates 1, 14) | PASS -- unchanged from before the mission |\n+| UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md definitions | all three defined | UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md | PASS -- resolved ambiguity section documents the split |\n+\n+### Contract item check\n+\n+Every contract check in contract.md was verified against the final file state:\n+\n+- Task 1: \"gate N\" naming throughout scrutiny-validator.md and SKILL.md. Zero \"check [0-9]\" hits. PASS.\n+- Task 2: \"Group checks by task\", \"minimum set of checks\", \"total contract checks\", \"Inspection checks\", \"check count feels right\" all present. PASS.\n+- Task 3: \"Contract Checks for This Task\" heading in both validator prompts. \"Check\" column headers. \"Failed Checks\" sections. \"checks\" in adversarial-reviewer.md, contract.md, plan.md, pr-body.md, worker-fix-brief.md, mission-resume/SKILL.md, docs/, README.md. PASS.\n+- Task 4: Smoke test verified. Preserved files unchanged. Awkward phrasings partially fixed. PASS with caveat on line 397.\n+- Task 5: No inconsistent capitalization found. No orphaned cross-references. PASS.\n+- Task 6: Module shape audit exists. Type Catalog entries match UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md. PASS.\n+\n+### Over-eager renames\n+\n+No code-test-context \"assertion\" was incorrectly renamed to \"check\". The three remaining \"assertion\" hits in scrutiny-validator.md (lines 113, 251, 257) are all about test assertions. Skills outside the rename scope (test-quality, tdd, prd) are untouched.\n+\n+### Missed renames\n+\n+No \"assertion\" in contract-item context remains in any in-scope file. grep confirmed zero hits.\n+\n+## Summary\n+\n+One MEDIUM finding (missed awkward phrasing on SKILL.md line 397), one LOW finding (README using \"check\" loosely for validator steps), and one INFO note (scope creep in task-1 that happens to be correct). The core rename is complete and consistent across all files. No over-eager renames. No missed renames. The three-way gate/check/assertion split is applied correctly in all formal contexts.\ndiff --git a/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/mission/validations/spec-delta.md b/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/mission/validations/spec-delta.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..af6c256\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/mission/validations/spec-delta.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@\n+# Spec Delta Check\n+\n+## Result: CLEAN\n+\n+All 13 coverage audit items verified present in the codebase.\n+\n+## Coverage Verification\n+\n+| # | PRD Requirement | Verified | Evidence |\n+|---|----------------|----------|----------|\n+| 1 | Progress log says \"12 checks in contract\" | YES | `skills/mission/SKILL.md` line 491: `<N> tasks, <M> checks in contract.` |\n+| 2 | PR body says \"Total checks: 15\" | YES | `skills/mission/templates/pr-body.md` line 22: `- Total checks: <M>` |\n+| 3 | Validator reports use \"Contract Checks\" and \"Failed Checks\" headings | YES | `skills/mission/prompts/scrutiny-validator.md` lines 288-294: `## Contract Checks` and `## Failed Checks (if any)` headings. `prompts/usertest-validator.md` lines 44-50: `## Contract Checks` and `## Failed Checks (if any)` headings. |\n+| 4 | Contract template uses \"check\" for items | YES | `skills/mission/templates/contract.md` lines 5-6, 10-11: items use `<check capturing specific spec scenario detail>` |\n+| 5 | Validator steps called \"gates\" in scrutiny prompt | YES | `skills/mission/prompts/scrutiny-validator.md`: `## Gate Sequence` heading (line 109), `## Gate Results` heading (line 270), table rows use `Gate 1:` through `Gate 14:` (lines 273-286). Zero matches for `check [0-9]` pattern. |\n+| 6 | Three-way split documented in UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md | YES | `UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md` line 183: `**\"check\" / \"assertion\" / \"gate\"** had overlapping usage... **Resolved** with a three-way split: a **Gate** is a numbered step in the scrutiny validator's sequence... A **Check** is a single verifiable statement in a contract. An **Assertion** is reserved for code test assertions only.` Also defined in tables: Check (line 17), Gate (line 28). |\n+| 7 | Consistent terminology in all prompts and templates | YES | Grep of `skills/mission/SKILL.md`, `skills/mission/prompts/`, and `skills/mission/templates/` for \"assertion\" returns only 3 hits, all in code-test contexts: test presence gate mentions \"test assertions\" (scrutiny-validator.md:113), P0 tautological assertions (scrutiny-validator.md:251, 257). No \"assertion\" used for contract items. |\n+| 8 | Validator subagent sees \"Contract Checks for This Task\" | YES | `skills/mission/prompts/scrutiny-validator.md` line 7: `## Contract Checks for This Task`. `prompts/usertest-validator.md` line 7: `## Contract Checks for This Task`. |\n+| 9 | \"Assertion\" preserved for code test concepts | YES | `skills/test-quality/SKILL.md`: \"assertion quality\" (line 23), \"tautological assertions\" (line 89), and assertion examples throughout. `skills/tdd/tests.md` line 23: \"One logical assertion per test\". Term is consistently used only for code test assertions. |\n+| 10 | Docs use \"contract checks\" consistently | YES | `docs/design-decisions.md` uses \"contract checks\" (lines 37, 44, 140, 142) and \"validation checks\" (line 84). No instances of \"assertion\" for contract items. |\n+| 11 | Launch dashboard says \"total contract checks\" | YES | `skills/mission/SKILL.md` line 485: `**Mission overview** -- change name, total tasks (feature + closing), total contract checks` |\n+| 12 | Fix brief says \"Do NOT copy check text\" | YES | `skills/mission/templates/worker-fix-brief.md` line 4: `Do NOT copy check text from the contract. Describe what went wrong, not what the contract expected.` |\n+| 13 | Mission-resume describes \"checks grouped by task\" | YES | `skills/mission-resume/SKILL.md` line 34: `| Contract | contract.md | Checks grouped by task for validators |` |\n+\n+## Approved Deviations\n+\n+None.\n+\n+## Notes\n+\n+- Item 10: `docs/design-decisions.md` line 84 uses \"validation checks\" once (`contract.md is a new OpenSpec artifact (validation checks, written during planning)`). This is describing the contract artifact's purpose, not naming a concept, so it does not conflict with the terminology standard. All other doc references use \"contract checks\" or \"checks\" consistently.\ndiff --git a/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/mission/validations/task-1-scrutiny-v2.md b/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/mission/validations/task-1-scrutiny-v2.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..bb90b41\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/mission/validations/task-1-scrutiny-v2.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@\n+# Scrutiny Validation: Task 1 (Fix v2)\n+\n+## Result: PASS\n+\n+## Gate Results\n+| Gate | Result | Notes |\n+|-------|--------|-------|\n+| Gate 1: Test presence | N/A | Markdown-only rename |\n+| Gate 2: Build | N/A | No build system |\n+| Gate 3: Tests | N/A | No test suite |\n+| Gate 4: Lint | N/A | No linter |\n+| Gate 5: Code review | PASS | Only intended terms changed. \"check\" renamed to \"gate\" for section headers and step-numbering contexts only. Verb uses (\"check if\", \"re-checking\", \"null checks\", etc.) correctly preserved. No content lost. Report template rows correctly prefixed with \"Gate N:\". SKILL.md updated count from \"11 checks\" to \"14 gates\" and renamed \"Failed Checks\" to \"Failed Gates\". |\n+| Gate 6: Module depth | N/A | Markdown files |\n+| Gate 7: Code standards | N/A | Markdown files |\n+| Gate 8: Code simplify | N/A | Markdown files |\n+| Gate 9: Security review | N/A | No security surfaces |\n+| Gate 10: Contract assertions | PASS | All 3 contract checks pass (see below) |\n+| Gate 11: Behavioral conformance | PASS | grep commands executed; file content inspected |\n+| Gate 12: Silent skip detection | SKIP | No test files |\n+| Gate 13: Diff coverage | SKIP | No production source |\n+| Gate 14: Test quality review | SKIP | No test files |\n+\n+## Contract Checks\n+| # | Check | Result | Method | Evidence |\n+|---|-------|--------|--------|----------|\n+| 1 | `grep -n \"check [0-9]\" skills/mission/prompts/scrutiny-validator.md` returns zero results | PASS | execution | Command returned exit code 1 (no matches), zero output lines |\n+| 2 | Report template labels each step as \"Gate N\" (Gate 1 through Gate 14) | PASS | inspection | Lines 273-286 of scrutiny-validator.md contain \"Gate 1: Test presence\" through \"Gate 14: Test quality review\" -- all 14 gates present with correct numbering |\n+| 3 | `grep -n \"check [0-9]\" skills/mission/SKILL.md` returns zero results | PASS | execution | Command returned exit code 1 (no matches), zero output lines |\n+\n+## Failed Checks (if any)\n+None.\n+\n+## Recommendations (if FAIL)\n+N/A.\ndiff --git a/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/mission/validations/task-1-scrutiny.md b/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/mission/validations/task-1-scrutiny.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..4034df0\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/mission/validations/task-1-scrutiny.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,75 @@\n+# Scrutiny Validation: Task 1\n+\n+## Result: FAIL\n+\n+## Named Facts\n+\n+- `Detected language: Unknown`\n+- `File sizes: skills/mission/prompts/scrutiny-validator.md: 301, skills/mission/SKILL.md: 902`\n+- `Error handling smells: 0 matches in 0 changed production lines (0 per KLOC). Locations: none`\n+- `Test runner: N/A -- no test suite in this repo`\n+\n+## Gate Results\n+| Gate | Result | Notes |\n+|-------|--------|-------|\n+| Test presence | N/A | Exempt: markdown-only terminology rename, no testable application code |\n+| Build | N/A | No build system in this repo |\n+| Tests | N/A | No test suite in this repo |\n+| Lint | N/A | No linter in th