 like 'check each check' exist in any modified file -- verb forms use 'verify' or 'mark' instead.\"\n+\n+Two instances exist:\n+\n+1. **`skills/mission/SKILL.md:351`** -- \"A validator reading only the contract and the diff should be able to check every check without guessing.\"\n+   - Modified in task-2 commit `8d87791`.\n+   - Fix: \"...should be able to verify every check without guessing.\"\n+\n+2. **`skills/mission/prompts/usertest-validator.md:19`** -- \"Check each contract check:\"\n+   - Modified in task-3 commit `99037c9`.\n+   - Fix: \"Verify each contract check:\" or \"Mark each contract check:\"\n+\n+The smoke test correctly identified these instances but classified them as \"WARN\" rather than recognizing they violate the contract. The contract check is unambiguous: these phrasings must not exist. The smoke test's own findings are the evidence of failure.\n+\n+## Recommendations\n+\n+1. Fix the two awkward phrasings by replacing the verb \"check\" with \"verify\" in both instances:\n+   - `skills/mission/SKILL.md:351`: \"...should be able to **verify** every check without guessing.\"\n+   - `skills/mission/prompts/usertest-validator.md:19`: \"**Verify** each contract check:\"\n+2. Re-run the smoke test to confirm no other doubled \"check\" patterns remain.\ndiff --git a/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/mission/validations/task-4-usertest.md b/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/mission/validations/task-4-usertest.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..6d5f06b\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/mission/validations/task-4-usertest.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@\n+# Task 4 User-Test Validation\n+\n+**Result: PASS**\n+\n+## Check 1: \"assertion\" hits are all in code-test context\n+\n+**PASS**\n+\n+`grep -rni \"assertion\"` across mission skills, prompts, templates, mission-resume, docs, and README returned 3 text hits (plus a binary match in `docs/architecture.png`):\n+\n+1. `scrutiny-validator.md:113` -- \"zero new test assertions\" in the test presence gate. Code-test context.\n+2. `scrutiny-validator.md:251` -- \"tautological assertions\" in severity rules. Code-test context.\n+3. `scrutiny-validator.md:257` -- \"tautological assertion in test_list_open\" in example output. Code-test context.\n+\n+All hits refer to test/assertion semantics. No user-facing \"assertion\" used as a synonym for \"check\" or \"verification.\"\n+\n+## Check 2: No \"check N\" pattern in scrutiny-validator.md\n+\n+**PASS**\n+\n+`grep -rn \"check [0-9]\" skills/mission/prompts/scrutiny-validator.md` returned zero hits (exit code 1).\n+\n+## Check 3: test-quality/SKILL.md contains required phrases\n+\n+**PASS**\n+\n+- Line 23: `### 1. Assertion quality (P0 if tautological)` -- contains both \"assertion quality\" and \"tautological\" together.\n+- Description line: `Evaluates assertion quality,...`\n+- Line 89 (example output): `Tautological assertion in test_list_open`\n+\n+## Check 4: tdd/tests.md contains \"one logical assertion per test\"\n+\n+**PASS**\n+\n+- Line 23: `- One logical assertion per test`\n+\n+## Check 5: No awkward doubled phrases\n+\n+**PASS**\n+\n+`grep -rni` for patterns \"check each check\", \"verify each verif\", \"test each test\", \"validate each validat\" across skills/, docs/, and README.md returned zero hits.\ndiff --git a/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/mission/validations/task-5-scrutiny.md b/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/mission/validations/task-5-scrutiny.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..7f33322\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/mission/validations/task-5-scrutiny.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@\n+# Scrutiny Validation: Task 5\n+\n+## Result: PASS\n+\n+## Gate Results\n+| Gate | Result | Notes |\n+|-------|--------|-------|\n+| Gate 1: Test presence | SKIP | Closing cleanup task -- exempt from test presence gate |\n+| Gate 2: Build | SKIP | No code changes -- handoff-only commit |\n+| Gate 3: Tests | SKIP | No code changes -- handoff-only commit |\n+| Gate 4: Lint | SKIP | No code changes -- handoff-only commit |\n+| Gate 5: Code review | SKIP | No code changes to review |\n+| Gate 6: Module depth | SKIP | No code changes |\n+| Gate 7: Code standards | SKIP | No code changes |\n+| Gate 8: Code simplify | SKIP | No code changes |\n+| Gate 9: Security review | N/A | No code changes |\n+| Gate 10: Contract checks | PASS | All 3 checks pass -- see below |\n+| Gate 11: Behavioral conformance | PASS | grep executed, results verified |\n+| Gate 12: Silent skip detection | SKIP | No test files in diff |\n+| Gate 13: Diff coverage | SKIP | No production source files in diff |\n+| Gate 14: Test quality review | SKIP | No test files in diff |\n+\n+## Contract Checks\n+| # | Check | Result | Method | Evidence |\n+|---|-------|--------|--------|----------|\n+| 1 | No inconsistent capitalization (e.g., \"Check\" mid-sentence where \"check\" is appropriate) | PASS | inspection | Reviewed all 12 instances of capitalized \"Check\" across SKILL.md, scrutiny-validator.md, and usertest-validator.md. Every instance is at sentence start, in a heading, or in a table header. No mid-sentence capitalization errors found. |\n+| 2 | No orphaned cross-references to old terminology | PASS | inspection | `grep -rn \"check [0-9]\" scrutiny-validator.md` returns zero hits -- no old \"check N\" numbered step references remain. All validator steps use \"gate N\". No \"assertion\" used in contract-item context -- only code-test context uses remain. |\n+| 3 | `grep -rni \"assertion\" ...` returns only code-test-context hits | PASS | execution | 3 hits found, all in scrutiny-validator.md, all code-test context: (1) line 113 \"test assertions\" referring to code test assertions, (2) line 251 \"tautological assertions\" in test quality severity rules, (3) line 257 \"tautological assertion\" in example test-quality output. Binary match in docs/architecture.png ignored. |\n+\n+## Notes\n+\n+The commit (593c063) contains only the handoff file `mission/handoffs/task-5.md`. The worker reported scanning all 14 files modified by this mission and found no cleanup needed. Independent verification confirms: capitalization is correct, no orphaned cross-references exist, and all \"assertion\" hits are code-test context.\n+\n+Minor observation: the handoff references commit SHA `cf253937...` which does not match the commit SHA `593c063...` being validated. This is cosmetic -- the handoff was written as part of commit 593c063 and the content is accurate regardless.\ndiff --git a/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/mission/validations/task-5-usertest.md b/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/mission/validations/task-5-usertest.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..460f282\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/mission/validations/task-5-usertest.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@\n+# User-Test Validation: Task 5\n+\n+## Result: PASS\n+\n+## Test Strategy\n+Infrastructure-only change (cleanup task producing only a handoff file). Behavioral checks verified by running the grep command specified in the contract and classifying each hit. Inspection checks verified by reading the files.\n+\n+## Tests Run\n+| # | Test Description | Method | Result |\n+|---|-----------------|--------|--------|\n+| 1 | Run `grep -rni \"assertion\" skills/mission/SKILL.md skills/mission/prompts/ skills/mission/templates/ skills/mission-resume/ docs/ README.md` | CLI execution | PASS -- 3 text hits, all code-test context |\n+| 2 | Spot-check capitalized \"Check\" across SKILL.md, scrutiny-validator.md, usertest-validator.md | Manual inspection | PASS -- all 12 instances correctly capitalized |\n+| 3 | Run `grep -rn \"check [0-9]\" skills/mission/prompts/scrutiny-validator.md` for orphaned old terminology | CLI execution | PASS -- zero hits |\n+\n+## Contract Checks\n+| # | Check | Result | Evidence |\n+|---|-------|--------|----------|\n+| 1 | No inconsistent capitalization | PASS | 12 instances of \"Check\" reviewed: 3 in headings, 4 in table headers, 2 at sentence start, 3 in section titles. All correct. |\n+| 2 | No orphaned cross-references to old terminology | PASS | No \"check N\" validator step references remain. No \"assertion\" used in contract-item context. All terminology updated by prior tasks is consistent. |\n+| 3 | grep returns only code-test-context hits | PASS | 3 hits: \"test assertions\" (line 113), \"tautological assertions\" (line 251), \"tautological assertion\" (line 257). All in scrutiny-validator.md test quality review section. Zero hits in SKILL.md, templates, mission-resume, docs, or README.md. |\ndiff --git a/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/mission/validations/task-6-scrutiny.md b/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/mission/validations/task-6-scrutiny.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..510fe82\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/mission/validations/task-6-scrutiny.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@\n+# Task 6 Scrutiny Validation\n+\n+## Result: PASS\n+\n+## Contract Checks\n+\n+| # | Check | Result | Evidence |\n+|---|-------|--------|----------|\n+| 1 | `mission/validations/module-shape-audit.md` exists and documents the comparison of design.md Type Catalog entries (Check, Gate, Contract) against UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md | PASS | File exists at expected path. Contains dedicated sections for Check, Gate, and Contract, each comparing the Type Catalog definition against the UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md definition and reporting drift status. Also includes module inventory verification across 7 modules. |\n+| 2 | Each Type Catalog entry (Check, Gate, Contract) has a matching definition in UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md | PASS | **Check** -- line 17, \"Planning and contracts\" section. **Gate** -- line 28, \"Validation\" section. **Contract** -- line 16, \"Planning and contracts\" section. All three definitions in UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md match the definitions reported in the audit file. |\n+\n+## Gate Sequence\n+\n+| Gate | Description | Result |\n+|------|-------------|--------|\n+| 1 | Output file exists | PASS |\n+| 2 | Audit covers all three Type Catalog entries | PASS |\n+| 3 | UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md contains Check definition | PASS |\n+| 4 | UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md contains Gate definition | PASS |\n+| 5 | UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md contains Contract definition | PASS |\n+| 6 | Audit definitions match actual UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md text | PASS |\n+| 7 | Audit reports no drift | PASS |\n+\n+## Notes\n+\n+The audit file is thorough. Beyond the three required Type Catalog entries, it also verifies terminology consistency across all modules (SKILL.md, scrutiny-validator.md, usertest-validator.md, adversarial-reviewer.md, templates, docs). No stale terminology was found.\ndiff --git a/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/mission/validations/task-6-usertest.md b/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/mission/validations/task-6-usertest.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..32f7f08\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/mission/validations/task-6-usertest.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@\n+# Task 6 User-Test Validation\n+\n+## Result: PASS\n+\n+## Contract Checks\n+\n+| # | Check | Result | Evidence |\n+|---|-------|--------|----------|\n+| 1 | `mission/validations/module-shape-audit.md` exists and documents the comparison of design.md Type Catalog entries (Check, Gate, Contract) against UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md | PASS | File is present and readable. Documents all three Type Catalog entries with cross-references to UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md sections. |\n+| 2 | Each Type Catalog entry (Check, Gate, Contract) has a matching definition in UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md | PASS | Verified by direct inspection of UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md. Check (line 17), Gate (line 28), Contract (line 16) are all present with definitions that match the audit's reported text. |\n+\n+## Behavioral Verification\n+\n+Verified the audit file's factual claims against the source file:\n+\n+- **Check**: Audit claims definition is \"A single verifiable statement in a contract that a validator can verify from outside the code.\" UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md line 17 confirms this exact text. PASS.\n+- **Gate**: Audit claims definition starts with \"A numbered step in the scrutiny validator's sequence.\" UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md line 28 confirms this exact text. PASS.\n+- **Contract**: Audit claims definition is \"A set of checks written during planning that define 'done' independently of implementation, consumed only by validators.\" UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md line 16 confirms this exact text. PASS.\n+- **No drift**: Audit reports zero drift across all modules. The resolved ambiguities section (line 183) of UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md documents the three-way split (gate/check/assertion) that this mission implemented. PASS.\ndiff --git a/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/mission/validations/task-7-scrutiny.md b/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/mission/validations/task-7-scrutiny.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..0db85f0\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/mission/validations/task-7-scrutiny.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@\n+# Task 7 Scrutiny Validation\n+\n+## Verdict: PASS\n+\n+## Checks\n+\n+### CLAUDE.md exists at project root\n+- **Result:** PASS\n+- CLAUDE.md exists at `/Users/stuart/.darkfactory/CLAUDE.md` (669 bytes)\n+\n+### ARCH.md exists at project root\n+- **Result:** PASS\n+- ARCH.md exists at `/Users/stuart/.darkfactory/ARCH.md` (4.3K)\n+\n+### CLAUDE.md was not modified by this mission\n+- **Result:** PASS\n+- `git diff f0102913..HEAD -- CLAUDE.md` produced no output\n+- Both files existed before the mission (verified with `git show f0102913:CLAUDE.md` and `git show f0102913:ARCH.md`)\n+- The task contract says \"if it already existed, it was not modified\" -- confirmed\n+\n+### ARCH.md was not modified by this mission\n+- **Result:** PASS\n+- `git diff f0102913..HEAD -- ARCH.md` produced no output\ndiff --git a/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/mission/validations/task-7-usertest.md b/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/mission/validations/task-7-usertest.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..e86d2c1\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/mission/validations/task-7-usertest.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@\n+# Task 7 User-Test Validation\n+\n+## Verdict: PASS\n+\n+## Test\n+\n+Since both CLAUDE.md and ARCH.md already existed before this mission, Task 7's only obligation was to leave them unmodified. Verified by:\n+\n+1. `git show f0102913:CLAUDE.md` -- succeeded, confirming the file existed at the base commit\n+2. `git show f0102913:ARCH.md` -- succeeded, confirming the file existed at the base commit\n+3. `git diff f0102913..HEAD -- CLAUDE.md ARCH.md` -- empty output, confirming zero modifications\n+\n+No worker commit was needed for this task. The contract is satisfied by the absence of changes.\ndiff --git a/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/mission/validations/task-8-scrutiny.md b/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/mission/validations/task-8-scrutiny.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..0b80ed4\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/mission/validations/task-8-scrutiny.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,43 @@\n+# Task 8 Scrutiny Validation\n+\n+## Verdict: PASS\n+\n+## Checks\n+\n+### README.md contains no \"assertion\" references in contract-item context\n+- **Result:** PASS\n+- `grep -ni \"assertion\" README.md` returned zero hits\n+- The word \"assertion\" does not appear anywhere in README.md\n+\n+### All documentation files use UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md terms consistently\n+- **Result:** PASS\n+- Searched all documentation files for \"assertion\":\n+  - README.md: 0 hits\n+  - docs/provenance.md: 0 hits\n+  - docs/design-decisions.md: 0 hits\n+  - docs/reference_factory_talk.md: 0 hits\n+  - docs/reference_pocock_talk.md: 0 hits (file does not contain \"assertion\")\n+  - ARCH.md: 0 hits (not modified, but confirmed clean)\n+  - CLAUDE.md: 0 hits (not modified, but confirmed clean)\n+- The grep command exited with code 1 (no matches) across all 7 files\n+\n+### README.md uses \"checks\" terminology correctly\n+- **Result:** PASS\n+- Contract items are called \"checks\" throughout (lines 84, 96, 103, 104, 105, 117, 118)\n+- Validator steps are called \"gates\" where appropriate (line 77, 119, 196)\n+- The three-way split from UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md is respected:\n+  - \"Gate\" for validator steps (e.g., \"phase gates\", \"mandatory gate\", \"not an automated gate\")\n+  - \"Check\" for contract items (e.g., \"contract check\", \"contract checks\", \"checks trace back\")\n+  - \"Assertion\" reserved for code test assertions only (not present in README since README does not discuss code-level test assertions)\n+\n+### Terminology consistency with UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md\n+- **Result:** PASS\n+- Spot-checked key terms in README.md:\n+  - \"Contract\" used correctly as \"a set of checks\" (line 86)\n+  - \"Check\" used for contract items (lines 84, 103)\n+  - \"Gate\" used for validator steps (lines 77, 119)\n+  - \"Brief\" used for worker input (lines 90, 133)\n+  - \"Handoff\" used for worker output (line 90)\n+  - \"Scrutiny validator\" and \"user-test validator\" named correctly (lines 96, 107)\n+  - \"Circuit breaker\" used correctly (line 111)\n+  - \"Fix loop\" described correctly (line 109)\ndiff --git a/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/mission/validations/task-8-usertest.md b/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/mission/validations/task-8-usertest.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..e18ba71\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/mission/validations/task-8-usertest.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@\n+# Task 8 User-Test Validation\n+\n+## Verdict: PASS\n+\n+## Test\n+\n+Read README.md end-to-end (307 lines) and verified terminology from a user's perspective:\n+\n+1. **No \"assertion\" in contract context.** The word \"assertion\" does not appear anywhere in README.md. Contract items are consistently called \"checks.\"\n+\n+2. **\"Check\" vs \"gate\" distinction is clear.** A reader encountering the README would understand:\n+   - A \"check\" is something the contract says the code should do (e.g., \"contract check\" on line 103)\n+   - A \"gate\" is a validator step (e.g., \"mandatory gate\" on line 77, \"not an automated gate\" on line 119)\n+\n+3. **Documentation files are consistent.** All docs under `docs/` (provenance.md, design-decisions.md, reference_factory_talk.md, reference_pocock_talk.md) contain zero instances of \"assertion\" in any context. The UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md resolved-ambiguities section (line 183) correctly documents the three-way split between gate/check/assertion.\n+\n+4. **Commit [task-8] 3256b83 message says \"Documentation: verified consistent\"** -- this aligns with the observed state. The task-8 worker confirmed consistency rather than needing to make changes, which is a valid outcome given that task-3 (99037c9) already renamed assertions to checks across prompts, templates, and docs.\ndiff --git a/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/proposal.md b/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/proposal.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..d606bd3\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/proposal.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@\n+## Why\n+\n+Non-developers interacting with Darkfactory mission output (progress logs, PR bodies, validator reports, contract files) are confused by \"assertions\" appearing everywhere. The word carries developer-specific meaning from testing contexts. Meanwhile, the most natural replacement -- \"check\" -- was blocked because the ubiquitous language used \"check\" for scrutiny validator steps, creating an ambiguity that was resolved by banning \"check\" for contract items. A three-way terminology split resolves both problems.\n+\n+## What Changes\n+\n+- Rename contract items from \"assertion\" to \"check\" across all living source files (skills/, templates/, prompts/, docs/, UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md, README.md)\n+- Rename scrutiny validator steps from \"check\" to \"gate\" to free up \"check\" for contract items\n+- Reserve \"assertion\" exclusively for code test assertions (tautological assertion, test assertions in code)\n+- Update UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md with the new three-way split (already completed in Phase 2)\n+- Update all validator prompts, contract templates, worker brief templates, PR body templates, and documentation to use consistent new terminology\n+\n+## Capabilities\n+\n+### New Capabilities\n+- `contract-check-rename`: Rename all contract-item uses of \"assertion\" to \"check\" across skills, templates, prompts, and docs\n+- `validator-gate-rename`: Rename all scrutiny validator step uses of \"check\" to \"gate\" in validator prompts and related references\n+\n+### Modified Capabilities\n+\n+## Impact\n+\n+- ~160 occurrences across ~15 living source files\n+- Bulk of changes (~50+) in skills/mission/SKILL.md (the main mission orchestrator skill)\n+- Validator prompts (scrutiny, user-test, adversarial) produce reports with renamed section headings\n+- Contract template items use new terminology\n+- PR body template and progress log language changes\n+- No runtime code changes -- darkfactory has no application code\n+- No breaking changes to external interfaces -- all changes are internal to skill definitions and templates\n+- Future missions will use new terminology; past missions retain historical terminology\ndiff --git a/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/specs/contract-check-rename/spec.md b/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/specs/contract-check-rename/spec.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..71680b8\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/specs/contract-check-rename/spec.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,88 @@\n+## ADDED Requirements\n+\n+### Requirement: Contract items use \"check\" terminology\n+All living source files SHALL use \"check\" (not \"assertion\") when referring to a single verifiable statement in a contract. The term \"assertion\" SHALL be reserved exclusively for code test assertions (e.g., tautological assertion, `assert_eq!`, `expect().toBe()`).\n+\n+#### Scenario: Contract definition in UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md\n+- **WHEN** a reader looks up the Contract definition in UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md\n+- **THEN** the definition says \"a set of checks\" (not \"a set of assertions\")\n+\n+#### Scenario: Check definition in UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md\n+- **WHEN** a reader looks up contract item terminology in UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md\n+- **THEN** the entry is named \"Check\" with \"Assertion (in contract context)\" listed as an alias to avoid\n+\n+#### Scenario: Mission skill contract rules\n+- **WHEN** the orchestrator reads the contract rules in skills/mission/SKILL.md\n+- **THEN** the rules use \"check\" for contract items (e.g., \"Group checks by task\", \"Write the minimum set of checks\")\n+\n+#### Scenario: Contract template format\n+- **WHEN** the orchestrator reads the contract template in templates/contract.md\n+- **THEN** the template items use \"check\" (e.g., `[execution] <check capturing specific spec scenario detail>`)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Validator report section headings\n+- **WHEN** a validator produces a report using the scrutiny or user-test validator prompt\n+- **THEN** the report uses \"Contract Checks\" and \"Failed Checks\" as section headings, and \"Check\" as the column header in results tables\n+\n+#### Scenario: PR body template\n+- **WHEN** the orchestrator generates a PR body from templates/pr-body.md\n+- **THEN** the template says \"Total checks: <M>\" (not \"Total assertions\")\n+\n+#### Scenario: Progress log language\n+- **WHEN** the orchestrator writes to progress.md during launch confirmation or task completion\n+- **THEN** the entries use \"checks\" (e.g., \"<N> tasks, <M> checks in contract\")\n+\n+#### Scenario: Worker brief and fix brief guidance\n+- **WHEN** a worker reads a brief or fix brief\n+- **THEN** the guidance says \"Do NOT copy check text from the contract\" (not \"assertion text\")\n+\n+#### Scenario: Documentation consistency\n+- **WHEN** a developer reads docs/provenance.md, docs/design-decisions.md, or docs/reference_factory_talk.md\n+- **THEN** references to contract items use \"checks\" (not \"assertions\")\n+\n+#### Scenario: README consistency\n+- **WHEN** a developer reads README.md\n+- **THEN** references to contract items use \"checks\" (not \"assertions\")\n+\n+### Requirement: Code test assertion terminology preserved\n+The term \"assertion\" SHALL be preserved in all contexts that refer to code test assertions, including the test-quality skill, tdd skill, and test presence gate.\n+\n+#### Scenario: Tautological assertion unchanged\n+- **WHEN** a reader looks up \"Tautological assertion\" in UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md or the test-quality skill\n+- **THEN** the term remains \"Tautological assertion\" (not \"Tautological check\")\n+\n+#### Scenario: Test quality skill unchanged\n+- **WHEN** the scrutiny validator invokes the test-quality skill\n+- **THEN** the skill uses \"assertion quality\", \"tautological assertion\", and \"test assertion\" unchanged\n+\n+#### Scenario: TDD skill unchanged\n+- **WHEN** a developer reads the tdd skill guidance\n+- **THEN** it says \"one logical assertion per test\" (not \"one logical check per test\")\n+\n+#### Scenario: Test presence gate code test reference\n+- **WHEN** the scrutiny validator runs the test presence gate\n+- **THEN** the prompt says \"zero new test assertions\" referring to code-level assertions in test files\n+\n+### Requirement: Archived and in-flight files untouched\n+Living source files SHALL be renamed, but archived mission files and in-flight change directories SHALL NOT be modified.\n+\n+#### Scenario: Archived missions preserved\n+- **WHEN** a grep for \"assertion\" is run against files under openspec/changes/archive/\n+- **THEN** the results are unchanged from before this mission\n+\n+#### Scenario: In-flight changes preserved\n+- **WHEN** a grep for \"assertion\" is run against in-flight change directories (e.g., skill-decomposition, deterministic-planning)\n+- **THEN** the results are unchanged from before this mission\n+\n+### Requirement: Resolved ambiguity updated\n+The resolved ambiguity about \"check\" and \"assertion\" in UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md SHALL document the three-way split.\n+\n+#### Scenario: Three-way split documented\n+- **WHEN** a reader looks at the resolved ambiguities section\n+- **THEN** there is an entry explaining: Gate = scrutiny validator step, Check = contract item, Assertion = code test assertion only\n+\n+### Requirement: Relationships section updated\n+The Relationships section of UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md SHALL use \"Checks\" for contract items.\n+\n+#### Scenario: Contract contains Checks\n+- **WHEN** a reader looks at the Relationships section\n+- **THEN** it says \"A Contract contains Checks grouped by Task\" (not \"Assertions\")\ndiff --git a/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/specs/validator-gate-rename/spec.md b/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/specs/validator-gate-rename/spec.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..2f3bef1\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/specs/validator-gate-rename/spec.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@\n+## ADDED Requirements\n+\n+### Requirement: Scrutiny validator steps use \"gate\" terminology\n+All references to numbered scrutiny validator steps SHALL use \"gate\" (not \"check\"). This frees \"check\" for contract items.\n+\n+#### Scenario: Gate definition in UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md\n+- **WHEN** a reader looks up scrutiny validator step terminology in UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md\n+- **THEN** there is a \"Gate\" entry defining it as a numbered step in the scrutiny validator's sequence, with outcomes PASS, FAIL, WARN, SKIP, or N/A\n+\n+#### Scenario: Scrutiny validator prompt uses gates\n+- **WHEN** the orchestrator fills in the scrutiny validator prompt from prompts/scrutiny-validator.md\n+- **THEN** numbered steps are called \"gate N\" (not \"check N\") throughout the prompt\n+\n+#### Scenario: Behavioral conformance references gate\n+- **WHEN** a reader looks up \"Behavioral conformance\" in UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md\n+- **THEN** it references \"gate 11\" (not \"check 11\")\n+\n+#### Scenario: Self-skipping gate renamed\n+- **WHEN** a reader looks up the concept of a validator step that auto-skips\n+- **THEN** the term is \"Self-skipping gate\" (not \"Self-gating check\")\n+\n+#### Scenario: Mission skill references gates\n+- **WHEN** the orchestrator reads skills/mission/SKILL.md for validator step references\n+- **THEN** the text uses \"gate\" for validator steps (e.g., \"gate 10: contract checks\" not \"check 10: contract assertions\")\n+\n+#### Scenario: Scrutiny validator report gate numbering\n+- **WHEN** a scrutiny validator produces a report following the prompt template\n+- **THEN** each validator step result is labeled as a gate (e.g., \"Gate 1: Test presence\", \"Gate 10: Contract checks\")\ndiff --git a/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/tasks.md b/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/tasks.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..9cb84cb\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/openspec/changes/user-friendly-contract-language/tasks.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,88 @@\n+## 1. Validator Gate Rename\n+\n+- [x] Task 1: Rename scrutiny validator steps from \"check\" to \"gate\"\n+  Depends on: none\n+  Consumes: current scrutiny-validator.md, SKILL.md validator step references\n+  Produces: updated scrutiny-validator.md with \"gate N\" numbering, updated SKILL.md validator step references\n+  Layers: scrutiny-prompt, mission-skill\n+\n+  Rename all numbered validator step references from \"check N\" to \"gate N\" in `skills/mission/prompts/scrutiny-validator.md`. Update any references to validator steps in `skills/mission/SKILL.md` that use \"check\" in the validator-step sense (e.g., \"check 10: contract assertions\" becomes \"gate 10: contract checks\"). Do NOT rename \"assertion\" to \"check\" in this task -- only rename validator step \"check\" to \"gate\". Verify: `grep -n \"check [0-9]\" skills/mission/prompts/scrutiny-validator.md` returns zero hits.\n+\n+## 2. Contract Check Rename -- Mission Skill\n+\n+- [x] Task 2: Rename contract \"assertions\" to \"checks\" in skills/mission/SKILL.md\n+  Depends on: Task 1\n+  Consumes: updated SKILL.md from Task 1 (validator step references already say \"gate\")\n+  Produces: updated SKILL.md with \"check\" for all contract items\n+  Layers: mission-skill\n+\n+  Rename all contract-item uses of \"assertion/assertions\" to \"check/checks\" in `skills/mission/SKILL.md`. This is the bulk of the work (~50+ occurrences). Preserve \"assertion\" where it refers to code test assertions (e.g., \"test assertions\" in the test presence gate description). Verify: `grep -ni \"assertion\" skills/mission/SKILL.md` returns only code-test-context hits.\n+\n+## 3. Contract Check Rename -- Prompts, Templates, Docs\n+\n+- [x] Task 3: Rename contract \"assertions\" to \"checks\" in remaining living source files\n+  Depends on: Task 1\n+  Consumes: current validator prompts, templates, docs, README\n+  Produces: updated prompts, templates, docs, README with \"check\" for contract items\n+  Layers: scrutiny-prompt, usertest-prompt, adversarial-prompt, templates, docs\n+\n+  Rename all contract-item uses of \"assertion/assertions\" to \"check/checks\" in these files:\n+  - `skills/mission/prompts/scrutiny-validator.md` (contract sections, not gate numbering)\n+  - `skills/mission/prompts/usertest-validator.md`\n+  - `skills/mission/prompts/adversarial-reviewer.md`\n+  - `skills/mission/templates/contract.md`\n+  - `skills/mission/templates/pr-body.md`\n+  - `skills/mission/templates/plan.md`\n+  - `skills/mission/templates/worker-fix-brief.md`\n+  - `skills/mission-resume/SKILL.md`\n+  - `docs/provenance.md`\n+  - `docs/design-decisions.md`\n+  - `docs/reference_factory_talk.md`\n+  - `README.md`\n+  Do NOT modify `skills/test-quality/SKILL.md`, `skills/tdd/tests.md`, or `skills/prd/SKILL.md`. Verify: `grep -rni \"assertion\" <each modified file>` returns only code-test-context hits or zero hits.\n+\n+## 4. Closing Tasks\n+\n+- [x] Task 4: Smoke test -- verify terminology consistency across all in-scope files\n+  Depends on: Task 2, Task 3\n+  Consumes: all modified files from Tasks 1-3\n+  Produces: grep verification report confirming no stale \"assertion\" in contract context, no stale \"check N\" in validator step context\n+  Layers: glossary, mission-skill, scrutiny-prompt, usertest-prompt, adversarial-prompt, templates, docs\n+\n+  Run comprehensive grep verification across all in-scope files:\n+  1. `grep -rni \"assertion\" skills/mission/SKILL.md skills/mission/prompts/ skills/mission/templates/ skills/mission-resume/ docs/ README.md UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md` -- every hit must be code-test context\n+  2. `grep -rn \"check [0-9]\" skills/mission/prompts/scrutiny-validator.md` -- must return zero hits\n+  3. Verify preserved files are unchanged: `skills/test-quality/SKILL.md`, `skills/tdd/tests.md`, `skills/prd/SKILL.md`\n+  4. Read through each modified file to check for awkward phrasings introduced by the rename\n+\n+- [x] Task 5: Cleanup -- remove dead references and leftover inconsistencies\n+  Depends on: Task 4\n+  Consumes: all files from Tasks 1-3\n+  Produces: clean codebase with no debris from the rename\n+  Layers: all in-scope\n+\n+  Review all modified files for: unused backward-compatibility shims, inconsistent capitalization (Check vs check), orphaned cross-references, and any \"assertion\" that slipped through in a non-code-test context.\n+\n+- [x] Task 6: Module shape re-check\n+  Depends on: Task 5\n+  Consumes: design.md Type Catalog and Module Inventory, all committed code\n+  Produces: mission/validations/module-shape-audit.md\n+  Layers: all in-scope\n+\n+  Compare design.md module descriptions and Type Catalog entries (Check, Gate, Contract) against what the committed files actually contain. Verify that each Type Catalog term appears in UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md with a matching definition. Write findings to mission/validations/module-shape-audit.md.\n+\n+- [x] Task 7: CLAUDE.md + ARCH.md generation\n+  Depends on: Task 5\n+  Consumes: all committed changes, design.md\n+  Produces: CLAUDE.md and/or ARCH.md if they don't already exist\n+  Layers: docs\n+\n+  If the project root does not have a CLAUDE.md, create one using the built codebase. If CLAUDE.md already exists, do not modify it. If no ARCH.md exists, create one from design.md. If ARCH.md already exists, do not modify it.\n+\n+- [x] Task 8: Documentation update\n+  Depends on: Task 7\n+  Consumes: all committed changes, CLAUDE.md and ARCH.md (if newly created)\n+  Produces: updated README.md reflecting the terminology change\n+  Layers: docs\n+\n+  Verify README.md accurately describes the current terminology. Update any documentation that references the old \"assertion\" terminology for contract items. Ensure UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md terms are used consistently in all docs. Verify any newly generated CLAUDE.md or ARCH.md also use correct terminology.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
