{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '520,590p' skills/mission/SKILL.md\"","aggregated_output":"\nEnsure a feature branch. If `git rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD` equals `gh api repos/{owner}/{repo} --jq .default_branch` (abort Phase 7 if that gh call fails -- it means no GitHub remote or bad auth), run `git checkout -b mission/<change-name>` -- if that branch already exists, use `mission/<change-name>-$(date -u +%Y%m%d%H%M%S)`. Log the checkout to progress.md.\n\nShow the user a summary dashboard:\n1. **Mission overview** -- change name, total tasks (feature + closing), total contract checks\n2. **Coverage audit result** -- number of PRD requirements covered, any deferred/skipped items\n3. **Engine config** -- which engine runs each role (from config.yaml)\n\nAsk: \"Everything has been reviewed. Ready to start the build?\"\n\n- If yes: append `<timestamp> -- Plan approved. <N> tasks, <M> checks in contract.` to progress.md. Update plan status to BUILDING. Post a comment on the PRD issue: `gh issue comment <number> --body \"Mission dispatched. <N> tasks, <M> checks. Draft PR will link back on completion.\"` Proceed to Phase 8.\n- If the human wants to revisit something: loop back to the specific phase they name. Do not re-review everything.\n\n**Gate -- proceed when:**\n- [ ] Human confirms \"ready to start the build\"\n- [ ] progress.md updated with approval timestamp and task/check counts\n- [ ] Plan status = BUILDING\n\n---\n\n## Phase 8: Build Loop\n\n> **Rules:** 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 8, 9\n> **Goal:** Build all tasks with per-task validation.\n> **Inputs:** tasks.md, contract.md, design.md, proposal.md, config.yaml, UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md\n> **Outputs:** Committed code per task, validation reports in mission/validations/. Codebase deltas are internal (populate subsequent task briefs within this phase).\n\nFor each unchecked task (`- [ ]`) in tasks.md, run Steps 1-7. Process tasks in order, one at a time (serial execution). Skip tasks marked `- [~]` (skipped) and `- [x]` (complete).\n\n### Step 1: Assemble Brief\n\nWrite a brief to `mission/briefs/task-N.md`.\n\n#### Brief Template\n\nRead [templates/worker-brief.md](templates/worker-brief.md).\n\n**The brief NEVER contains contract.md content.** \n\n#### Browser Tools Override\n\nIf `browser_tools: false` in config.yaml (human override), omit visual verification procedures from the worker brief even for `/frontend` tasks. The worker follows the `/frontend` workflow but skips the chrome-devtools-mcp visual verify step in the Build phase.\n\n### Step 2: Dispatch Worker\n\nRead the engine from `mission/config.yaml`.\n\n#### Browser Tools Pre-flight (Skill: /frontend tasks only)\n\nBefore dispatching a `/frontend` task, check that chrome-devtools-mcp is available:\n- If available: proceed with dispatch, include visual verification in the brief\n- If unavailable: block dispatch. Log to progress.md: `<timestamp> -- Task N: chrome-devtools-mcp unavailable at dispatch. Pausing.` Surface to human with options: retry (check again), skip visual verify for this task, or abort mission\n\n#### If engine is `codex`:\n\nBefore dispatching, run `git rev-parse HEAD` and store the result as `PRE_TASK_SHA`. This value is used in Step 7 to generate the codebase delta — store it somewhere you can reference after the background worker returns (e.g. in the plan file or a local variable).\n\nUse the Bash tool with `run_in_background: true` to run the worker. Use this exact bash script:\n\n```bash\nBRIEF_PATH=\"<absolute path to mission/briefs/task-N.md>\"\nHANDOFF_PATH=\"<absolute path to mission/handoffs/task-N.md>\"\nLOG_PATH=\"<absolute path to mission/logs/task-N-codex.log>\"\nPRE_TASK_SHA=$(git rev-parse HEAD)\n# Clean stale temp files and directories from previous workers to avoid filling /tmp\nfind /tmp -mindepth 1 -maxdepth 1 -user \"$(whoami)\" -mmin +30 -not -name \"claude-*\" \\( -type f -delete -o -type d -exec rm -rf {} + \\) 2>/dev/null\n\n# Dispatch via darkfactory-dispatch: process supervisor with timeout, heartbeat, and structured JSON result\nDISPATCH_RESULT=$(darkfactory-dispatch \\\n  --model gpt-5.5 \\\n  --effort high \\\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"tool_end","dispatch_id":"01KQR534Y1SG1Q3ZEXCGT4QRH4","ts":"2026-05-04T00:10:56Z","tool":"command_execution"}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '100,150p' skills/mission-init/SKILL.md\"","aggregated_output":"After a first-time init, tell the user to restart Claude Code so `/opsx:` commands can register.\n\n## Step 3: Verify CLI Dependencies\n\nRun these checks. Each command must always exit 0 so parallel Bash calls do not cancel each other:\n\n```bash\ncodex --version 2>/dev/null || echo \"NOT_INSTALLED\"\ndarkfactory-dispatch --version 2>/dev/null || echo \"NOT_INSTALLED\"\ngh --version 2>/dev/null || echo \"NOT_INSTALLED\"\ngh auth status 2>/dev/null || echo \"NOT_INSTALLED\"\nopenspec --version 2>/dev/null || echo \"NOT_INSTALLED\"\njq --version 2>/dev/null || echo \"NOT_INSTALLED\"\n```\n\nReport each tool as installed, not installed, or not authenticated.\n\n- `codex`: if missing, fix with `npm install -g @openai/codex`. If installed but a Codex command reports an auth failure, fix with `codex login`.\n- `darkfactory-dispatch`: if missing, fix with `cd ~/.darkfactory/tools/darkfactory-dispatch && make install`.\n- `gh`: if `gh --version` is missing, fix with `brew install gh`. If `gh auth status` fails while `gh` is installed, fix with `gh auth login`.\n- `openspec`: if missing, fix with `npm install -g @fission-ai/openspec`.\n- `jq`: if missing, fix with `brew install jq`.\n\n## Step 4: Browser Tools Check (conditional)\n\nIf `browser_tools: true` in the mission's config.yaml (or if any task in the current mission has `Skill: /frontend`), check that chrome-devtools-mcp is registered:\n\n```bash\n# Check if chrome-devtools MCP tools are available.\n# The exact check depends on the MCP registration mechanism.\n```\n\nIf chrome-devtools-mcp is not registered:\n- Report: `[!] chrome-devtools-mcp - not registered (required when browser_tools: true)`\n- Fix: Install chrome-devtools-mcp from https://github.com/nichochar/chrome-devtools-mcp and add it to MCP configuration\n- This blocks mission launch for missions with `/frontend` tasks\n\nIf `browser_tools: false` or no `/frontend` tasks exist, skip this check.\n\n## Step 5: Coverage Tool Detection\n\nDetect the project language from build files at the project root:\n\n- `Cargo.toml` means Rust.\n- `package.json` means TypeScript/Node.\n- `pyproject.toml` or `requirements.txt` means Python.\n\nCheck the matching coverage tool.\n\nFor Rust:\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
