{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba skills/mission/prompts/scrutiny-validator.md | sed -n '158,183p'\"","aggregated_output":"   158\t\n   159\t   Report: write one bullet per individual finding instance; state which symbol or boundary is affected and why it matters for depth. If nothing flagged, write 'No module depth issues.'\n   160\t\n   161\t7. **Frontend depth review:** If the diff contains zero `.tsx` or `.jsx` files, report `frontend-depth | SKIP | no React component files in diff` and move to the next gate.\n   162\t\n   163\t   When `.tsx`/`.jsx` files are present, evaluate each against the four deep-component rules defined in `skills/frontend/DEEP-COMPONENTS.md`:\n   164\t\n   165\t   - **Small semantic interface:** Flag components where the caller must understand more than 7 independent semantic concepts (count props + context providers consumed + URL params read + cache keys depended on). Do not count raw prop count alone — a component with 6 props describing one domain concept is deep. Exempt components in `*/ui/*` directories, components with only `className` + `children` + `...rest` props (design system leaves), and components importing from `@radix-ui/*` that wrap a Radix primitive with styling (headless behavior primitives).\n   166\t   - **Derive don't sync:** Flag `useEffect` paired with `setState` where the effect body is pure data transformation (no I/O, no subscriptions, no browser APIs). Suggest `useMemo` or inline computation as remediation. Do not flag effects that perform I/O, subscribe to external sources, or call imperative browser APIs.\n   167\t   - **Composition over configuration:** Flag components accepting config-style props — arrays of item objects or option objects with more than 5 configuration entries — where compound components with children/slots would be clearer. Do not flag headless primitives or design system components that use config props by convention.\n   168\t   - **Collapse coordination:** Flag components that expose coordination knobs such as `onStep1Complete`, `onValidate`, `onReset`, `onLoadingChange` rather than semantic events such as `onSubmit`, `onCancel`, `onSelect`, `onChange`. Coordination knobs indicate the parent is driving the child's internal workflow rather than the child owning it.\n   169\t\n   170\t   Allowed-shallow exceptions (do not flag these for depth violations):\n   171\t   - Components in `*/ui/*` directories\n   172\t   - Components with only `className` + `children` + `...rest` props\n   173\t   - Components importing from `@radix-ui/*` that wrap a Radix primitive\n   174\t   - Route/layout glue components (thin wrappers that read route params and pass data)\n   175\t\n   176\t   Verdict:\n   177\t   - PASS: No violations found, or all flagged items are in allowed-shallow exception categories.\n   178\t   - WARN: Isolated finding in a single component.\n   179\t   - FAIL: Systematic violations found across multiple components in the diff.\n   180\t\n   181\t   Report: Write one bullet per finding instance; state which component, which rule, and what specifically violates it. If nothing flagged, write \"No frontend depth issues.\"\n   182\t\n   183\t8. **Code standards gate:** Review the diff for these specific anti-patterns. Flag any found:\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
