{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba skills/react-perf/SKILL.md | sed -n '3740,3825p'\"","aggregated_output":"  3740\t\n  3741\t**Incorrect: re-subscribes on every render**\n  3742\t\n  3743\t```tsx\n  3744\tfunction useWindowEvent(event: string, handler: (e) => void) {\n  3745\t  useEffect(() => {\n  3746\t    window.addEventListener(event, handler)\n  3747\t    return () => window.removeEventListener(event, handler)\n  3748\t  }, [event, handler])\n  3749\t}\n  3750\t```\n  3751\t\n  3752\t**Correct: stable subscription**\n  3753\t\n  3754\t```tsx\n  3755\timport { useEffectEvent } from 'react'\n  3756\t\n  3757\tfunction useWindowEvent(event: string, handler: (e) => void) {\n  3758\t  const onEvent = useEffectEvent(handler)\n  3759\t\n  3760\t  useEffect(() => {\n  3761\t    window.addEventListener(event, onEvent)\n  3762\t    return () => window.removeEventListener(event, onEvent)\n  3763\t  }, [event])\n  3764\t}\n  3765\t```\n  3766\t\n  3767\t**Alternative: use `useEffectEvent` if you're on latest React:**\n  3768\t\n  3769\t`useEffectEvent` provides a cleaner API for the same pattern: it creates a stable function reference that always calls the latest version of the handler.\n  3770\t\n  3771\t### 8.4 useEffectEvent for Stable Callback Refs\n  3772\t\n  3773\t**Impact: LOW (prevents effect re-runs)**\n  3774\t\n  3775\tAccess latest values in callbacks without adding them to dependency arrays. Prevents effect re-runs while avoiding stale closures.\n  3776\t\n  3777\t**Incorrect: effect re-runs on every callback change**\n  3778\t\n  3779\t```tsx\n  3780\tfunction SearchInput({ onSearch }: { onSearch: (q: string) => void }) {\n  3781\t  const [query, setQuery] = useState('')\n  3782\t\n  3783\t  useEffect(() => {\n  3784\t    const timeout = setTimeout(() => onSearch(query), 300)\n  3785\t    return () => clearTimeout(timeout)\n  3786\t  }, [query, onSearch])\n  3787\t}\n  3788\t```\n  3789\t\n  3790\t**Correct: using React's useEffectEvent**\n  3791\t\n  3792\t```tsx\n  3793\timport { useEffectEvent } from 'react';\n  3794\t\n  3795\tfunction SearchInput({ onSearch }: { onSearch: (q: string) => void }) {\n  3796\t  const [query, setQuery] = useState('')\n  3797\t  const onSearchEvent = useEffectEvent(onSearch)\n  3798\t\n  3799\t  useEffect(() => {\n  3800\t    const timeout = setTimeout(() => onSearchEvent(query), 300)\n  3801\t    return () => clearTimeout(timeout)\n  3802\t  }, [query])\n  3803\t}\n  3804\t```\n  3805\t\n  3806\t---\n  3807\t\n  3808\t## References\n  3809\t\n  3810\t1. [https://react.dev](https://react.dev)\n  3811\t2. [https://nextjs.org](https://nextjs.org)\n  3812\t3. [https://swr.vercel.app](https://swr.vercel.app)\n  3813\t4. [https://github.com/shuding/better-all](https://github.com/shuding/better-all)\n  3814\t5. [https://github.com/isaacs/node-lru-cache](https://github.com/isaacs/node-lru-cache)\n  3815\t6. [https://vercel.com/blog/how-we-optimized-package-imports-in-next-js](https://vercel.com/blog/how-we-optimized-package-imports-in-next-js)\n  3816\t7. [https://vercel.com/blog/how-we-made-the-vercel-dashboard-twice-as-fast](https://vercel.com/blog/how-we-made-the-vercel-dashboard-twice-as-fast)\n  3817\t\n  3818\t---\n  3819\t\n  3820\t# Web Interface Guidelines\n  3821\t\n  3822\tUpstream source: vercel-labs/web-interface-guidelines\n  3823\t\n  3824\t---\n  3825\tdescription: Review UI code for Vercel Web Interface Guidelines compliance\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
