{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba skills/ui-system/SKILL.md | sed -n '1,130p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t---\n     2\tname: ui-system\n     3\tuser-invokable: true\n     4\tdescription: ShadCN/Radix component selection, token discipline, composition patterns, and accessibility defaults. Use when working with ShadCN/ui components, Radix primitives, design system tokens, Tailwind styling for components, or component composition patterns. Constraint skill — use alongside /frontend methodology.\n     5\t---\n     6\t\n     7\t# UI System (ShadCN/Radix)\n     8\t\n     9\tUpstream source: shadcn/ui skill from github.com/shadcn-ui/ui\n    10\t\n    11\t> **IMPORTANT:** Run all CLI commands using the project's package runner: `npx shadcn@latest`, `pnpm dlx shadcn@latest`, or `bunx --bun shadcn@latest` — based on the project's `packageManager`. Examples below use `npx shadcn@latest` but substitute the correct runner for the project.\n    12\t\n    13\t## Principles\n    14\t\n    15\t1. **Use existing components first.** Use `npx shadcn@latest search` to check registries before writing custom UI. Check community registries too.\n    16\t2. **Compose, don't reinvent.** Settings page = Tabs + Card + form controls. Dashboard = Sidebar + Card + Chart + Table.\n    17\t3. **Use built-in variants before custom styles.** `variant=\"outline\"`, `size=\"sm\"`, etc.\n    18\t4. **Use semantic colors.** `bg-primary`, `text-muted-foreground` — never raw values like `bg-blue-500`.\n    19\t\n    20\t## Critical Rules\n    21\t\n    22\t### Styling & Tailwind\n    23\t\n    24\t- **`className` for layout, not styling.** Never override component colors or typography.\n    25\t- **No `space-x-*` or `space-y-*`.** Use `flex` with `gap-*`. For vertical stacks, `flex flex-col gap-*`.\n    26\t- **Use `size-*` when width and height are equal.** `size-10` not `w-10 h-10`.\n    27\t- **Use `truncate` shorthand.** Not `overflow-hidden text-ellipsis whitespace-nowrap`.\n    28\t- **No manual `dark:` color overrides.** Use semantic tokens (`bg-background`, `text-muted-foreground`).\n    29\t- **Use `cn()` for conditional classes.** Don't write manual template literal ternaries.\n    30\t- **No manual `z-index` on overlay components.** Dialog, Sheet, Popover, etc. handle their own stacking.\n    31\t\n    32\t### Semantic Colors\n    33\t\n    34\t**Incorrect:**\n    35\t\n    36\t```tsx\n    37\t<div className=\"bg-blue-500 text-white\">\n    38\t  <p className=\"text-gray-600\">Secondary text</p>\n    39\t</div>\n    40\t```\n    41\t\n    42\t**Correct:**\n    43\t\n    44\t```tsx\n    45\t<div className=\"bg-primary text-primary-foreground\">\n    46\t  <p className=\"text-muted-foreground\">Secondary text</p>\n    47\t</div>\n    48\t```\n    49\t\n    50\tFor status indicators, use Badge variants, semantic tokens like `text-destructive`, or define custom CSS variables — don't reach for raw Tailwind colors.\n    51\t\n    52\t**Incorrect:**\n    53\t\n    54\t```tsx\n    55\t<span className=\"text-emerald-600\">+20.1%</span>\n    56\t<span className=\"text-red-600\">-3.2%</span>\n    57\t```\n    58\t\n    59\t**Correct:**\n    60\t\n    61\t```tsx\n    62\t<Badge variant=\"secondary\">+20.1%</Badge>\n    63\t<span className=\"text-destructive\">-3.2%</span>\n    64\t```\n    65\t\n    66\t### className for Layout Only\n    67\t\n    68\tUse `className` for layout (e.g. `max-w-md`, `mx-auto`, `mt-4`), **not** for overriding component colors or typography.\n    69\t\n    70\t**Incorrect:**\n    71\t\n    72\t```tsx\n    73\t<Card className=\"bg-blue-100 text-blue-900 font-bold\">\n    74\t  <CardContent>Dashboard</CardContent>\n    75\t</Card>\n    76\t```\n    77\t\n    78\t**Correct:**\n    79\t\n    80\t```tsx\n    81\t<Card className=\"max-w-md mx-auto\">\n    82\t  <CardContent>Dashboard</CardContent>\n    83\t</Card>\n    84\t```\n    85\t\n    86\t### Use cn() for Conditional Classes\n    87\t\n    88\t**Incorrect:**\n    89\t\n    90\t```tsx\n    91\t<div className={`flex items-center ${isActive ? \"bg-primary text-primary-foreground\" : \"bg-muted\"}`}>\n    92\t```\n    93\t\n    94\t**Correct:**\n    95\t\n    96\t```tsx\n    97\timport { cn } from \"@/lib/utils\"\n    98\t\n    99\t<div className={cn(\"flex items-center\", isActive ? \"bg-primary text-primary-foreground\" : \"bg-muted\")}>\n   100\t```\n   101\t\n   102\t### Forms & Inputs\n   103\t\n   104\t- **Forms use `FieldGroup` + `Field`.** Never use raw `div` with `space-y-*` or `grid gap-*` for form layout.\n   105\t- **`InputGroup` uses `InputGroupInput`/`InputGroupTextarea`.** Never raw `Input`/`Textarea` inside `InputGroup`.\n   106\t- **Buttons inside inputs use `InputGroup` + `InputGroupAddon`.**\n   107\t- **Option sets (2–7 choices) use `ToggleGroup`.** Don't loop `Button` with manual active state.\n   108\t- **`FieldSet` + `FieldLegend` for grouping related checkboxes/radios.** Don't use a `div` with a heading.\n   109\t- **Field validation uses `data-invalid` + `aria-invalid`.** `data-invalid` on `Field`, `aria-invalid` on the control. For disabled: `data-disabled` on `Field`, `disabled` on the control.\n   110\t\n   111\t```tsx\n   112\t<FieldGroup>\n   113\t  <Field>\n   114\t    <FieldLabel htmlFor=\"email\">Email</FieldLabel>\n   115\t    <Input id=\"email\" />\n   116\t  </Field>\n   117\t</FieldGroup>\n   118\t\n   119\t// Validation: data-invalid on Field, aria-invalid on the control.\n   120\t<Field data-invalid>\n   121\t  <FieldLabel>Email</FieldLabel>\n   122\t  <Input aria-invalid />\n   123\t  <FieldDescription>Invalid email.</FieldDescription>\n   124\t</Field>\n   125\t```\n   126\t\n   127\t### Component Structure\n   128\t\n   129\t- **Items always inside their Group.** `SelectItem` → `SelectGroup`. `DropdownMenuItem` → `DropdownMenuGroup`. `CommandItem` → `CommandGroup`.\n   130\t- **Use `asChild` (radix) or `render` (base) for custom triggers.** Check `base` field from `npx shadcn@latest info`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
